featured focused roundtable discussions on “Reimagining HR Systems for High-Impact CPSE Performance” and “Translating Vision into Action: CPSE HR Strategy” where participants emphasised the need for institutionalised collaboration, shared knowledge platforms, and integrated capacity-building efforts to enhance efficiency, innovation, and public value creation beyond financial returns.</p><p>The program concluded with closing reflections by Shri S. P. Roy, Secretary, CBC who said that CBC is always committed to support capacity building initiatives of CPSEs. The vote of thanks was delivered by Ms Navneet Kaur, Director, CBC.</p><p>The CBC will also bring the Training Institutes, PSUs and States on a common platform for collaboration aligned with Karmayogi capacity building efforts across governance space.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 391, 541, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) organises National Consultative Workshop on Karmayogi Quality Framework</p><p>Aims to Strengthen Quality of Digital Learning for Civil Servants</p><p>Strong quality framework critical for building future-ready civil servants for Viksit Bharat: Ms S. Radha Chauhan<br><br>https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2206695&amp;reg=3&amp;lang=1</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 391, 1280, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) organises National Consultative Workshop on Karmyogi Quality Framework</p><p>Aims to Strengthen Quality of Digital Learning for Civil Servants</p><p>Strong quality framework critical for building future-ready civil servants for Viksit Bharat: Ms S. Radha Chauhan<br><br>https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2206695&amp;reg=3&amp;lang=1</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 392, 542, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr Alka Mittal, Member, Capacity Building Commission, addressed at the workshop on “Decoding Labour Codes – Understanding the New Era of Labour Reforms in India” at Mangaluru on December 20. The workshop was organised by Indian Institute of Skill Development and Research (IISDR), in collaboration with Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) Mangaluru, Mangalore Management Association (MMA), and Kanara Industries Association (KIA). The workshop brought together policymakers, industry leaders, labour administrators, HR professionals, academicians, and students to deliberate on India’s evolving labour regulatory framework.</p><p>Dr Mittal spoke on the importance of ethical leadership and strong governance in building people-centric organisations. She emphasised that effective governance frameworks guide employees through clear rules, fairness, and transparency, enabling organisations to function smoothly and sustainably.</p><p>Highlighting the role of labour laws, she noted that they support organizational stability by preventing exploitation, reducing disputes, and ensuring legal clarity through standardized labour practices. Stressing zero tolerance for discrimination in recruitment, wages, promotions, or training, she underlined the importance of protecting workers’ rights and promoting collective bargaining.</p><p>She highlighted the role of digital tools in enabling online registration, inspections, and compliance. She further stressed the importance of continuous reskilling and upskilling across technical and non-technical fields to prepare the workforce for technological change, advocating a holistic approach that balances worker welfare, employer flexibility, and digital transformation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 392, 543, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr Alka Mittal, Member, Capacity Building Commission, addressed at the workshop on “Decoding Labour Codes – Understanding the New Era of Labour Reforms in India” at Mangaluru on December 20. The workshop was organised by Indian Institute of Skill Development and Research (IISDR), in collaboration with Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) Mangaluru, Mangalore Management Association (MMA), and Kanara Industries Association (KIA). The workshop brought together policymakers, industry leaders, labour administrators, HR professionals, academicians, and students to deliberate on India’s evolving labour regulatory framework.</p><p>Dr Mittal spoke on the importance of ethical leadership and strong governance in building people-centric organisations. She emphasised that effective governance frameworks guide employees through clear rules, fairness, and transparency, enabling organisations to function smoothly and sustainably.</p><p>Highlighting the role of labour laws, she noted that they support organizational stability by preventing exploitation, reducing disputes, and ensuring legal clarity through standardized labour practices. Stressing zero tolerance for discrimination in recruitment, wages, promotions, or training, she underlined the importance of protecting workers’ rights and promoting collective bargaining.</p><p>She highlighted the role of digital tools in enabling online registration, inspections, and compliance. She further stressed the importance of continuous reskilling and upskilling across technical and non-technical fields to prepare the workforce for technological change, advocating a holistic approach that balances worker welfare, employer flexibility, and digital transformation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 393, 544, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), called on Shri Vishnu Deo Sai, Chief Minister, Chhattisgarh in Raipur today.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 393, 545, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), called on Shri Vishnu Deo Sai, Chief Minister, Chhattisgarh in Raipur today.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 393, 1247, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), called on Shri Vishnu Deo Sai, Chief Minister, Chhattisgarh in Raipur.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 394, 546, 'en', 0, '<p>As a part of the Good Governance Week, the Capacity Building Commission organized a thought-provoking talk by Dr. Onkar Sharma, Former Chief Labour Commissioner, Government of India on “Labour Codes towards Governance Reforms” reaffirming its commitment to strengthening Good Governance. Dr Alka Mittal, Member (Admin), CBC highlighted the importance of the topic of the Samuhik Charcha.</p><p>Shri S.P Roy, Secretary, CBC welcomed the speaker. Dr Sharma shared strategic perspectives on India’s labour reforms and the transition towards a more facilitative and responsive governance model. Drawing from his rich experience, he traced the origins of labour laws in the Indian traditional roots. He highlighted how the Labour Codes address contemporary labour challenges through simplification, transparency, and administrative coherence.</p><p>The discussion underscored the role of stakeholder consultations, institutional preparedness, and sustained capacity-building in effective implementation.</p><p>Such knowledge-sharing engagements remain central to CBC’s mandate of building future-ready institutions and enabling transformative governance reforms.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 395, 547, 'en', 0, '<p>A one-day workshop on the Development of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) was conducted jointly by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and the Chhattisgarh Academy of Administration (CAA) at IIIT, Naya Raipur.</p><p>The workshop was inaugurated by Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, CBC, along with Shri Vikas Sheel, Chief Secretary, Government of Chhattisgarh, in the presence of Additional Chief Secretary and other senior officers from various state departments.</p><p>Speaking on the occasion, Ms. S Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, CBC said that Training Institutes are critical to the success of Mission Karmayogi. She emphasised that Training Institutes need to stand out to meet the bigger challenges, adding that they need to reimagine, revamp and re-define their roles in the ever evolving training eco-system, where Artificial Intelligence is playing an important role.</p><p>Chairperson, CBC also added that in order to achieve the target of Viksit Bharat 2047, the public servants needs to be ‘Future Ready’ and for readying for the future we need to be ‘Present Ready’ and thus the iGOT Karmayogi plays an important part in making us ready for the future and thus in a way helps our country to achieve the growth and milestones.</p><p>The Chief Secretary of Chhattisgarh, Shri. Vikas Sheel highlighted how the State Government’s vision for \"Viksit Chhattisgarh @2047\" is reshaping the whole governance with the use of Information Technology. Shri. Vikas Sheel added that all the officers at the district level offices will start E-office from January, 2026 and also Aadhar based biometric attendance. He emphasized on Mid-Career level training and use of the AI-enabled Capacity Building Plan (CBP) tool to cater to the needs of the officers as per their duties and responsibilities.</p><p>Ms. Chandralekha Mukherjee, Principal Advisor, CBC, acknowledged the strong foundational work already undertaken by Chhattisgarh and highlighted the immense potential of the State to emerge as a leading example in the development and implementation of Capacity Building Plans, while guiding participants on strengthening CBPs through structured frameworks and strategic alignment.</p><p>The sessions also included inputs from Shri Abhishek Dubey, Nodal Officer, Mission Karmayogi, who outlined the implementation roadmap and priorities for Mission Karmayogi in Chhattisgarh.</p><p>The workshop witnessed active participation from 60+ officials across 8 departments, culminating in the development of department-wise Capacity Building Plans aligned with state and institutional priorities.</p><p>This workshop marks an important step towards building a future-ready civil services ecosystem and strengthening capacity building reforms in Chhattisgarh.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 396, 548, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission (CBC), delivered the keynote address at the Good Governance Day celebrations held in Jaipur</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 402, 554, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) has continued to play central role in strengthening India’s civil services architecture by driving the implementation of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>During the year 2025, the Commission focused on reaching out to the states with a more structured approach, aiming at creating capacities through Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) for State Departments by using AI-tool. In addition, the Commission updated its accreditation framework for Training Institutes incorporating new dimensions. The behavioural training in Seva Bhav through ‘Rashtriya Karmayogi Jan Sewa Programme’ was one of the important highlights of the year. In addition, the focus aimed at creating new courses in domain areas targeting domain competencies.</p><p>During 2025, the Commission took several key initiatives and achieved significant milestones.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2208111&amp;reg=3&amp;lang=2\">Read More&nbsp;</a></p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 402, 1373, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) has continued to play central role in strengthening India’s civil services architecture by driving the implementation of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>During the year 2025, the Commission focused on reaching out to the states with a more structured approach, aiming at creating capacities through Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) for State Departments by using AI-tool. In addition, the Commission updated its accreditation framework for Training Institutes incorporating new dimensions. The behavioural training in Seva Bhav through ‘Rashtriya Karmayogi Jan Sewa Program’ was one of the important highlights of the year. In addition, the focus aimed at creating new courses in domain areas targeting domain competencies.</p><p>During 2025, the Commission took several key initiatives and achieved significant milestones.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2208111&amp;reg=3&amp;lang=2\">Read More&nbsp;</a></p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 409, 561, 'en', 0, '<p>A State-level meeting chaired by Chief Minister of Uttar Pradesh, Yogi Adityanath, was held with the Chief Secretary, Shri Shashi Prakash Goyal and Secretaries of key citizen-facing departments.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 409, 563, 'en', 0, '<p>A State-level meeting chaired by Chief Minister of Uttar Pradesh, Yogi Adityanath, was held with the Chief Secretary, Shri Shashi Prakash Goyal and Secretaries of key citizen-facing departments.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 413, 566, 'en', 0, '<p>Chairperson CBC, Ms S Radha Chauhan, visited @upacademyup &amp; held detailed discussions with institute leadership on the pivotal role state training institutions can play in developing a robust State CBP &amp; strengthening overall capacity-building ecosystem under Mission Karmayogi.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 496, 657, 'en', 0, '<p>The Hon\'ble Minister of State for the Ministry of Science and Technology, Dr Jitendra Singh, inaugurated the phygital course on \'Building Science Leaders in India\' today.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">&nbsp;</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The course is implemented with support of Centre for Technology, Innovation and Economic Research (CTIER) and Ahmedabad University and marks a unique collaboration between Capacity Building Commission and ISRO - Indian Space Research Organization for executive development of scientists in Government of India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 496, 1067, 'en', 0, '<p>The Hon\'ble Minister of State for the Ministry of Science and Technology, Dr Jitendra Singh, inaugurated the phygital course on \'Building Science Leaders in India\' today.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">&nbsp;</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The course is implemented with support of Centre for Technology, Innovation and Economic Research (CTIER) and Ahmedabad University and marks a unique collaboration between Capacity Building Commission and ISRO - Indian Space Research Organization for executive development of scientists in Government of India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 511, 673, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission and Administrative Staff College of India (ASCI) signed an MoU to enhance cooperation and collaboration in strengthening the capacity building ecosystem.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">We look forward to a fruitful and exciting partnership with ASCI.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 523, 685, 'en', 0, '<p>“India is moving towards a “less government, more governance” approach. This requires a paradigmatic shift in the capacities, mindset, and actions of the civil servant.”</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Dr. R Balasubramaniam writes in The Indian Express where he talks about the evolution in governance and the role of Capacity Building Commission in building capacity and supporting the aspirations of a modern and future-ready civil service</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 523, 1281, 'en', 0, '<p>“India is moving towards a “less government, more governance” approach. This requires a paradigmatic shift in the capacities, mindset, and actions of the civil servant.”</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Dr. R Balasubramaniam writes in The Indian Express where he talks about the evolution in governance and the role of Capacity Building Commission in building capacity and supporting the aspirations of a modern and future-ready civil service</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 524, 686, 'en', 0, '<p>‘Science is the energy in development of India in 21st century, it has the power to accelerate the development of every region and state of the nation’ - PM Narendra Modi</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The Research and Information Systems for Developing Countries (RIS) and Office of the Principal Scientific Adviser to the Government of India hosted the Workshop on Science, Technology, and Innovation for Sustainable Development Goals.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Speaking at the inauguration program of the workshop, Shri Hemang Jani, Secretary, Capacity Building Commission added that ‘Technologies are the new humanities’, and India is and will continue to play a key role in supporting development of Science, Technology, and Innovations. He added that India is emerging as one of the most innovative countries in the world and serves as test bed for innovations applicable for global south. India is steadfast to develop its own capacity to ensure its STI outputs are taking ‘Local to Global’.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The program is part of the global pilot programme on STI for SDGs Roadmap hosted by United Nations (and endorsed by G20). The global STI for SDGs program is aimed towards enhancing global cooperation for global Technology Facilitation Mechanism (TFM). The program is being piloted in five countries, viz. Ethiopia, Ghana, Kenya, Serbia, and India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 529, 691, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission and School of Planning and Architecture, New Delhi signed an MoU for collaboration on various capacity building initiatives in spatial planning, design, architecture, and management for the various departments of Government of India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 534, 696, 'en', 0, '<p>\"We are committed to protecting IPR which is essential to fostering creativity\"</p><p lang=\"en-US\">- Hon\'ble PM Narendra Modi</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Hemang Jani, Secretary, Capacity Building Commission participated in the National IP Conference 2022, chaired by Hon\'ble CIM Shri Piyush Goyal. The conference was jointly organized by Capacity Building Commission and Office of The Controller General of Patents, Designs And Trademarks.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The conference bought together policy makers, IP officers, creators, and practitioners on one platform to discuss futuristic IP challenges related to developmental issues.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Speaking during the conference, Hon\'ble CIM Piyush Goyal said innovation is that one defining characteristic that has always pushed mankind forward and the key factor that would determine the fate of the country.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">He urged patent office to setup interactions of patent offices with applicants and stakeholders through video conferencing to take inputs from IP practitioners and public.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Speaking at the conference, Secretary, CBC stressed on the need to streamline the IPR granting mechanism through capacity building of key functionaries, which would be a key to meet the needs of growing intellectual capital in the nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 538, 700, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission in collaboration with the Ministry of Textiles and Office of Textiles Commissioner organized a workshop to \"Strengthen collaboration between the industry and Ministry of Textiles\".</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The workshop saw representatives from various textiles industry associations and companies across the country. The workshop was aimed towards understanding priority capacity needs of the Ministry from their direct and indirect stakeholders.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Post feedback from industry associations, the Annual Capacity Building Plan was presented to and launched by Shri U. P. Singh, Secretary, Ministry of Textiles.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 544, 706, 'en', 0, '<p>“Technology for us is a medium to empower the people of the country. For us, technology is the mainstay of making the country self-reliant”</p><p lang=\"en-US\">-PM Narendra Modi</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The Phygital course on ‘Emerging Technologies’ by Capacity Building Commission was launched today by Hon’ble MoS, Rajeev Chandrasekhar in presence of Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman CBC and Hemang Jani, Secretary CBC. The course is developed by CBC in partnership with Indian Institute of Public Administration (IIPA) and Wadhwani Institute of Technology and Policy.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The course is designed as an introduction on key emerging technologies for civil servants, wherein the online part of the course is already available on iGOT and is now being followed by 2 days offline program at IIPA.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">While addressing the gathering, Hon’ble MoS said that countries around the world are in awe of India’s prowess in technology. Post the pandemic, digitization is the way of 21st century for world governments and markets, and India has emerged as a leader in this trend. A big credit for which goes to PM’s push for digital India since 2014.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">&nbsp;</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman CBC, added that the goal of the program is to use technology to leapfrog development. Hemang Jani, Secretary CBC, further added that technology is the solution for efficient governance, and the phygital course on emerging technology will enable civil servants to build skill set required for this transformation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 549, 711, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission organized an experience sharing session for effective implementation of FRAC in Government of India in collaboration with iGOT Karmayogi team, Indian Oil Corporation Limited, and Department of Telecommunications (DOT).</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The discussion was focused on the future of competency mapping and e-learning for civil servants.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 555, 717, 'en', 0, '<p>\"I believe India\'s new National Education Policy is one of the major factors in the mahayagna of nation building. Therefore, the country has made this education policy modern and future ready\"</p><p lang=\"en-US\">-PM Narendra Modi</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Hemang Jani, Secretary Capacity Building Commission addressed the gathering Inaugural session of the ongoing 12th Education Summit by Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) on \"Improving Industry-Academia engagements in India\". The session was chaired by Dr Rajkumar Ranjan Singh, Minister of State, Ministry of Education &amp; Ministry of External Affairs, India.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">The summit brings together subject matters, experts, and policy to highlight the key points in the education sector and discuss the way forward,</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Addressing the gathering during the inaugural address, Secretary CBC spoke about the salient approach of National Education Policy (NEP) to enable practical learning and innovation in education. He highlighted on key areas where Academia-Industry can collaborate to improve curricula, pedagogy, and support translation of research of research into innovations.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 558, 722, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission held an interaction with The World Bank\'s India team, led by Country Director Auguste Tano Kouame.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Capacity building initiatives within ministries and departments, National Standards of Civil Service Training Institutions, Innovations in public administration and the Annual Report of the commission was discussed.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 559, 723, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission held a workshop with all external partners working with ministries, departments, and organizations within the Government of India on Annual Capacity Building Plans.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">An Annual Capacity Building Plan (ACBP) of an MDO identifies capacity needs through three lenses of National Priorities, Emerging Technologies, and Citizen Centricity. Further, it details all training and non-training interventions required to develop the competencies of individuals and the organization as a whole.</p><p lang=\"en-US\">All our partners joined us at Vigyan Bhavan:</p><p lang=\"en-US\">Deloitte, Grant Thornton Bharat LLP, KPMG India, PwC India, EY, Sattva Consulting, National Institute for Smart Government, Asian Development Bank (ADB), Centre for Effective Governance of Indian States (CEGIS), Invest India, Primus Partners India, Foundation for Advancing Science and Technology - India and Centre for Good Governance (cgg.gov.in)</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 585, 749, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission organised a three-day workshop to train Central Training Institutes (CTI) and State Training Institutes (ATI) faculty members on developing case studies. The workshop was facilitated by Harvard Business School India Research Center. The workshop was based on a combination of participant-centred learning as well as learning-by-doing approaches and involved case development through interviews with protagonists, who were Public Administrative Officials and had done exemplary work for the nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 600, 764, 'en', 0, '<p>In the roundtable, the various experts in the field of Bharatiya Civilisation gave their inputs on the first draft of the karmayogi competency model and made the discussion enriching and enlightening for the CBC team to guide the way forward.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 619, 783, 'en', 0, '<p>Faculty Development Programme in collaboration with the Indian School of Business was conducted at the Yashwantrao Chavan Academy of Development Administration (YASHADA), Pune. The 3-day-long event encompassed multiple sessions on the teaching methods of trainers, the importance of experiential learning and the usage of technology in teaching methods.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 619, 1376, 'en', 0, '<p>Faculty Development Program in collaboration with the Indian School of Business was conducted at the Yashwantrao Chavan Academy of Development Administration (YASHADA), Pune. The 3-day-long event encompassed multiple sessions on the teaching methods of trainers, the importance of experiential learning and the usage of technology in teaching methods.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 620, 784, 'en', 0, '<p>The officers trained for the Common Mid Career Training Programme CMCTP came together to share and gather knowledge and inspire others in the regional event for the \"Community of Leaders\" from North India. Dr Madan Pillutla Dean and Professor at the Indian School of Business coached the participants on skills of Negotiation and Professor Aroon P Manoharan conducted a session on Strategic Communication, where the participants had simulating discussions about the art of policy communications.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 620, 1378, 'en', 0, '<p>The officers trained for the Common Mid Career Training Program CMCTP came together to share and gather knowledge and inspire others in the regional event for the \"Community of Leaders\" from North India. Dr Madan Pillutla Dean and Professor at the Indian School of Business coached the participants on skills of Negotiation and Professor Aroon P Manoharan conducted a session on Strategic Communication, where the participants had simulating discussions about the art of policy communications.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('photo_gallery', 0, 622, 797, 'en', 0, '<p>01 January 2026</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 623, 789, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission&nbsp; hosted a&nbsp; workshop for the Civil Services training institutes at Sri Krishna Institute of Public Administration (SKIPA), Ranchi.</p><p>The workshop was targeted for training institutes in the East zone of India, intended to guide the institutes through the process of National Standards for Civil Services Training Institutes (NSCSTI).</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('photo_gallery', 0, 624, 798, 'en', 0, '<p>07 January 2026</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('photo_gallery', 0, 625, 799, 'en', 0, '<p>07 January 2026</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('photo_gallery', 0, 626, 800, 'en', 0, '<p>08 January 2026</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 627, 802, 'en', 0, '<p>The officers trained under the Common Mid Career Training Programme CMCTP came together to share &amp; gain knowledge in the regional event for the “Community of Practice” (COP) conducted for the southern region.</p><p>Several officers from across the cadres and services came together to be a part of the programme and strengthen their leadership skills via experiential session.</p><p>Dr R Balasubramaniam, Member HR delivered the inaugural address and lauded the efforts of the officers in keeping this learning and knowledge sharing journey active.</p><p>Shri Amit Garg, Director of Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel National Police Academy, also spoke to the participants and shared his experiences with them.</p><p>Raghu Ananthanarayanan, delivered an enriching session on “Leadership Journey through inner presence” which was appreciated by the participants of the programme.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 637, 812, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission and Department of Finance (DFS), Ministry of Finance, collaborated to host a one-day Fintech workshop held on October 04, 2023 at Vanijya Bhawan, New Delhi.&nbsp;</p><p>The workshop addressed digital technology\'s role in improving financial access and inclusion to address national priorities for involving ministries such as Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises, Ministry of Commerce and Industry, Government of India &nbsp;Ministry of External Affairs, India, Ministry Of Corporate Affairs, Prime Ministers Office, NITI Aayog, Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade, Ministry of Agriculture &amp; Farmers Welfare, Government of India and more. Chaired by DFS secretary, it brought together administrative, regulatory, and industry stakeholders. The morning sessions covered the fintech sector\'s sectoral scenario in India, in a global evolutionary context. Industry experts and thought leaders led discussions on Digital Public Infrastructure, Regulatory Issues, and India\'s fintech future. Afternoon sessions showcased impactful fintech stories, demos, and group activities.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 638, 813, 'en', 0, '<p>As part of ACBP for the Department of Defence Production, Capacity Building Commission facilitated an a 2-day immersion program for officials from Defence PSUs such as Hindustan Aeronautics Limited (HAL), Bharat Earth Movers Limited - India (BEML), and Bharat Dynamics Limited (BDL) at Walchandnagar Industries Limited (WIL). The immersion program was held on the topic \"Quality Control and Quality Assurance processes in Aerospace and Missile Manufacturing\".&nbsp;</p><p>During the program, WIL made an elaborate presentation on how it imparts Quality Assurance, Quality Control, and Quality Ethics in its processes. This was followed by a shop floor round where the visiting team had a hands-on experience with facilities and infrastructure, and also an understanding of mass and size, intricacies of product and manufacturing process, qualification and trials.&nbsp;</p><p>The feedback from the visiting officials was unanimously positive as they intend to use the learnings gained at WIL in their own organizations.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 639, 815, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC) facilitated an Industry Immersion program at Siemens on the topic \'Industry 4.0 with a defence lens\" for officials of Defence PSUs including shipyards such as Mazagon Docks Limited (MDL), Goa Shipyard Limited (GSL) and Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL), Bharat Dynamics Limited (BDL), Hindustan Aeronautics Limited (HAL), Advanced Weapons and Equipment India Limited (AWEIL).&nbsp;</p><p>Siemens demonstrated cutting-edge digital transformation interventions it has implemented in its brownfield factory to turn it around from a bleeding plant to a benchmark in \"Factory of the Future\". DPSU officials experienced the Global Data Monitoring &amp; Remote Analysis Center (GAVATAR) which tracks energy and carbon data coming from all site locations through KPIs. Participants also learned about leveraging Digital Twin technologies in processes, shop floor management, and Industrial Additive manufacturing technologies along with Robot integration</p><p>We thank Siemens for organizing the visit and showcasing their state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 640, 816, 'en', 0, '<p>As part of State Level Capacity Building Initiatives, CBC was invited by Sardar Patel Institute of Public Administration (SPIPA), Gujarat to participate in a \'One day workshop of Departments and Training Institutes of Gujarat.\'&nbsp;</p><p>CBC team provided an overview of the learnings &amp; insights from Annual Capacity Building Planning Process. The workshop also intended to guide the institutes through the process of National Standards for Civil Services Training Institutes (NSCSTI). (www.nscsti.org)</p><p>Over 50 participants from various departments &amp; Training institutions like Gujarat Police Academy, Public Policy and Finance Institute of Gujarat, Gujarat, Jal Sewa Training Institute etc engaged in this Knowledge sharing workshop.&nbsp;</p><p>The Commission remains steadfast in its commitment to empowering the Karmayogi\'s and Enhancing State Capacity.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 641, 817, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship, India &amp; Microsoft India have teamed up again and entered into an MOU to develop and deploy digital learning resources for civil servants. &nbsp;This strategic partnership is a step towards empowering our civil servants with the knowledge and skills needed for navigating the dynamic landscape of emerging technologies.&nbsp;</p><p>The Microsoft modules onboarded on Karmayogi Bharat (IGOT) platform help enhance the knowledge on topics such as Cyber Security, Project Management, AI fluency skilling, Power BI as well as Functional Computer Literacy skills like MS word, Excell, PowerPoint etc. The first year of this collaboration resulted in over 3.1 Lakh course enrollments and 2.14 lakh course completions by civil servants across India.&nbsp;</p><p>Together, we are poised to create a future where technological advancements are seamlessly integrated into the governance framework by our Future Ready Civil Servants.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 642, 818, 'en', 0, '<p>Officers from the Ministry of Steel, Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change, and NITI Aayog on an immersion visit to Bhilai Steel Plant, SAIL</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 643, 820, 'en', 0, '<p>CBC, in collaboration with the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI), organized a workshop focused on Enhancing Survey Quality by Dr. Brady West.</p><p>The sessions were well-received and attended by officers of the Indian Statistical Services, including the Chief Statistician of India and by field officers from several regional offices of MoSPI.</p><p>We extend our gratitude to Dr. Brady West from the University of Michigan.</p><p>Special thanks to Prof. Sonalde Desai and Dr. Sharan Sharma for moderating the discussions and for their invaluable support in conceptualizing the workshop.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 644, 823, 'en', 0, '<p>The Department of Commerce is pivotal in driving India\'s economic growth. As we aim to achieve USD 1 trillion in exports and move towards a USD 10 trillion economy by 2047, capacity building becomes essential.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 645, 824, 'en', 0, '<p>Secretary, Capacity Building Commission(CBC) gave a talk on Mission Karmayogi to the 1st Executive Batch on 16th February, 2024 at New Delhi .</p><p>Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration (SLIDA), shared some of their learnings and appreciated the path taken under Mission Karmayogi.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 646, 826, 'en', 0, '<p>CBC, in collaboration with L&amp;T Defence IU organized a day-long immersion visit for Defence PSUs such as Hindustan Aeronautics Limited, Bharat Dynamics Limited, and Bharat Electronics Limited at Larsen &amp; Toubro\'s Hazira complex in Surat on the topic \" Supply Chain and Procurement Process Management\".</p><p>The visiting DPSU team deliberated, learned, and exchanged best practices on vendor development, material management, and mitigating supply chain risks. They also visited L&amp;T\'s state-of-the-art heavy manufacturing shops and armored systems complex.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 647, 827, 'en', 0, '<p>Minister of State for Communications launched 25 new courses after the completion of the 2nd phase of the Dak Karmayogi Project and released a Special Cover commemorating the successful journey of the Dak Karmayogi Project.</p><p>The interactive session provided trainees and trainers with an opportunity to share their experiences and insights, emphasizing the practical benefits of the capacity-building programs.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 647, 1284, 'en', 0, '<p>Minister of State for Communications launched 25 new courses after the completion of the 2nd phase of the Dak Karmyogi Project and released a Special Cover commemorating the successful journey of the Dak Karmyogi Project.</p><p>The interactive session provided trainees and trainers with an opportunity to share their experiences and insights, emphasizing the practical benefits of the capacity-building programs.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 682, 870, 'en', 0, '<p>Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, Dr. R Balasubramaniam visited All India Institute of Speech and Hearing (AIISH), Mysore and address the staff there on 4th December, 2025. He stressed on imbibing the spirit of continuous learning, bringing about the behavioural change, becoming future-ready and to encourage &amp; derive benefit by cross-pollination of ideas and collaboration.</p><p>His address also covered concepts of Vikas, Garv, Kartavya and Ekta, principles of Swadhyaya, Sahkaryata, RajyaKarma and Swadharma besides adoption of Indian Knowledge Systems and Quotes from Indic literature.</p><p>A brief presentation about the Institute was made by the Director, AIISH, covering governance aspects and the Institute’s work across four verticals-manpower development, clinical services, research, and public education in the area of communication (speech and hearing). This was followed by visits to the Departments of Special Education, Clinical services, Centre for Public Education in Communication Disorders (CPEC-D) and department of Prevention of Communication Disorders.</p><p>The Visit concluded with the Member (HR), CBC addressing the Officers of the Institute, followed by an interactive session. During the visit, the AIISHians of the Year 2025 were presented awards by Member (HR), CBC.</p><p>AIISH has achieved 98.4% staff coverage under the Rashtriya Karmayogi Jan Sewa (RKJS) program by CBC, and has developed 18 domain-specific courses for the KB in the domain of health.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 683, 871, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat , and the Government of Mizoram signed a Memorandum of Understanding in Aizawl to strengthen capacity building initiatives in the state.</p><p>Mr. Khilli Ram Meena, Chief Secretary, Mizoram, acknowledged the need for systematic capacity building to meet the requirements of an evolving workforce. He welcomed the support of CBC and Karmayogi Bharat in enabling the state to ensure that officials are equipped with the right competencies and skills for effective governance. He emphasised on lifelong learning of officers in Mizoram.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, emphasized the vital role of Administrative Training Institutes in shaping a future-ready civil service. He highlighted the importance of competency-based capacity building, integration of e-HRMS with the iGOT platform, and preparing officers today to deliver on the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047.</p><p>Shri. S P Roy, Secretary, CBC highlighted the role of Capacity Building Units in enabling the Capacity Building in the state. He explained the structural framework of overall coordination between the state and Capacity Building Commission. He also highlighted the importance of capacity building plan and the workshop to be planned for its development.</p><p>This partnership marks a significant step in advancing #MissionKarmayogi and building an agile, skilled, and citizen-centric workforce.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 683, 1285, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmyogi Bharat , and the Government of Mizoram signed a Memorandum of Understanding in Aizawl to strengthen capacity building initiatives in the state.</p><p>Mr. Khilli Ram Meena, Chief Secretary, Mizoram, acknowledged the need for systematic capacity building to meet the requirements of an evolving workforce. He welcomed the support of CBC and Karmyogi Bharat in enabling the state to ensure that officials are equipped with the right competencies and skills for effective governance. He emphasised on lifelong learning of officers in Mizoram.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, emphasized the vital role of Administrative Training Institutes in shaping a future-ready civil service. He highlighted the importance of competency-based capacity building, integration of e-HRMS with the iGOT platform, and preparing officers today to deliver on the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047.</p><p>Shri. S P Roy, Secretary, CBC highlighted the role of Capacity Building Units in enabling the Capacity Building in the state. He explained the structural framework of overall coordination between the state and Capacity Building Commission. He also highlighted the importance of capacity building plan and the workshop to be planned for its development.</p><p>This partnership marks a significant step in advancing #MissionKarmyogi and building an agile, skilled, and citizen-centric workforce.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 686, 874, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R. Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, along with Shri S. P. Roy, Secretary, CBC, &amp; Ms. Soumi Banerjee, General Manager, Karmayogi Bharat visited the Administrative Training Institute (ATI), Mizoram. visited the campus and its facilities.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 686, 875, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R. Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, along with Shri S. P. Roy, Secretary, CBC, &amp; Ms. Soumi Banerjee, General Manager, Karmayogi Bharat visited the Administrative Training Institute (ATI), Mizoram. visited the campus and its facilities.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 687, 876, 'en', 0, '<p>Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, Dr R Balasubramaniam addressed a session on “Leadership &amp; Management” at IIFM, Bhopal on 01.12.2025. The session was a part of the Management Module of the Mid-Career Training Phase-V for the in-service IFS Officers (1995 – 1999 batches).</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 688, 877, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission extends its heartfelt congratulations to the Lal Bahadur Shastri National Academy of Administration (LBSNAA) for achieving 5-star rating under the NSCSTI 2.0 Framework of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>This milestone reflects LBSNAA’s commitment to strengthening public sector capacity and setting high standards in training, innovation, and governance excellence.</p><p>CBC remains steadfast in supporting and collaborating with institutions that are driving transformation across India’s civil services.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 689, 878, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) conducted a focused workshop on “Delivering Quality at Scale,” facilitated by Dr. R. Balasubramaniam, to strengthen quality standards in digital learning products and programmes across the public sector. The workshop saw the participation of Ms. S. Radha Chauhan (Chairperson, CBC), Dr. Alka Mittal (Member Administration, CBC), Shri S. P. Roy (Secretary, CBC), along with the Mission Karmayogi team.</p><p>The workshop encouraged participants to reflect deeply on what quality truly signifies in a learning environment—and how it shapes the overall user experience. Through practical illustrations, interactive exercises, and group discussions, the sessions helped participants examine how users perceive quality and how consistency can be intentionally designed across the learning lifecycle.</p><p>Aligned with the vision of Mission Karmayogi, CBC continues to foster an ecosystem where digital learning is not only accessible but also effective, reliable, future-ready, and designed to strengthen the competencies of India’s civil servants.</p>', '', 'basic_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_event_description` (`bundle`, `deleted`, `entity_id`, `revision_id`, `langcode`, `delta`, `field_event_description_value`, `field_event_description_summary`, `field_event_description_format`) VALUES
('event', 0, 690, 879, 'en', 0, '<p>Congratulations to the Institute of Secretariat Training &amp; Management (ISTM) on being re-accredited with a 5-Star rating following the successful Post-QIP implementation facilitated by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC).</p><p>The Capacity Building Commission is proud to support institutions in consistently raising the bar for excellence in civil service capacity building.</p><p>#CapacityBuilding #MissionKarmayogi #ISTM #Governance #PublicService #GoodGovernance #ViksitBharat2047 #InstitutionalExcellence</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 690, 880, 'en', 0, '<p>Congratulations to the Institute of Secretariat Training &amp; Management (ISTM) on being re-accredited with a 5-Star rating following the successful Post-QIP implementation facilitated by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC).</p><p>The Capacity Building Commission is proud to support institutions in consistently raising the bar for excellence in civil service capacity building.</p><p>#CapacityBuilding #MissionKarmayogi #ISTM #Governance #PublicService #GoodGovernance #ViksitBharat2047 #InstitutionalExcellence</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 691, 882, 'en', 0, '<p>Today, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) observed the 76th Constitution Day (Samvidhan Diwas), reflecting on the values and vision that continue to guide India’s governance framework.</p><p>To mark the occasion, CBC organised a series of engaging and reflective activities for its officials and staff:</p><p>✅ Reading of the Preamble: Reaffirming our collective commitment to the Constitution’s foundational principles.</p><p>✅ Samuhik Charcha: Facilitating thoughtful dialogue on constitutional duties and their significance in public service.</p><p>✅ Digital Live Quiz: An interactive, real-time quiz designed to strengthen understanding of key constitutional concepts.</p><p>✅ Blog Writing Competition: Encouraging participants to articulate their perspectives on constitutional values, good governance, and public service ethics—fostering deeper reflection through creative expression.</p><p>These engagements provided a meaningful opportunity to revisit the core values that underpin effective governance and to reflect on how they translate into our day-to-day responsibilities as public servants.</p><p>As we work toward building a future-ready civil service under Mission Karmayogi, Constitution Day serves as a timely reminder to uphold a governance ecosystem grounded in integrity, accountability, and public service excellence.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 692, 884, 'en', 0, '<p>CBC in its commitment to strengthen the capacity building ecosystem by enhancing the capacity of Civil Service Training Institutions of the centre &amp; the states, launched its first Advanced Faculty Development Program at&nbsp;<br>@ISBedu with 34 carefully selected participants.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 693, 885, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), visited the Yashwantrao Chavan Academy of Development Administration (YASHADA), Pune &nbsp;Maharashtra, to discuss the implementation of Mission Karmayogi initiatives undertaken by the academy.<br>During the visit, she met Shri N. K. Sudhanshu, Director General, YASHADA, along with senior officials and faculty members. The meeting focused on the ongoing efforts to establish State and Departmental Capacity Building Units (CBUs), as well as the development of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs).<br>She emphasised the importance of sustained inter-departmental collaboration and the creation of State-specific training content in partnership with various training institutions.&nbsp;<br>The Chairperson reaffirmed CBC’s commitment to supporting YASHADA in further strengthening the implementation of Mission Karmayogi across Maharashtra.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 693, 886, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), visited the Yashwantrao Chavan Academy of Development Administration (YASHADA), Pune &nbsp;Maharashtra, to discuss the implementation of Mission Karmayogi initiatives undertaken by the academy.<br>During the visit, she met Shri N. K. Sudhanshu, Director General, YASHADA, along with senior officials and faculty members. The meeting focused on the ongoing efforts to establish State and Departmental Capacity Building Units (CBUs), as well as the development of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs).<br>She emphasised the importance of sustained inter-departmental collaboration and the creation of State-specific training content in partnership with various training institutions.&nbsp;<br>The Chairperson reaffirmed CBC’s commitment to supporting YASHADA in further strengthening the implementation of Mission Karmayogi across Maharashtra.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 694, 887, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), interacted with the Karmayogi Sarthis, outlining the key priorities and expectations for the forthcoming state-level capacity-building engagements under Mission Karmayogi</p><p>Mission Karmayogi is equipping State Departments to systematically develop structured CBPs aligned with assessed competency gaps, desired service delivery outcomes, and organisational priorities.</p><p>This initiative marks a significant step towards establishing a more efficient, robust, and future-ready civil service across&nbsp;the&nbsp;nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 694, 1287, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), interacted with the Karmyogi Sarthis, outlining the key priorities and expectations for the forthcoming state-level capacity-building engagements under Mission Karmyogi</p><p>Mission Karmyogi is equipping State Departments to systematically develop structured CBPs aligned with assessed competency gaps, desired service delivery outcomes, and organisational priorities.</p><p>This initiative marks a significant step towards establishing a more efficient, robust, and future-ready civil service across&nbsp;the&nbsp;nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 695, 888, 'en', 0, '<p>As a part of our collaborative effort towards development, a 3-day State Capacity Building workshop on creating State Capacity Building Plan was conducted at the RCVP Noronha Administrative Academy, Bhopal from 19–21 November, 2025, with participation from 30 departments and their sub-organisations.</p><p>The workshop opened with an address by Shri Sachin Sinha, IAS, Director General, who outlined the objectives and expected institutional outcomes of the workshop, followed by a detailed presentation by Shri Mujeebur Rehman Khan, IAS, Director-ATI, setting the operational and strategic context for departmental engagement.</p><p>Mission Karmayogi team facilitated the departments towards adopting state-wide standardisation of CBPs, ensuring data-driven capacity building and seamless integration with the iGOT Karmayogi platform.</p><p>The workshop marks a significant milestone in enabling the shift from creating rule-based to role-based Capacity Building Plans.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 695, 1288, 'en', 0, '<p>As a part of our collaborative effort towards development, a 3-day State Capacity Building workshop on creating State Capacity Building Plan was conducted at the RCVP Noronha Administrative Academy, Bhopal from 19–21 November, 2025, with participation from 30 departments and their sub-organisations.</p><p>The workshop opened with an address by Shri Sachin Sinha, IAS, Director General, who outlined the objectives and expected institutional outcomes of the workshop, followed by a detailed presentation by Shri Mujeebur Rehman Khan, IAS, Director-ATI, setting the operational and strategic context for departmental engagement.</p><p>Mission Karmyogi team facilitated the departments towards adopting state-wide standardisation of CBPs, ensuring data-driven capacity building and seamless integration with the iGOT Karmyogi platform.</p><p>The workshop marks a significant milestone in enabling the shift from creating rule-based to role-based Capacity Building Plans.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 697, 890, 'en', 0, '<p>“THE VOCABULARY OF GOVERNANCE IS EVOLVING FROM AUTHORITY TO EMPATHY, FROM SECRECY TO OPENNESS, FROM ‘DOING FOR’ TO ‘DOING WITH’.”</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 698, 892, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission, addressed the Senior Civil Servants of the Republic of Mauritius during the 2nd Capacity Building Programme for Senior Civil Servants from Mauritius at the National Centre for Good Governance (NCGG), New Delhi.</p><p>She shared insights on Mission Karmayogi and the iGOT Karmayogi platform, highlighting its transformative role in fostering continuous learning and capacity building among civil servants.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 698, 1380, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission, addressed the Senior Civil Servants of the Republic of Mauritius during the 2nd Capacity Building Program for Senior Civil Servants from Mauritius at the National Centre for Good Governance (NCGG), New Delhi.</p><p>She shared insights on Mission Karmayogi and the iGOT Karmayogi platform, highlighting its transformative role in fostering continuous learning and capacity building among civil servants.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 699, 893, 'en', 0, '<p>Today, the newly joined CBC officials and employees participated in the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Programme training — marking a major milestone: 7 lakh government officials trained with Seva Bhav from across India in Phase II.</p><p><br>Chairperson Ms. S. Radha Chauhan joined the team to mark this occasion. She talked about the values that shaped this journey — citizen-first governance and the belief that real change shows up in how we serve the citizens every day.</p><p>Dr. R. Balasubramaniam, Member (HR) reminded participants that the Karmayogi spirit must continue — the Seva Bhav nurtured through this programme should stay alive in their daily work.</p><p>We believe that the milestones mark progress, but it’s the intent we carry forward that transforms systems.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 699, 1289, 'en', 0, '<p>Today, the newly joined CBC officials and employees participated in the Rashtriya Karmyogi Large Scale Jan Seva Programme training — marking a major milestone: 7 lakh government officials trained with Seva Bhav from across India in Phase II.</p><p><br>Chairperson Ms. S. Radha Chauhan joined the team to mark this occasion. She talked about the values that shaped this journey — citizen-first governance and the belief that real change shows up in how we serve the citizens every day.</p><p>Dr. R. Balasubramaniam, Member (HR) reminded participants that the Karmyogi spirit must continue — the Seva Bhav nurtured through this programme should stay alive in their daily work.</p><p>We believe that the milestones mark progress, but it’s the intent we carry forward that transforms systems.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 700, 899, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission, graced the Graduation Ceremony of the Advanced Management Programs (AMPs), Class of 2025, at the Indian School of Business (ISB), Mohali.</p><p>In her address, she highlighted that the world of management is evolving at an unprecedented pace — urging the graduating cohort to anticipate change, harness innovation, and build organisations and institutions that are resilient, ethical, and future-ready.</p><p>She encouraged them to situate their professional journeys within the larger national vision of Viksit Bharat@2047 — a vision of a developed, prosperous, inclusive, and globally influential India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 700, 902, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission, graced the Graduation Ceremony of the Advanced Management Programs (AMPs), Class of 2025, at the Indian School of Business (ISB), Mohali.</p><p>In her address, she highlighted that the world of management is evolving at an unprecedented pace — urging the graduating cohort to anticipate change, harness innovation, and build organisations and institutions that are resilient, ethical, and future-ready.</p><p>She encouraged them to situate their professional journeys within the larger national vision of Viksit Bharat@2047 — a vision of a developed, prosperous, inclusive, and globally influential India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 700, 903, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission, graced the Graduation Ceremony of the Advanced Management Programs (AMPs), Class of 2025, at the Indian School of Business (ISB), Mohali.</p><p>In her address, she highlighted that the world of management is evolving at an unprecedented pace — urging the graduating cohort to anticipate change, harness innovation, and build organisations and institutions that are resilient, ethical, and future-ready.</p><p>She encouraged them to situate their professional journeys within the larger national vision of Viksit Bharat@2047 — a vision of a developed, prosperous, inclusive, and globally influential India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 700, 904, 'en', 0, '<p>Ms. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission, graced the Graduation Ceremony of the Advanced Management Programs (AMPs), Class of 2025, at the Indian School of Business (ISB), Mohali.</p><p>In her address, she highlighted that the world of management is evolving at an unprecedented pace — urging the graduating cohort to anticipate change, harness innovation, and build organisations and institutions that are resilient, ethical, and future-ready.</p><p>She encouraged them to situate their professional journeys within the larger national vision of Viksit Bharat@2047 — a vision of a developed, prosperous, inclusive, and globally influential India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 701, 905, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission organised the mass singing of ‘Vande Mataram’ today, joining the nationwide commemoration marking 150 years of India’s National Song.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 701, 1243, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission organised the mass singing of ‘Vande Mataram’ today, joining the nationwide commemoration marking 150 years of India’s National Song.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 701, 1246, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission organised the mass singing of ‘Vande Mataram, joining the nationwide commemoration marking 150 years of India’s National Song.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 702, 906, 'en', 0, '<p>As part of the Vigilance Awareness Week 2025, being observed from 27th October to 2nd November, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) organized a #SamuhikCharcha on the theme “Vigilance: Our Shared Responsibility.”</p><p>The discussion centered on the significance of collective responsibility in promoting integrity, transparency, and ethical governance. Participants reflected on the role of #vigilance as a continuous process that strengthens institutional credibility and fosters public trust.</p><p>The session reaffirmed CBC’s commitment to upholding the highest standards of accountability and public service in all its endeavors.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 703, 907, 'en', 0, '<p>On the occasion of #RashtriyaEktaDiwas 2025, officers and staff of the Capacity Building Commission, took the Integrity Pledge, reaffirming their commitment to uphold unity, integrity and security of the nation.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 704, 908, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with Lal Bahadur Shastri National Academy of Administration (LBSNAA) and Karmayogi Bharat, organized a workshop to strengthen the Mission Karmayogi team, preparing them to effectively facilitate the capacity building initiatives being implemented across States and Union Territories.</p><p>The workshop was graced by Shri Sriram Taranikanti, Director, LBSNAA; Smt Chandralekha Mukherjee, Former Director General, Haryana Institute of Public Administration (HIPA); Shri S P Roy, Secretary, CBC; Ms Shanmuga Priya Mishra, Deputy Director, LBSNAA and others.</p><p>Their participation and insights underscored the importance of collaboration and innovation in advancing the objectives of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>This initiative marks another step towards realizing the shared vision of a #ViksitBharat, enabled by future-ready, and citizen-centric civil service.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 704, 909, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with Lal Bahadur Shastri National Academy of Administration (LBSNAA) and Karmayogi Bharat, organized a workshop to strengthen the Mission Karmayogi team, preparing them to effectively facilitate the capacity building initiatives being implemented across States and Union Territories.</p><p>The workshop was graced by Shri Sriram Taranikanti, Director, LBSNAA; Smt Chandralekha Mukherjee, Former Director General, Haryana Institute of Public Administration (HIPA); Shri S P Roy, Secretary, CBC; Ms Shanmuga Priya Mishra, Deputy Director, LBSNAA and others.</p><p>Their participation and insights underscored the importance of collaboration and innovation in advancing the objectives of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>This initiative marks another step towards realizing the shared vision of a #ViksitBharat, enabled by future-ready, and citizen-centric civil service.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 704, 1290, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with Lal Bahadur Shastri National Academy of Administration (LBSNAA) and Karmyogi Bharat, organized a workshop to strengthen the Mission Karmyogi team, preparing them to effectively facilitate the capacity building initiatives being implemented across States and Union Territories.</p><p>The workshop was graced by Shri Sriram Taranikanti, Director, LBSNAA; Smt Chandralekha Mukherjee, Former Director General, Haryana Institute of Public Administration (HIPA); Shri S P Roy, Secretary, CBC; Ms Shanmuga Priya Mishra, Deputy Director, LBSNAA and others.</p><p>Their participation and insights underscored the importance of collaboration and innovation in advancing the objectives of Mission Karmyogi.</p><p>This initiative marks another step towards realizing the shared vision of a #ViksitBharat, enabled by future-ready, and citizen-centric civil service.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 705, 910, 'en', 0, '<p>It is our privilege to announce the signing of a tripartite MoU between the Capacity Building Commission, the School of Ultimate Leadership, and the Government of Gujarat to roll out the 𝐃𝐢𝐬𝐭𝐫𝐢𝐜𝐭 𝐊𝐚𝐫𝐦𝐚𝐲𝐨𝐠𝐢 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐠𝐫𝐚𝐦, an initiative to strengthen citizen-centric governance.</p><p>SOUL shall serve as the lead knowledge and leadership program implementation partner.</p><p>The MoU was signed by 𝐒 𝐏 𝐑𝐨𝐲, Secretary, CBC, 𝐒𝐚𝐮𝐫𝐚𝐛𝐡 𝐉𝐨𝐡𝐫𝐢, CEO, SOUL, and 𝐇𝐚𝐫𝐞𝐞𝐭 𝐒𝐡𝐮𝐤𝐥𝐚, IAS, Principal Secretary, ARTD, GoG, in the presence of 𝐃𝐫. 𝐇𝐚𝐬𝐦𝐮𝐤𝐡 𝐀𝐝𝐡𝐢𝐚, Principal Advisor to the H’ble Chief Minister of Gujarat, 𝐌𝐬. 𝐒 𝐑𝐚𝐝𝐡𝐚 𝐂𝐡𝐚𝐮𝐡𝐚𝐧, Chairperson, CBC and 𝐑. 𝐁𝐚𝐥𝐚𝐬𝐮𝐛𝐫𝐚𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐢𝐚𝐦, Member – HR, CBC.</p><p>SOUL shall design and implement behavioural transformation, functional excellence, and technological enablement programs for Grade 1 and Grade 2 officers, starting with the Narmada district as a pilot to create a scalable and replicable model for the state and the nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 705, 911, 'en', 0, '<p>It is our privilege to announce the signing of a tripartite MoU between the Capacity Building Commission, the School of Ultimate Leadership, and the Government of Gujarat to roll out the 𝐃𝐢𝐬𝐭𝐫𝐢𝐜𝐭 𝐊𝐚𝐫𝐦𝐚𝐲𝐨𝐠𝐢 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐠𝐫𝐚𝐦, an initiative to strengthen citizen-centric governance.</p><p>SOUL shall serve as the lead knowledge and leadership program implementation partner.</p><p>The MoU was signed by 𝐒 𝐏 𝐑𝐨𝐲, Secretary, CBC, 𝐒𝐚𝐮𝐫𝐚𝐛𝐡 𝐉𝐨𝐡𝐫𝐢, CEO, SOUL, and 𝐇𝐚𝐫𝐞𝐞𝐭 𝐒𝐡𝐮𝐤𝐥𝐚, IAS, Principal Secretary, ARTD, GoG, in the presence of 𝐃𝐫. 𝐇𝐚𝐬𝐦𝐮𝐤𝐡 𝐀𝐝𝐡𝐢𝐚, Principal Advisor to the H’ble Chief Minister of Gujarat, 𝐌𝐬. 𝐒 𝐑𝐚𝐝𝐡𝐚 𝐂𝐡𝐚𝐮𝐡𝐚𝐧, Chairperson, CBC and 𝐑. 𝐁𝐚𝐥𝐚𝐬𝐮𝐛𝐫𝐚𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐢𝐚𝐦, Member – HR, CBC.</p><p>SOUL shall design and implement behavioural transformation, functional excellence, and technological enablement programs for Grade 1 and Grade 2 officers, starting with the Narmada district as a pilot to create a scalable and replicable model for the state and the nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 706, 912, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member HR, Capacity Building Commission, and the team visited AIIMS, Delhi.</p><p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) is conducting an extensive research study across Public Sector Hospitals to comprehend citizen-centric practices in healthcare delivery and propose templates for scaling those practices in other healthcare institutions.</p><p>Therefore, this visit aimed to gain firsthand insights into how processes, governance, and patient experience are interconnected.</p><p>The Director, Shri Srinivas, presented details about the initiatives in AIIMS, Delhi, that have improved patient experiences. The Heads of Departments, faculty members, discussed their experiences and how they contribute to these initiatives.</p><p>Dr. Balasubramaniam interacted with healthcare service providers, front desk officers, and some patients about these services.</p><p>This exercise is part of a larger effort to identify and document citizen-centric best practices. It also seeks to facilitate the exchange of ideas across public sector hospitals and develop models that can guide hospitals across India and globally.</p><p>The exceptional zeal and leadership capabilities of specific department staff, such as the NICU department, were insightful.</p><p>The cross-pollination of such practices will significantly enhance the citizen-centricity of healthcare services.</p><p>The insights gained from this visit will contribute to the development of healthcare systems that are accessible, transparent, and compassionate, with citizens firmly at the centre.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 706, 914, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member HR, Capacity Building Commission, and the team visited AIIMS, Delhi.</p><p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) is conducting an extensive research study across Public Sector Hospitals to comprehend citizen-centric practices in healthcare delivery and propose templates for scaling those practices in other healthcare institutions.</p><p>Therefore, this visit aimed to gain firsthand insights into how processes, governance, and patient experience are interconnected.</p><p>The Director, Shri Srinivas, presented details about the initiatives in AIIMS, Delhi, that have improved patient experiences. The Heads of Departments, faculty members, discussed their experiences and how they contribute to these initiatives.</p><p>Dr. Balasubramaniam interacted with healthcare service providers, front desk officers, and some patients about these services.</p><p>This exercise is part of a larger effort to identify and document citizen-centric best practices. It also seeks to facilitate the exchange of ideas across public sector hospitals and develop models that can guide hospitals across India and globally.</p><p>The exceptional zeal and leadership capabilities of specific department staff, such as the NICU department, were insightful.</p><p>The cross-pollination of such practices will significantly enhance the citizen-centricity of healthcare services.</p><p>The insights gained from this visit will contribute to the development of healthcare systems that are accessible, transparent, and compassionate, with citizens firmly at the centre.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 707, 916, 'en', 0, '<p>ATIs to function as Catalysts in State-Level Capacity Building.&nbsp;</p><p>The 2-day workshop on \'Developing State-Level Capacity Building Plans\' brought ATIs as key stakeholders of capacity building in states. Through hands-on group exercises, ATI teams designed draft CBPs for key sectors. To begin with, six such key sectors were chosen: Education, Women &amp; Child Development, Agriculture, Rural Development, Health and Urban Development. These culminated in presentations that showcased their approach, key learnings, and next steps.</p><p>In the closing session, Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson CBC, called ATIs a “pivotal pillar” in creating CBPs. She underlined that ATIs must act as mentors and catalysts, helping state governments own their CBPs and embed a whole-of-government approach. Importantly, she emphasized the shift from rule-based structures to role-based learning, focusing not just on designations, but on the competencies required for roles that officials actually perform.</p><p>Shri Sriram Taranikanti, Director, LBSNAA, reflected on the workshop presentations, stressing the importance of carrying forward the exercises into concrete state-level CBPs and highlighting the broader role ATIs must play in shaping this reform journey.</p><p>Smt. Chhavi Bhardwaj, CEO (Karmayogi Bharat) &amp; Joint Secretary (DoPT), underlined key priorities, from integrating training calendars to creating domain courses in regional languages, to make the ecosystem more relevant and impactful.</p><p>Member (Administration), CBC, Dr. Alka Mittal, officers and team members from Capacity Building Commission, Karmayogi Bharat and LBSNAA were also present during the conclusion of the workshop. The workshop brought together heads and senior faculty members from 17 State ATIs. Participants were introduced to the core principles of Mission Karmayogi, the Karmayogi Competency Model, and tools and templates for designing Capacity Building Plans (CBPs).</p><p>This workshop marked a significant step in deepening capacity building initiatives at the State level. With ATIs positioned as knowledge hubs and mentors, they will anchor CBPs across departments, ensuring that capacity building directly empowers every official to serve citizens better.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 707, 918, 'en', 0, '<p>ATIs to function as Catalysts in State-Level Capacity Building.&nbsp;</p><p>The 2-day workshop on \'Developing State-Level Capacity Building Plans\' brought ATIs as key stakeholders of capacity building in states. Through hands-on group exercises, ATI teams designed draft CBPs for key sectors. To begin with, six such key sectors were chosen: Education, Women &amp; Child Development, Agriculture, Rural Development, Health and Urban Development. These culminated in presentations that showcased their approach, key learnings, and next steps.</p><p>In the closing session, Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson CBC, called ATIs a “pivotal pillar” in creating CBPs. She underlined that ATIs must act as mentors and catalysts, helping state governments own their CBPs and embed a whole-of-government approach. Importantly, she emphasized the shift from rule-based structures to role-based learning, focusing not just on designations, but on the competencies required for roles that officials actually perform.</p><p>Shri Sriram Taranikanti, Director, LBSNAA, reflected on the workshop presentations, stressing the importance of carrying forward the exercises into concrete state-level CBPs and highlighting the broader role ATIs must play in shaping this reform journey.</p><p>Smt. Chhavi Bhardwaj, CEO (Karmayogi Bharat) &amp; Joint Secretary (DoPT), underlined key priorities, from integrating training calendars to creating domain courses in regional languages, to make the ecosystem more relevant and impactful.</p><p>Member (Administration), CBC, Dr. Alka Mittal, officers and team members from Capacity Building Commission, Karmayogi Bharat and LBSNAA were also present during the conclusion of the workshop. The workshop brought together heads and senior faculty members from 17 State ATIs. Participants were introduced to the core principles of Mission Karmayogi, the Karmayogi Competency Model, and tools and templates for designing Capacity Building Plans (CBPs).</p><p>This workshop marked a significant step in deepening capacity building initiatives at the State level. With ATIs positioned as knowledge hubs and mentors, they will anchor CBPs across departments, ensuring that capacity building directly empowers every official to serve citizens better.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 708, 917, 'en', 0, '<p>ATIs to function as Catalysts in State-Level Capacity Building.&nbsp;</p><p>The 2-day workshop on \'Developing State-Level Capacity Building Plans\' brought ATIs as key stakeholders of capacity building in states. Through hands-on group exercises, ATI teams designed draft CBPs for key sectors. To begin with, six such key sectors were chosen: Education, Women &amp; Child Development, Agriculture, Rural Development, Health and Urban Development. These culminated in presentations that showcased their approach, key learnings, and next steps.</p><p>In the closing session, Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson CBC, called ATIs a “pivotal pillar” in creating CBPs. She underlined that ATIs must act as mentors and catalysts, helping state governments own their CBPs and embed a whole-of-government approach. Importantly, she emphasized the shift from rule-based structures to role-based learning, focusing not just on designations, but on the competencies required for roles that officials actually perform.</p><p>Shri Sriram Taranikanti, Director, LBSNAA, reflected on the workshop presentations, stressing the importance of carrying forward the exercises into concrete state-level CBPs and highlighting the broader role ATIs must play in shaping this reform journey.</p><p>Smt. Chhavi Bhardwaj, CEO (Karmayogi Bharat) &amp; Joint Secretary (DoPT), underlined key priorities, from integrating training calendars to creating domain courses in regional languages, to make the ecosystem more relevant and impactful.</p><p>Member (Administration), CBC, Dr. Alka Mittal, officers and team members from Capacity Building Commission, Karmayogi Bharat and LBSNAA were also present during the conclusion of the workshop. The workshop brought together heads and senior faculty members from 17 State ATIs. Participants were introduced to the core principles of Mission Karmayogi, the Karmayogi Competency Model, and tools and templates for designing Capacity Building Plans (CBPs).</p><p>This workshop marked a significant step in deepening capacity building initiatives at the State level. With ATIs positioned as knowledge hubs and mentors, they will anchor CBPs across departments, ensuring that capacity building directly empowers every official to serve citizens better.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 708, 919, 'en', 0, '<p>The Workshop on \'Developing State-Level Capacity Building Plans\' was inaugurated by Hon’ble MoS (PP) Dr Jitendra Singh at CSOI, Vinay Marg today, who called for a future-ready, citizen-centric civil service built on continuous learning.</p><p>Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson CBC, reflected on the journey of Mission Karmayogi-moving from rule-based to role-based competencies-and stressed that ATIs must become the fulcrum for driving State Capacity Building Plans.</p><p>Smt. Rachna Shah, Secretary, DoPT, highlighted that ATIs must become the nerve centres of reform by guiding states to embed capacity building into their departmental workflows.</p><p>Shri Sriram Taranikanti, Director, LBSNAA, highlighted the pivotal role of ATIs and assured sustained mentorship from LBSNAA to institutionalise Mission Karmayogi across states.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, stressed that citizen-centricity and continuous learning must remain the guiding values of every CBP.</p><p>Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Admin), CBC, spoke about strengthening institutional ecosystems to enable ATIs to lead this reform at the grassroots.</p><p>Shri S P Roy, Secretary, CBC, emphasised the commitment and teamwork required to make capacity building a lived practice in governance.</p><p>Smt. Chhavi Bhardwaj, CEO (Karmayogi Bharat) &amp; Joint Secretary (DoPT), along with COO (Karmayogi Bharat) Shri Rakesh Verma, oriented ATIs on designing effective Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) with the use of technology to anchor this transformation.</p><p>As the momentum amongst ATIs grows, the day ahead will focus on group activities and hands-on exercises, with the two-day workshop charting the way forward to build State-level Capacity Building Plans (CBPs).</p><p><a href=\"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2170806\">Press Release Link</a></p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 709, 920, 'en', 0, '<p>In a significant step for strengthening public service in Manipur, a tripartite Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed today (23 September 2025) between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat, and the Government of Manipur.</p><p>Signed in the presence of Dr Puneet Kumar Goel, Chief Secretary, Government of Manipur, and Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, the partnership will deepen the state’s engagement with hashtag#MissionKarmayogi.</p><p>The MoU marks the beginning of an institutional partnership to implement Mission Karmayogi’s vision of a competency-based, technology-driven, and continuous learning ecosystem for government officials in Manipur-enabling civil servants to serve citizens better, faster, and with empathy.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 709, 921, 'en', 0, '<p>In a significant step for strengthening public service in Manipur, a tripartite Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed today (23 September 2025) between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat, and the Government of Manipur.</p><p>Signed in the presence of Dr Puneet Kumar Goel, Chief Secretary, Government of Manipur, and Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, the partnership will deepen the state’s engagement with hashtag#MissionKarmayogi.</p><p>The MoU marks the beginning of an institutional partnership to implement Mission Karmayogi’s vision of a competency-based, technology-driven, and continuous learning ecosystem for government officials in Manipur-enabling civil servants to serve citizens better, faster, and with empathy.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 709, 1292, 'en', 0, '<p>In a significant step for strengthening public service in Manipur, a tripartite Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed today (23 September 2025) between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmyogi Bharat, and the Government of Manipur.</p><p>Signed in the presence of Dr Puneet Kumar Goel, Chief Secretary, Government of Manipur, and Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, the partnership will deepen the state’s engagement with hashtag#MissionKarmyogi.</p><p>The MoU marks the beginning of an institutional partnership to implement Mission Karmyogi’s vision of a competency-based, technology-driven, and continuous learning ecosystem for government officials in Manipur-enabling civil servants to serve citizens better, faster, and with empathy.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 710, 922, 'en', 0, '<p>To mark the launch of Swachhta Hi Seva (SHS) 2025, Swachhta Pledge was administered by Ms S Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission and Shri S.P Roy, Joint Secretary, to all officers and staff of Capacity Building Commission.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 710, 923, 'en', 0, '<p>To mark the launch of Swachhta Hi Seva (SHS) 2025, Swachhta Pledge was administered by Ms S Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission and Shri S.P Roy, Joint Secretary, to all officers and staff of Capacity Building Commission.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 711, 924, 'en', 0, '<p>Team CBC bid farewell to Ms. V. Lalithalakshmi, Secretary, Capacity Building Commission and CEO, Karmayogi Bharat. We wish her the very best in all her future endeavors.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 711, 1293, 'en', 0, '<p>Team CBC bid farewell to Ms. V. Lalithalakshmi, Secretary, Capacity Building Commission and CEO, Karmyogi Bharat. We wish her the very best in all her future endeavors.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 712, 925, 'en', 0, '<p>Learning in action at the Second Edition of the Advanced Case Writing Workshop!</p><p>Today, Rajarshi Dey’s case study on \'Ordnance Factory Balangir\' was used for a live teaching demonstration. Rajarshi, an officer from National Academy of Defence Production, Nagpur (NADP), and participant of last year’s workshop, developed this case to highlight how procurement practices can be strengthened.</p><p>With participants stepping into role plays guided by the teaching note, the session came alive-showing how case teaching can turn policy dilemmas into real-time learning experiences.</p><p>📚 This case, along with its teaching note (faculty access only), is now part of the Amrit Gyaan Kosh on hashtag#iGOT.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 713, 926, 'en', 0, '<p>Advanced Case Writing Workshop at IRIFM, Secunderabad&nbsp;<br>Indian Railways Institute of Financial Management (IRIFM) is proud to host the Second Edition of the Advanced Case Writing Workshop in collaboration with the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), supported by the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and Asian Development Bank Institute (ADBI) and featuring Program Instructors like Blair Cameron (The World Bank) and Prof. Sanjay Dhir (Indian Institute of Technology, Delhi) in person and KE Seetha Ram, Dr. Eng. (Asian Development Bank Institute) virtually.&nbsp;<br><br>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, in his opening address emphasized that policies are not born in textbooks; they emerge from the experiences and partnership between government and citizens. He further highlighted the Hon’ble Prime Minister’s vision to adopt the case studies in Indian context for training purposes.&nbsp;<br><br>In her address, Aparna Garg, Director General, IRIFM, shared her perspective on the transformative role of case studies in officer training, as the learning outcome is proven to be most optimal. Equipped with right learning, the gap between government and governance gets minimized.&nbsp;<br><br>IRIFM is committed to contributing to this ecosystem of knowledge and to be a partner with CBC in this transformative mission.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 713, 927, 'en', 0, '<p>Advanced Case Writing Workshop at IRIFM, Secunderabad&nbsp;<br>Indian Railways Institute of Financial Management (IRIFM) is proud to host the Second Edition of the Advanced Case Writing Workshop in collaboration with the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), supported by the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and Asian Development Bank Institute (ADBI) and featuring Program Instructors like Blair Cameron (The World Bank) and Prof. Sanjay Dhir (Indian Institute of Technology, Delhi) in person and KE Seetha Ram, Dr. Eng. (Asian Development Bank Institute) virtually.&nbsp;<br><br>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, in his opening address emphasized that policies are not born in textbooks; they emerge from the experiences and partnership between government and citizens. He further highlighted the Hon’ble Prime Minister’s vision to adopt the case studies in Indian context for training purposes.&nbsp;<br><br>In her address, Aparna Garg, Director General, IRIFM, shared her perspective on the transformative role of case studies in officer training, as the learning outcome is proven to be most optimal. Equipped with right learning, the gap between government and governance gets minimized.&nbsp;<br><br>IRIFM is committed to contributing to this ecosystem of knowledge and to be a partner with CBC in this transformative mission.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 714, 928, 'en', 0, '<p>The Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva program has commenced at one of India’s premier healthcare institutions, #AIIMS, New Delhi, which serves over 10,000 patients every day. Addressing the second batch of Master Trainers, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, applauded their commitment and highlighted the program’s vision of nurturing Seva Bhav (spirit of service) and Svadharma (sense of duty) among civil servants. Officials were encouraged to step away from their desks and recognize that every action—big or small—shapes the lives of citizens. This marks a fundamental shift from being process-driven to becoming purpose-driven and moving from Rule based to Role based governance.</p><p>A true #Karmayogi moment was witnessed when, six inspiring posters on “Who is a Karmayogi” and “Karmayogi Moments” were prepared by organisation and inaugurated by Member (HR) with Director, AIIMS New Delhi. This symbolic gesture underscored the spirit of agility, dedication, and collective ownership.</p><p>The session marked a shared Sankalp to strengthen India’s #healthcare system, with AIIMS New Delhi emerging as a model institution that will inspire and set benchmarks for others across the nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 714, 929, 'en', 0, '<p>The Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva program has commenced at one of India’s premier healthcare institutions, #AIIMS, New Delhi, which serves over 10,000 patients every day. Addressing the second batch of Master Trainers, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, applauded their commitment and highlighted the program’s vision of nurturing Seva Bhav (spirit of service) and Svadharma (sense of duty) among civil servants. Officials were encouraged to step away from their desks and recognize that every action—big or small—shapes the lives of citizens. This marks a fundamental shift from being process-driven to becoming purpose-driven and moving from Rule based to Role based governance.</p><p>A true #Karmayogi moment was witnessed when, six inspiring posters on “Who is a Karmayogi” and “Karmayogi Moments” were prepared by organisation and inaugurated by Member (HR) with Director, AIIMS New Delhi. This symbolic gesture underscored the spirit of agility, dedication, and collective ownership.</p><p>The session marked a shared Sankalp to strengthen India’s #healthcare system, with AIIMS New Delhi emerging as a model institution that will inspire and set benchmarks for others across the nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 714, 1294, 'en', 0, '<p>The Rashtriya Karmyogi Large Scale Jan Seva program has commenced at one of India’s premier healthcare institutions, #AIIMS, New Delhi, which serves over 10,000 patients every day. Addressing the second batch of Master Trainers, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, applauded their commitment and highlighted the program’s vision of nurturing Seva Bhav (spirit of service) and Svadharma (sense of duty) among civil servants. Officials were encouraged to step away from their desks and recognize that every action—big or small—shapes the lives of citizens. This marks a fundamental shift from being process-driven to becoming purpose-driven and moving from Rule based to Role based governance.</p><p>A true #Karmyogi moment was witnessed when, six inspiring posters on “Who is a Karmyogi” and “Karmyogi Moments” were prepared by organisation and inaugurated by Member (HR) with Director, AIIMS New Delhi. This symbolic gesture underscored the spirit of agility, dedication, and collective ownership.</p><p>The session marked a shared Sankalp to strengthen India’s #healthcare system, with AIIMS New Delhi emerging as a model institution that will inspire and set benchmarks for others across the nation.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 715, 930, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) is pleased to announce the renewal of its Statement of Intent with IDinsight. This partnership reflects our shared vision of strengthening data-driven governance and fostering a culture of continuous improvement across the civil services.</p><p>Through this renewed collaboration, #CBC and #IDinsight will continue to work together to enhance the impact of #capacitybuilding initiatives by leveraging rigorous research, evidence-based strategies, and actionable insights.</p><p>We look forward to deepening this partnership to drive more informed, effective, and citizen-centric policies for a #ViksitBharat.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 716, 933, 'en', 0, '<p>After the resounding success of its first edition, the Advanced Case Writing Workshop returns this September with a bold mission-to build a practice-driven knowledge ecosystem for the public sector.</p><p>The Second Edition will bring together 75 Government Officials across three cohorts (Delhi/Goa/Secunderabad) for an intensive 3-day workshop designed to enhance their Case Writing Skills.</p><p>Pillars of the Workshop:</p><p>Atmanirbharta in Learning – Building a self-reliant Indian case-writing ecosystem.<br>Practice-Driven Knowledge – Converting governance experiences into learning resources.<br>Skill Building in Case Crafting – Developing impactful cases and teaching notes anchored in public sector challenges.<br>Policy Reflection &amp; Teaching Excellence – Advancing case pedagogy and policy insights.<br>Global–Local Collaboration – Featuring Program Instructors like Blair Cameron (World Bank) and Prof. Sanjay Dhir (IIT Delhi).</p><p>Supported by the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and Asian Development Bank Institute (ADBI), this workshop is shaping an India-centric case writing ecosystem with global reach under Mission Karmayogi.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 717, 934, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission (CBC), visited the BEL Academy for Excellence, Bengaluru - a training institution that exemplifies sustainable design and capacity building.</p><p>The Academy is envisaged to serve not only BEL employees, but also its customers, vendors, and partners—especially MSMEs/SMEs. Its programmes are structured around three core areas: Quality, Technology, and Leadership, designed in collaboration with experts from premier institutes such as IITs, IIMs, IISc, IETE, ISI, ASQ, and others.</p><p>It was inspiring to discuss the Academy’s vision and its immediate priority of launching the Quality Improvement Programme (QIP). Together, we look forward to elevating training standards and fostering continuous excellence in public sector learning.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 717, 1382, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission (CBC), visited the BEL Academy for Excellence, Bengaluru - a training institution that exemplifies sustainable design and capacity building.</p><p>The Academy is envisaged to serve not only BEL employees, but also its customers, vendors, and partners—especially MSMEs/SMEs. Its programs are structured around three core areas: Quality, Technology, and Leadership, designed in collaboration with experts from premier institutes such as IITs, IIMs, IISc, IETE, ISI, ASQ, and others.</p><p>It was inspiring to discuss the Academy’s vision and its immediate priority of launching the Quality Improvement Program (QIP). Together, we look forward to elevating training standards and fostering continuous excellence in public sector learning.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 718, 935, 'en', 0, '<p>India’s single largest behavioural training program is entering its most powerful phase—scale with purpose.</p><p>Today marks the final Lead Trainer batch at CSOI, New Delhi under Phase II of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large-Scale Jan Seva Program (RKLSJSP)—a transformative initiative reimagining how civil servants are trained to serve with Seva Bhav.</p><p>Phase II trained 740 Lead Trainers, 7,500 Master Trainers, who have already trained 1,57,806 civil servants across Bharat on iGOT.</p><p>As this pyramid of learning cascades further, 7,00,000+ government officials will be empowered through 1-day training sessions—ensuring that every citizen experiences responsive, empathetic, and effective governance.</p><p>RKLSJSP is a quiet revolution to realise Viksit Bharat—one that touches lives, villages, and cities through every act of improved public service.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 718, 936, 'en', 0, '<p>India’s single largest behavioural training program is entering its most powerful phase—scale with purpose.</p><p>Today marks the final Lead Trainer batch at CSOI, New Delhi under Phase II of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large-Scale Jan Seva Program (RKLSJSP)—a transformative initiative reimagining how civil servants are trained to serve with Seva Bhav.</p><p>Phase II trained 740 Lead Trainers, 7,500 Master Trainers, who have already trained 1,57,806 civil servants across Bharat on iGOT.</p><p>As this pyramid of learning cascades further, 7,00,000+ government officials will be empowered through 1-day training sessions—ensuring that every citizen experiences responsive, empathetic, and effective governance.</p><p>RKLSJSP is a quiet revolution to realise Viksit Bharat—one that touches lives, villages, and cities through every act of improved public service.</p>', '', 'basic_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_event_description` (`bundle`, `deleted`, `entity_id`, `revision_id`, `langcode`, `delta`, `field_event_description_value`, `field_event_description_summary`, `field_event_description_format`) VALUES
('event', 0, 718, 1295, 'en', 0, '<p>India’s single largest behavioural training program is entering its most powerful phase—scale with purpose.</p><p>Today marks the final Lead Trainer batch at CSOI, New Delhi under Phase II of the Rashtriya Karmyogi Large-Scale Jan Seva Program (RKLSJSP)—a transformative initiative reimagining how civil servants are trained to serve with Seva Bhav.</p><p>Phase II trained 740 Lead Trainers, 7,500 Master Trainers, who have already trained 1,57,806 civil servants across Bharat on iGOT.</p><p>As this pyramid of learning cascades further, 7,00,000+ government officials will be empowered through 1-day training sessions—ensuring that every citizen experiences responsive, empathetic, and effective governance.</p><p>RKLSJSP is a quiet revolution to realise Viksit Bharat—one that touches lives, villages, and cities through every act of improved public service.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 719, 937, 'en', 0, '<p>The largest behavioural change program in India’s governance is shaping a new era of public service transformation.</p><p>A future-ready civil service begins with capacity building at scale. Under hashtag#MissionKarmayogi, the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program has now crossed its first major milestone – 1,00,000 central government officials across Bharat trained to deliver governance with hashtag#SevaBhav at the core.</p><p>But this is only the beginning. The journey ahead envisions training 7,00,000 officials across the nation, building a civil service that is citizen-focused, technology-enabled, and rooted in continuous learning – where capacity building becomes second nature and public service keeps evolving to meet the aspirations of a Viksit Bharat.</p><p>This achievement stands as a testament to the collective effort of ministries, states, training institutions, who have worked in unison, shaping a system where knowledge spreads its wings and governance rises to serve better, every single day.</p><p>CBC remains committed to accelerating this journey – creating a culture where learning never stops, and service to the people stays at the heart of governance.</p><p>For in the service of people, the truest growth lies, As knowledge spreads its wings, a brighter Bharat shall rise.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 719, 1296, 'en', 0, '<p>The largest behavioural change program in India’s governance is shaping a new era of public service transformation.</p><p>A future-ready civil service begins with capacity building at scale. Under hashtag#MissionKarmyogi, the Rashtriya Karmyogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program has now crossed its first major milestone – 1,00,000 central government officials across Bharat trained to deliver governance with hashtag#SevaBhav at the core.</p><p>But this is only the beginning. The journey ahead envisions training 7,00,000 officials across the nation, building a civil service that is citizen-focused, technology-enabled, and rooted in continuous learning – where capacity building becomes second nature and public service keeps evolving to meet the aspirations of a Viksit Bharat.</p><p>This achievement stands as a testament to the collective effort of ministries, states, training institutions, who have worked in unison, shaping a system where knowledge spreads its wings and governance rises to serve better, every single day.</p><p>CBC remains committed to accelerating this journey – creating a culture where learning never stops, and service to the people stays at the heart of governance.</p><p>For in the service of people, the truest growth lies, As knowledge spreads its wings, a brighter Bharat shall rise.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 720, 938, 'en', 0, '<p>Mrs. S. Radha Chauhan assumed charge as the Chairperson of Capacity Building Commission, in New Delhi today. She is a retired IAS officer of UP Cadre (1988 batch). She has served in various capacities in the State and Centre Government. She is also the former Secretary of Department of Personnel and Training (DoPT). She took charge from Shri Adil Zainulbhai, who served as Chairman of the Capacity Building Commission since April, 2021.</p><p>Constituted on 1st April 2021, by the Government of India, the Capacity Building Commission has been mandated to drive standardisation and harmonisation across the Indian civil services landscape. As the custodian of civil services capacity building reforms, the Commission’s role is central to the overall institutional framework of Mission Karmayogi.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 721, 939, 'en', 0, '<p>In a major stride towards strengthening the capacity-building framework for civil servants in Jammu &amp; Kashmir, the Government of Jammu &amp; Kashmir, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), and Karmayogi Bharat signed a tripartite Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on August 5, 2025, in Srinagar.</p><p>The MoU aims to institutionalize Mission Karmayogi across J&amp;K by facilitating structured, role-based, and continuous learning for government officials through the iGOT Karmayogi platform. The initiative will help build future-ready, and citizen-centric civil service ecosystem in the region.</p><p>Shri Atal Dulloo, Chief Secretary, Government of Jammu &amp; Kashmir, reiterated the government’s commitment to enhancing governance through capacity building. He emphasized the vital role of the General Administration Department (GAD) and the Institute of Management, Public Administration and Rural Development (IMPARD) in leading the implementation efforts and expediting the onboarding of officials across departments onto the iGOT Karmayogi platform.<br>The MoU signing was attended by senior dignitaries including Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), CBC; Shri M Raju, Secretary, General Administration Department, J&amp;K; Smt. Rehana Batul, Director General, IMPARD; Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi, CEO, Karmayogi Bharat; Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC; Shri Rakesh Verma, Chief Executive Officer, Karmayogi Bharat.</p><p>As part of the engagement, an orientation session was attended by Additional Secretaries and Deputy Secretaries of various departments at IMPARD. The session was conducted by Smt. Navneet Kaur, Director, CBC, and Shri Rakesh Verma, COO, Karmayogi Bharat, who outlined the core objectives of Mission Karmayogi, with a focus on digital learning, need-based skilling, and the transition to a competency-driven public administration system.</p><p>Shri Rakesh Verma, COO of Karmayogi Bharat, delivered a live demonstration of the iGOT Karmayogi platform, highlighting its modular and self-paced learning design. He noted that over 1.26 crore learners across India have already benefited from the platform’s flexible and contextual learning modules.<br>A key outcome of the event was the Government of J&amp;K’s affirmation to begin onboarding officials from different departments and launch their curated learning journeys on iGOT Karmayogi. The administration also expressed interest in implementing customized blended learning programs tailored to their unique developmental priorities.</p><p>This MoU marks the beginning of a collaborative institutional effort to build a dynamic, digitally empowered, and continuously evolving public workforce aligned with the vision of Mission Karmayogi.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 721, 940, 'en', 0, '<p>In a major stride towards strengthening the capacity-building framework for civil servants in Jammu &amp; Kashmir, the Government of Jammu &amp; Kashmir, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), and Karmayogi Bharat signed a tripartite Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on August 5, 2025, in Srinagar.</p><p>The MoU aims to institutionalize Mission Karmayogi across J&amp;K by facilitating structured, role-based, and continuous learning for government officials through the iGOT Karmayogi platform. The initiative will help build future-ready, and citizen-centric civil service ecosystem in the region.</p><p>Shri Atal Dulloo, Chief Secretary, Government of Jammu &amp; Kashmir, reiterated the government’s commitment to enhancing governance through capacity building. He emphasized the vital role of the General Administration Department (GAD) and the Institute of Management, Public Administration and Rural Development (IMPARD) in leading the implementation efforts and expediting the onboarding of officials across departments onto the iGOT Karmayogi platform.<br>The MoU signing was attended by senior dignitaries including Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), CBC; Shri M Raju, Secretary, General Administration Department, J&amp;K; Smt. Rehana Batul, Director General, IMPARD; Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi, CEO, Karmayogi Bharat; Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC; Shri Rakesh Verma, Chief Executive Officer, Karmayogi Bharat.</p><p>As part of the engagement, an orientation session was attended by Additional Secretaries and Deputy Secretaries of various departments at IMPARD. The session was conducted by Smt. Navneet Kaur, Director, CBC, and Shri Rakesh Verma, COO, Karmayogi Bharat, who outlined the core objectives of Mission Karmayogi, with a focus on digital learning, need-based skilling, and the transition to a competency-driven public administration system.</p><p>Shri Rakesh Verma, COO of Karmayogi Bharat, delivered a live demonstration of the iGOT Karmayogi platform, highlighting its modular and self-paced learning design. He noted that over 1.26 crore learners across India have already benefited from the platform’s flexible and contextual learning modules.<br>A key outcome of the event was the Government of J&amp;K’s affirmation to begin onboarding officials from different departments and launch their curated learning journeys on iGOT Karmayogi. The administration also expressed interest in implementing customized blended learning programs tailored to their unique developmental priorities.</p><p>This MoU marks the beginning of a collaborative institutional effort to build a dynamic, digitally empowered, and continuously evolving public workforce aligned with the vision of Mission Karmayogi.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 721, 1297, 'en', 0, '<p>In a major stride towards strengthening the capacity-building framework for civil servants in Jammu &amp; Kashmir, the Government of Jammu &amp; Kashmir, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), and Karmyogi Bharat signed a tripartite Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on August 5, 2025, in Srinagar.</p><p>The MoU aims to institutionalize Mission Karmyogi across J&amp;K by facilitating structured, role-based, and continuous learning for government officials through the iGOT Karmyogi platform. The initiative will help build future-ready, and citizen-centric civil service ecosystem in the region.</p><p>Shri Atal Dulloo, Chief Secretary, Government of Jammu &amp; Kashmir, reiterated the government’s commitment to enhancing governance through capacity building. He emphasized the vital role of the General Administration Department (GAD) and the Institute of Management, Public Administration and Rural Development (IMPARD) in leading the implementation efforts and expediting the onboarding of officials across departments onto the iGOT Karmyogi platform.<br>The MoU signing was attended by senior dignitaries including Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), CBC; Shri M Raju, Secretary, General Administration Department, J&amp;K; Smt. Rehana Batul, Director General, IMPARD; Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi, CEO, Karmyogi Bharat; Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC; Shri Rakesh Verma, Chief Executive Officer, Karmyogi Bharat.</p><p>As part of the engagement, an orientation session was attended by Additional Secretaries and Deputy Secretaries of various departments at IMPARD. The session was conducted by Smt. Navneet Kaur, Director, CBC, and Shri Rakesh Verma, COO, Karmyogi Bharat, who outlined the core objectives of Mission Karmyogi, with a focus on digital learning, need-based skilling, and the transition to a competency-driven public administration system.</p><p>Shri Rakesh Verma, COO of Karmyogi Bharat, delivered a live demonstration of the iGOT Karmyogi platform, highlighting its modular and self-paced learning design. He noted that over 1.26 crore learners across India have already benefited from the platform’s flexible and contextual learning modules.<br>A key outcome of the event was the Government of J&amp;K’s affirmation to begin onboarding officials from different departments and launch their curated learning journeys on iGOT Karmyogi. The administration also expressed interest in implementing customized blended learning programs tailored to their unique developmental priorities.</p><p>This MoU marks the beginning of a collaborative institutional effort to build a dynamic, digitally empowered, and continuously evolving public workforce aligned with the vision of Mission Karmyogi.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 722, 942, 'en', 0, '<p>Arunachal Pradesh takes a step towards citizen-first governance!</p><p>On 4th August 2025, the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program was officially launched in Itanagar by Hon’ble Chief Minister Shri Pema Khandu, marking a key milestone in the state’s journey towards strengthening public service delivery under the vision of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>The launch event was attended by several senior dignitaries, including Shri Manish Gupta, Chief Secretary, Government of Arunachal Pradesh; Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (Human Resources), Capacity Building Commission; Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission; and Shri Vivek HP, Secretary, Health &amp; Family Welfare, Government of Arunachal Pradesh, along with Secretaries and Heads of Departments from across the state administration.</p><p>Speaking at the event, Dr. R Balasubramaniam shared the program’s vision to build a more empathetic, citizen-centric civil service by training over 7,00,000 government officials across the country. He also highlighted the relevance of key Mission Karmayogi initiatives such as Gyaan Kosh and Indian Knowledge Systems for the governance ecosystem of Arunachal Pradesh.</p><p>In his keynote address, the Hon’ble Chief Minister reaffirmed the state’s commitment to capacity building and formally launched the Jan Seva Program, underscoring its importance in empowering civil servants to deliver better outcomes for citizens.</p><p>This marks a significant step forward in advancing a responsive, accountable, and people-first civil service.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 722, 1298, 'en', 0, '<p>Arunachal Pradesh takes a step towards citizen-first governance!</p><p>On 4th August 2025, the Rashtriya Karmyogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program was officially launched in Itanagar by Hon’ble Chief Minister Shri Pema Khandu, marking a key milestone in the state’s journey towards strengthening public service delivery under the vision of Mission Karmyogi.</p><p>The launch event was attended by several senior dignitaries, including Shri Manish Gupta, Chief Secretary, Government of Arunachal Pradesh; Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (Human Resources), Capacity Building Commission; Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission; and Shri Vivek HP, Secretary, Health &amp; Family Welfare, Government of Arunachal Pradesh, along with Secretaries and Heads of Departments from across the state administration.</p><p>Speaking at the event, Dr. R Balasubramaniam shared the program’s vision to build a more empathetic, citizen-centric civil service by training over 7,00,000 government officials across the country. He also highlighted the relevance of key Mission Karmyogi initiatives such as Gyaan Kosh and Indian Knowledge Systems for the governance ecosystem of Arunachal Pradesh.</p><p>In his keynote address, the Hon’ble Chief Minister reaffirmed the state’s commitment to capacity building and formally launched the Jan Seva Program, underscoring its importance in empowering civil servants to deliver better outcomes for citizens.</p><p>This marks a significant step forward in advancing a responsive, accountable, and people-first civil service.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 723, 943, 'en', 0, '<p>In a significant step towards transforming the capacity-building landscape of civil servants in #Chhattisgarh, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat, and the Government of Chhattisgarh signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on 28th July 2025 in Raipur. The signing ceremony took place in the august presence of the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Chhattisgarh, Shri Vishnu Deo Sai.</p><p>In his address, the Hon’ble Chief Minister affirmed that the initiative will be pivotal in nurturing a culture of excellence in governance and public administration across Chhattisgarh.</p><p>The event was attended by senior dignitaries including Shri Amitabh Jain, Chief Secretary, Government of Chhattisgarh; Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), Capacity Building Commission; Shri Subrat Sahoo, Director General, Chhattisgarh Academy of Administration; Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi Secretary, Capacity Building Commission and Chief Executive Officer, Karmayogi Bharat; and Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission.</p><p>As part of the engagement, an orientation session was conducted for Secretaries, Heads of Departments, and Departmental Nodal Officers. The session highlighted #MissionKarmayogi’s vision of creating a future-ready and citizen-centric civil service through digital learning, role-based training, and continuous professional development.</p><p>Shri Rakesh Verma, Chief Operating Officer of Karmayogi Bharat, provided a live demonstration of the #iGOT Karmayogi platform, showcasing its key features that enable modular, self-paced, and role-aligned learning. He also emphasized the platform’s growing impact, with over 1.26 crore learners across the country benefiting from flexible, need-based capacity-building opportunities.</p><p>A key outcome of the discussions was the Government of Chhattisgarh’s commitment to onboard officials from various departments onto the iGOT platform and initiate their structured learning journeys. The state also expressed interest in co-creating learning content tailored to its unique governance needs. &nbsp;</p><p>The MoU marks the beginning of an institutional partnership to implement Mission Karmayogi’s vision of a competency-based, technology-driven, and continuous learning ecosystem for government officials in Chhattisgarh.</p><p>The Capacity Building Commission extends its gratitude to the Government of Chhattisgarh for its steadfast commitment to advancing Mission Karmayogi in the state. This collaboration underscores our shared resolve to empower public servants and foster a more agile, accountable, and citizen-centric governance ecosystem.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 723, 1300, 'en', 0, '<p>In a significant step towards transforming the capacity-building landscape of civil servants in #Chhattisgarh, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmyogi Bharat, and the Government of Chhattisgarh signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on 28th July 2025 in Raipur. The signing ceremony took place in the august presence of the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Chhattisgarh, Shri Vishnu Deo Sai.</p><p>In his address, the Hon’ble Chief Minister affirmed that the initiative will be pivotal in nurturing a culture of excellence in governance and public administration across Chhattisgarh.</p><p>The event was attended by senior dignitaries including Shri Amitabh Jain, Chief Secretary, Government of Chhattisgarh; Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), Capacity Building Commission; Shri Subrat Sahoo, Director General, Chhattisgarh Academy of Administration; Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi Secretary, Capacity Building Commission and Chief Executive Officer, Karmyogi Bharat; and Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission.</p><p>As part of the engagement, an orientation session was conducted for Secretaries, Heads of Departments, and Departmental Nodal Officers. The session highlighted #MissionKarmyogi’s vision of creating a future-ready and citizen-centric civil service through digital learning, role-based training, and continuous professional development.</p><p>Shri Rakesh Verma, Chief Operating Officer of Karmyogi Bharat, provided a live demonstration of the #iGOT Karmyogi platform, showcasing its key features that enable modular, self-paced, and role-aligned learning. He also emphasized the platform’s growing impact, with over 1.26 crore learners across the country benefiting from flexible, need-based capacity-building opportunities.</p><p>A key outcome of the discussions was the Government of Chhattisgarh’s commitment to onboard officials from various departments onto the iGOT platform and initiate their structured learning journeys. The state also expressed interest in co-creating learning content tailored to its unique governance needs. &nbsp;</p><p>The MoU marks the beginning of an institutional partnership to implement Mission Karmyogi’s vision of a competency-based, technology-driven, and continuous learning ecosystem for government officials in Chhattisgarh.</p><p>The Capacity Building Commission extends its gratitude to the Government of Chhattisgarh for its steadfast commitment to advancing Mission Karmyogi in the state. This collaboration underscores our shared resolve to empower public servants and foster a more agile, accountable, and citizen-centric governance ecosystem.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 724, 944, 'en', 0, '<p>S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission conducted an enlightening session on Mission Karmayogi for all faculties of Mahatma Gandhi State Institute of Public Administration, (MGSIPA) on 25th July 25.</p><p>He talked about the process of creating Capacity Building Plans, Jan Seva Trainings, Amrit Gyaan Kosh, Faculty Development Program and the NSCSTI framework.</p><p>MGSIPA is making strides in progress of Mission Karmayogi and also working towards creating culture and courses fostering Indian Knowledge Systems.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 724, 945, 'en', 0, '<p>S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission conducted an enlightening session on Mission Karmayogi for all faculties of Mahatma Gandhi State Institute of Public Administration, (MGSIPA) on 25th July 25.</p><p>He talked about the process of creating Capacity Building Plans, Jan Seva Trainings, Amrit Gyaan Kosh, Faculty Development Program and the NSCSTI framework.</p><p>MGSIPA is making strides in progress of Mission Karmayogi and also working towards creating culture and courses fostering Indian Knowledge Systems.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 724, 1301, 'en', 0, '<p>S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission conducted an enlightening session on Mission Karmyogi for all faculties of Mahatma Gandhi State Institute of Public Administration, (MGSIPA) on 25th July 25.</p><p>He talked about the process of creating Capacity Building Plans, Jan Seva Trainings, Amrit Gyaan Kosh, Faculty Development Program and the NSCSTI framework.</p><p>MGSIPA is making strides in progress of Mission Karmyogi and also working towards creating culture and courses fostering Indian Knowledge Systems.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 725, 946, 'en', 0, '<p>On 25th July 2025, a landmark MoU was signed between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat, and the Union Territory of Chandigarh, in the presence of the Chief Secretary, UT Chandigarh. An MoU between MGSIPA and Chandigarh Administration was also formalized to further the goals of Mission Karmayogi in the region.</p><p>Ms. V. Lalithalakshmi, IAS, Secretary, CBC and CEO, Karmayogi Bharat, emphasized the importance of mandatory annual course completions on the iGOT Karmayogi platform and informed about its linkage with APARs, as directed by DoPT. She also highlighted the new scoring framework that assesses Ministries/Departments on their capacity building progress.</p><p>Sh. Shyama Prasad Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC, introduced the Rashtriya Karmayogi Jan Seva Program, a behavioural training initiative, and urged for early identification of Master Trainers in Chandigarh to enable its rollout before 15th August 2025.</p><p>Ms. Alka Mittal, Member (Admin), CBC, joined the event virtually and lauded Chandigarh Administration for onboarding over 25,000 officials, enrolling in 1,00,000+ courses, and completing 90,000+ learning modules on the iGOT Karmayogi platform.</p><p>Shri Rajeev Verma, Chief Secretary, Chandigarh, directed all departments to expedite onboarding and course completion and proposed a review meeting under his chairmanship to track progress.</p><p>This collaboration marks a significant step toward transforming governance through continuous learning and upskilling under Mission Karmayogi.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 725, 1302, 'en', 0, '<p>On 25th July 2025, a landmark MoU was signed between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmyogi Bharat, and the Union Territory of Chandigarh, in the presence of the Chief Secretary, UT Chandigarh. An MoU between MGSIPA and Chandigarh Administration was also formalized to further the goals of Mission Karmyogi in the region.</p><p>Ms. V. Lalithalakshmi, IAS, Secretary, CBC and CEO, Karmyogi Bharat, emphasized the importance of mandatory annual course completions on the iGOT Karmyogi platform and informed about its linkage with APARs, as directed by DoPT. She also highlighted the new scoring framework that assesses Ministries/Departments on their capacity building progress.</p><p>Sh. Shyama Prasad Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC, introduced the Rashtriya Karmyogi Jan Seva Program, a behavioural training initiative, and urged for early identification of Master Trainers in Chandigarh to enable its rollout before 15th August 2025.</p><p>Ms. Alka Mittal, Member (Admin), CBC, joined the event virtually and lauded Chandigarh Administration for onboarding over 25,000 officials, enrolling in 1,00,000+ courses, and completing 90,000+ learning modules on the iGOT Karmyogi platform.</p><p>Shri Rajeev Verma, Chief Secretary, Chandigarh, directed all departments to expedite onboarding and course completion and proposed a review meeting under his chairmanship to track progress.</p><p>This collaboration marks a significant step toward transforming governance through continuous learning and upskilling under Mission Karmyogi.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 726, 947, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member–HR, Capacity Building Commission, visited the Delhi Metro Rail Corporation (DMRC) Academy today to engage with the institution and gain insights into its training approach and organizational development model.</p><p>The Academy has demonstrated consistent improvements in training quality, currently holding a Three-Star rating under the NSCSTI framework. Dr. Balu reviewed their ongoing practices and experienced the simulation-based training technology used in preparing metro pilots.</p><p>He encouraged the Academy to:</p><p>1. Share selected training modules on the iGOT platform,<br>2. Contribute case studies to the Amrit Gyaan Kosh, and<br>3. Pursue re-accreditation under NSCSTI for continued quality enhancement.</p><p>Member HR also urged the Academy to strive for higher benchmarks of excellence and actively share its practices and learnings across the broader capacity building ecosystem. CBC and DMRC Academy discussed potential avenues for future collaboration in training design and knowledge exchange.</p><p>The Commission expresses its sincere appreciation to Mr. Ghansham Bansal, Dean, DMRC Academy, and his team for their hospitality and commitment to strengthening public service training.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 727, 948, 'en', 0, '<p>In alignment with our mission to empower Urban Local Body (ULB) officials to be citizen-centric, future-ready, and outcomes-driven, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with the Housing &amp; Urban Development Department, Government of Odisha, conducted a capacity-building workshop on 23rd July 2025 at the Odisha Urban Academy (OUA), Bhubaneswar.</p><p>The workshop convened 100+ ULB officials from across the state and featured domain and functional sessions on key areas such as the principles of #MissionKarmayogi, public procurement, and budget planning for ULBs, among others—equipping officials with the tools to drive more effective and accountable urban governance.</p><p>A major highlight was the demonstration of the #iGOTKarmayogi platform, emphasizing its role-based digital learning capabilities. With over 3 lakh officials from Odisha already onboarded, the state stands at the forefront of India’s digital capacity-building transformation.</p><p>The workshop was graced by senior dignitaries from both the Centre and the State, including Dr. Alka Mittal (Member – Administration, CBC), Smt. Usha Padhee, IAS (Principal Secretary, H&amp;UD Department, Government of Odisha), Shri S P Roy (Joint Secretary, CBC), Shri Satrughna Kar (Additional Secretary, H&amp;UD Department, Government of Odisha), and Dr Santanu Rath (Director, Odisha Urban Academy). Their presence and insights reaffirmed the shared commitment to strengthening institutional and individual capacities.</p><p>This initiative marks a significant step toward scalable, inclusive, and sustained capacity building across Odisha’s ULB ecosystem.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 727, 949, 'en', 0, '<p>In alignment with our mission to empower Urban Local Body (ULB) officials to be citizen-centric, future-ready, and outcomes-driven, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with the Housing &amp; Urban Development Department, Government of Odisha, conducted a capacity-building workshop on 23rd July 2025 at the Odisha Urban Academy (OUA), Bhubaneswar.</p><p>The workshop convened 100+ ULB officials from across the state and featured domain and functional sessions on key areas such as the principles of #MissionKarmayogi, public procurement, and budget planning for ULBs, among others—equipping officials with the tools to drive more effective and accountable urban governance.</p><p>A major highlight was the demonstration of the #iGOTKarmayogi platform, emphasizing its role-based digital learning capabilities. With over 3 lakh officials from Odisha already onboarded, the state stands at the forefront of India’s digital capacity-building transformation.</p><p>The workshop was graced by senior dignitaries from both the Centre and the State, including Dr. Alka Mittal (Member – Administration, CBC), Smt. Usha Padhee, IAS (Principal Secretary, H&amp;UD Department, Government of Odisha), Shri S P Roy (Joint Secretary, CBC), Shri Satrughna Kar (Additional Secretary, H&amp;UD Department, Government of Odisha), and Dr Santanu Rath (Director, Odisha Urban Academy). Their presence and insights reaffirmed the shared commitment to strengthening institutional and individual capacities.</p><p>This initiative marks a significant step toward scalable, inclusive, and sustained capacity building across Odisha’s ULB ecosystem.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 727, 950, 'en', 0, '<p>In alignment with our mission to empower Urban Local Body (ULB) officials to be citizen-centric, future-ready, and outcomes-driven, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with the Housing &amp; Urban Development Department, Government of Odisha, conducted a capacity-building workshop on 23rd July 2025 at the Odisha Urban Academy (OUA), Bhubaneswar.</p><p>The workshop convened 100+ ULB officials from across the state and featured domain and functional sessions on key areas such as the principles of #MissionKarmayogi, public procurement, and budget planning for ULBs, among others—equipping officials with the tools to drive more effective and accountable urban governance.</p><p>A major highlight was the demonstration of the #iGOTKarmayogi platform, emphasizing its role-based digital learning capabilities. With over 3 lakh officials from Odisha already onboarded, the state stands at the forefront of India’s digital capacity-building transformation.</p><p>The workshop was graced by senior dignitaries from both the Centre and the State, including Dr. Alka Mittal (Member – Administration, CBC), Smt. Usha Padhee, IAS (Principal Secretary, H&amp;UD Department, Government of Odisha), Shri S P Roy (Joint Secretary, CBC), Shri Satrughna Kar (Additional Secretary, H&amp;UD Department, Government of Odisha), and Dr Santanu Rath (Director, Odisha Urban Academy). Their presence and insights reaffirmed the shared commitment to strengthening institutional and individual capacities.</p><p>This initiative marks a significant step toward scalable, inclusive, and sustained capacity building across Odisha’s ULB ecosystem.</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 728, 951, 'en', 0, '<p>The National Standards for Civil Services Training Institutions (NSCSTI) 2.0 was officially launched today by the Hon’ble Minister of State for Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions, Dr Jitendra Singh at CSOI, Vinay Marg, New Delhi.</p><p>Developed by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) under Mission Karmayogi, NSCSTI 2.0 marks a significant upgrade to the world\'s first accreditation framework designed exclusively for civil services training institutions (CSTIs). The framework offers enhanced flexibility, addresses emerging tech needs, and promotes a holistic, future-ready and community-driven ecosystem for civil services training institutions.</p><p>In the keynote address by Hon’ble Minister, Dr Jitendra Singh emphasized the importance of creating future-ready civil servants through globally benchmarked, outcome-oriented training systems. He noted that NSCSTI 2.0 reflects India’s commitment to building a citizen-centric and performance-driven bureaucracy.</p><p>Setting the context for the new framework, Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman, CBC, highlighted the need for CSTIs to evolve in step with a rapidly changing governance landscape and underlined the importance of continuous institutional learning and improvement.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member HR, CBC, outlined the new and unique features of the framework, including the Karmayogi Competency Model (KCM), the Amrit Gyaan Kosh digital knowledge repository, and the Indian Knowledge System (IKS).</p><p>Dr Alka Mittal, Member Admin, CBC, spoke about the importance of quality in public training and urged CSTIs to pursue reaccreditation under the upgraded framework. She highlighted that NSCSTI 2.0 is not just about compliance but about driving a culture of excellence, innovation and accountability in training.</p><p>The event featured dignitaries from DoPT, CBC, and Karmayogi Bharat who spoke about the importance of strengthening the training ecosystem of civil services and furthering the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047.</p><p>As part of the launch, a ceremonial distribution of certificates was also held for institutes which were accredited under NSCSTI 1.0, recognizing the efforts of the civil service training institutions that have met national standards of excellence.</p><p>NSCSTI 2.0 sets a new benchmark in public sector training globally and reflects India’s leadership in governance reform and digital transformation in capacity building.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 728, 1242, 'en', 0, '<p>The National Standards for Civil Services Training Institutions (NSCSTI) 2.0 was officially launched today by the Hon’ble Minister of State for Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions, Dr Jitendra Singh at CSOI, Vinay Marg, New Delhi.</p><p>Developed by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) under Mission Karmayogi, NSCSTI 2.0 marks a significant upgrade to the world\'s first accreditation framework designed exclusively for civil services training institutions (CSTIs). The framework offers enhanced flexibility, addresses emerging tech needs, and promotes a holistic, future-ready and community-driven ecosystem for civil services training institutions.</p><p>In the keynote address by Hon’ble Minister, Dr Jitendra Singh emphasized the importance of creating future-ready civil servants through globally benchmarked, outcome-oriented training systems. He noted that NSCSTI 2.0 reflects India’s commitment to building a citizen-centric and performance-driven bureaucracy.</p><p>Setting the context for the new framework, Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman, CBC, highlighted the need for CSTIs to evolve in step with a rapidly changing governance landscape and underlined the importance of continuous institutional learning and improvement.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member HR, CBC, outlined the new and unique features of the framework, including the Karmayogi Competency Model (KCM), the Amrit Gyaan Kosh digital knowledge repository, and the Indian Knowledge System (IKS).</p><p>Dr Alka Mittal, Member Admin, CBC, spoke about the importance of quality in public training and urged CSTIs to pursue reaccreditation under the upgraded framework. She highlighted that NSCSTI 2.0 is not just about compliance but about driving a culture of excellence, innovation and accountability in training.</p><p>The event featured dignitaries from DoPT, CBC, and Karmayogi Bharat who spoke about the importance of strengthening the training ecosystem of civil services and furthering the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047.</p><p>As part of the launch, a ceremonial distribution of certificates was also held for institutes which were accredited under NSCSTI 1.0, recognizing the efforts of the civil service training institutions that have met national standards of excellence.</p><p>NSCSTI 2.0 sets a new benchmark in public sector training globally and reflects India’s leadership in governance reform and digital transformation in capacity building.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 728, 1244, 'en', 0, '<p>The National Standards for Civil Services Training Institutions (NSCSTI) 2.0 was officially launched today by the Hon’ble Minister of State for Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions, Dr Jitendra Singh at CSOI, Vinay Marg, New Delhi.</p><p>Developed by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) under Mission Karmayogi, NSCSTI 2.0 marks a significant upgrade to the world\'s first accreditation framework designed exclusively for civil services training institutions (CSTIs). The framework offers enhanced flexibility, addresses emerging tech needs, and promotes a holistic, future-ready and community-driven ecosystem for civil services training institutions.</p><p>In the keynote address by Hon’ble Minister, Dr Jitendra Singh emphasized the importance of creating future-ready civil servants through globally benchmarked, outcome-oriented training systems. He noted that NSCSTI 2.0 reflects India’s commitment to building a citizen-centric and performance-driven bureaucracy.</p><p>Setting the context for the new framework, Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman, CBC, highlighted the need for CSTIs to evolve in step with a rapidly changing governance landscape and underlined the importance of continuous institutional learning and improvement.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member HR, CBC, outlined the new and unique features of the framework, including the Karmayogi Competency Model (KCM), the Amrit Gyaan Kosh digital knowledge repository, and the Indian Knowledge System (IKS).</p><p>Dr Alka Mittal, Member Admin, CBC, spoke about the importance of quality in public training and urged CSTIs to pursue reaccreditation under the upgraded framework. She highlighted that NSCSTI 2.0 is not just about compliance but about driving a culture of excellence, innovation and accountability in training.</p><p>The event featured dignitaries from DoPT, CBC, and Karmayogi Bharat who spoke about the importance of strengthening the training ecosystem of civil services and fur