ite-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\"><br>&nbsp;</div>', '', 'full_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_event_description` (`bundle`, `deleted`, `entity_id`, `revision_id`, `langcode`, `delta`, `field_event_description_value`, `field_event_description_summary`, `field_event_description_format`) VALUES
('event', 0, 730, 953, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Capacity Building Commission, along with Karmayogi Bharat, met the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Delhi, Smt. Rekha Gupta and Chief Secretary to discuss the way forward for implementing #MissionKarmayogi in the Government of NCT of Delhi.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Under the Hon’ble CM’s leadership, Delhi is set to onboard 80,000 officials onto the #iGOTKarmayogi platform-marking a significant step in building a future-ready civil service.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The discussion led to 3 key outcomes:<br>• 100% Onboarding: All Group A, B, and C officials of the Delhi Government will be onboarded on #iGOT portal to enable continuous, structured learning.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">• Departmental Participation: A directive will be issued mandating participation of all departments with a nodal officer designated to drive the effort.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">• Jan Seva Rollout: A large-scale citizen-first governance initiative will be launched across departments.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Mission Karmayogi continues to expand across states and UTs empowering every civil servant with the competencies and tools to deliver better #governance and public service.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 730, 955, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Capacity Building Commission, along with Karmayogi Bharat, met the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Delhi, Smt. Rekha Gupta and Chief Secretary to discuss the way forward for implementing #MissionKarmayogi in the Government of NCT of Delhi.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Under the Hon’ble CM’s leadership, Delhi is set to onboard 80,000 officials onto the #iGOTKarmayogi platform-marking a significant step in building a future-ready civil service.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The discussion led to 3 key outcomes:<br>• 100% Onboarding: All Group A, B, and C officials of the Delhi Government will be onboarded on #iGOT portal to enable continuous, structured learning.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">• Departmental Participation: A directive will be issued mandating participation of all departments with a nodal officer designated to drive the effort.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">• Jan Seva Rollout: A large-scale citizen-first governance initiative will be launched across departments.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Mission Karmayogi continues to expand across states and UTs empowering every civil servant with the competencies and tools to deliver better #governance and public service.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 730, 1304, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Capacity Building Commission, along with Karmyogi Bharat, met the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Delhi, Smt. Rekha Gupta and Chief Secretary to discuss the way forward for implementing #MissionKarmyogi in the Government of NCT of Delhi.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Under the Hon’ble CM’s leadership, Delhi is set to onboard 80,000 officials onto the #iGOTKarmyogi platform-marking a significant step in building a future-ready civil service.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The discussion led to 3 key outcomes:<br>• 100% Onboarding: All Group A, B, and C officials of the Delhi Government will be onboarded on #iGOT portal to enable continuous, structured learning.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">• Departmental Participation: A directive will be issued mandating participation of all departments with a nodal officer designated to drive the effort.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">• Jan Seva Rollout: A large-scale citizen-first governance initiative will be launched across departments.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Mission Karmyogi continues to expand across states and UTs empowering every civil servant with the competencies and tools to deliver better #governance and public service.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 731, 954, 'en', 0, '<p>Under #MissionKarmayogi, states are stepping forward to build a culture of continuous learning and #Bihar joins the growing list, embracing it.</p><p>As envisioned by the Hon’ble Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi Ji, every state is being encouraged to onboard onto #iGOTKarmayogi to make learning a core part of governance.</p><p>After successful Learning Weeks in Andaman &amp; Nicobar, Maharashtra and Rajasthan, it’s encouraging to see Bihar take this forward through the launch of #BiharLearningWeek (11–17 July 2025), a powerful step toward building a self-driven and future-ready government workforce.</p><p>As part of Mission Karmayogi, every official is encouraged to complete at least 4 hours of learning on #iGOT platform or curated webinars.</p><p>This growing momentum reflects a shared national commitment to make learning continuous, relevant, and rooted in-service delivery.</p><p>Congratulations to the Government of Bihar, Capacity Building Commission and Karmayogi Bharat team for taking this forward.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 731, 956, 'en', 0, '<p>Under #MissionKarmayogi, states are stepping forward to build a culture of continuous learning and #Bihar joins the growing list, embracing it.</p><p>As envisioned by the Hon’ble Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi Ji, every state is being encouraged to onboard onto #iGOTKarmayogi to make learning a core part of governance.</p><p>After successful Learning Weeks in Andaman &amp; Nicobar, Maharashtra and Rajasthan, it’s encouraging to see Bihar take this forward through the launch of #BiharLearningWeek (11–17 July 2025), a powerful step toward building a self-driven and future-ready government workforce.</p><p>As part of Mission Karmayogi, every official is encouraged to complete at least 4 hours of learning on #iGOT platform or curated webinars.</p><p>This growing momentum reflects a shared national commitment to make learning continuous, relevant, and rooted in-service delivery.</p><p>Congratulations to the Government of Bihar, Capacity Building Commission and Karmayogi Bharat team for taking this forward.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 732, 957, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Member-HR, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Capacity Building Commission, led a workshop on 10th July 2025 for Capacity Building Units of MDOs, attended by CBU Heads and officials from 30 Ministries and Departments.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">It focused on:</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">🔹 Clarifying the roles of CBUs<br>🔹Understanding what competencies are needed for different roles<br>🔹 Improving implementation and monitoring of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs)<br>🔹 Planning for domain course development and the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program rollout<br>🔹Facilitating cross-learning through the exchange of good practices across Ministries</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dr. Anju Rathi Rana, ILS, Secretary, Department of Legal Affairs, shared impactful best practices for implementing Mission Karmayogi undertaken under her leadership—setting a strong example for peer Ministries. The workshop enabled CBUs to recalibrate their strategies for structured, demand-driven capacity building aligned with the Karmayogi Competency Model.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 732, 958, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Member-HR, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Capacity Building Commission, led a workshop on 10th July 2025 for Capacity Building Units of MDOs, attended by CBU Heads and officials from 30 Ministries and Departments.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">It focused on:</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">🔹 Clarifying the roles of CBUs<br>🔹Understanding what competencies are needed for different roles<br>🔹 Improving implementation and monitoring of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs)<br>🔹 Planning for domain course development and the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program rollout<br>🔹Facilitating cross-learning through the exchange of good practices across Ministries</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dr. Anju Rathi Rana, ILS, Secretary, Department of Legal Affairs, shared impactful best practices for implementing Mission Karmayogi undertaken under her leadership—setting a strong example for peer Ministries. The workshop enabled CBUs to recalibrate their strategies for structured, demand-driven capacity building aligned with the Karmayogi Competency Model.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 732, 965, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Member-HR, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Capacity Building Commission, led a workshop on 10th July 2025 for Capacity Building Units of MDOs, attended by CBU Heads and officials from 30 Ministries and Departments.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">It focused on:</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">🔹 Clarifying the roles of CBUs<br>🔹Understanding what competencies are needed for different roles<br>🔹 Improving implementation and monitoring of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs)<br>🔹 Planning for domain course development and the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program rollout<br>🔹Facilitating cross-learning through the exchange of good practices across Ministries</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dr. Anju Rathi Rana, ILS, Secretary, Department of Legal Affairs, shared impactful best practices for implementing Mission Karmayogi undertaken under her leadership—setting a strong example for peer Ministries. The workshop enabled CBUs to recalibrate their strategies for structured, demand-driven capacity building aligned with the Karmayogi Competency Model.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 733, 959, 'en', 0, '<p>Through deep partnerships with states, the Capacity Building Commission is building the foundation for a future-ready civil service, one that is skilled, responsive and aligned to the aspirations of a changing #India.</p><p>Today, a tripartite MoU was signed between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat and the Government of Tripura, marking a key milestone in strengthening governance capabilities in the state.</p><p>The signing was followed by an orientation session led by Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, introducing the framework and vision of #MissionKarmayogi. Ms. Shobhana Rana, Advisor on Content Development and Partnerships, Karmayogi Bharat, familiarised officials with the functionalities and usage of #iGOTKarmayogi Platform. Shri J.K. Sinha, Chief Secretary, Tripura, reaffirmed the state’s resolve to promote mindset change and strengthen a governance model that is both citizen-centric and digitally driven. S P Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC, outlined specific areas where #Tripura can collaborate with #CBC and #KarmayogiBharat, reinforcing the state’s intent to embed structured capacity-building in its governance approach.</p><p>The orientation witnessed active participation from Secretaries, Special Secretaries, Directors, and Heads of 51 departments of the Government of Tripura.</p><p>With this partnership, Tripura joins the national movement to build responsive, capable and future-ready civil service contributing to the vision of #ViksitBharat. The state is also experimenting with several transformational initiatives, offering valuable learnings for CBC and other states we collaborate with.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 733, 1306, 'en', 0, '<p>Through deep partnerships with states, the Capacity Building Commission is building the foundation for a future-ready civil service, one that is skilled, responsive and aligned to the aspirations of a changing #India.</p><p>Today, a tripartite MoU was signed between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmyogi Bharat and the Government of Tripura, marking a key milestone in strengthening governance capabilities in the state.</p><p>The signing was followed by an orientation session led by Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, introducing the framework and vision of #MissionKarmyogi. Ms. Shobhana Rana, Advisor on Content Development and Partnerships, Karmyogi Bharat, familiarised officials with the functionalities and usage of #iGOTKarmyogi Platform. Shri J.K. Sinha, Chief Secretary, Tripura, reaffirmed the state’s resolve to promote mindset change and strengthen a governance model that is both citizen-centric and digitally driven. S P Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC, outlined specific areas where #Tripura can collaborate with #CBC and #KarmyogiBharat, reinforcing the state’s intent to embed structured capacity-building in its governance approach.</p><p>The orientation witnessed active participation from Secretaries, Special Secretaries, Directors, and Heads of 51 departments of the Government of Tripura.</p><p>With this partnership, Tripura joins the national movement to build responsive, capable and future-ready civil service contributing to the vision of #ViksitBharat. The state is also experimenting with several transformational initiatives, offering valuable learnings for CBC and other states we collaborate with.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 734, 960, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission and Karmayogi Bharat jointly hosted ‘DigiManthan’ at Vigyan Bhawan on 16.04.24 to help Civil Services Training Institutions create more e-learning courses.</p><p>In a significant step towards embracing technology, Central Training Institutes are stepping up their game. Yesterday, 24 CTIs committed to launching a total of 78 digital courses by June 30th. This initiative will revolutionize the delivery of digital training for all central civil servants!</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 735, 962, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member-HR, Capacity Building Commission, participated as a panelist in the session on “IKS and Institutional Building” at the First Annual Academic Conference on Indian Knowledge Systems, held at Jawaharlal Nehru University.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The session focused on the relevance of Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS) in shaping institutional frameworks and building public leadership. Dr. Balasubramaniam spoke about how IKS and capacity building are closely linked, particularly in the context of lifelong learning as a continuous process for both individuals and institutions.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">He also highlighted the need to integrate citizen-centric governance as a core outcome of capacity building efforts, drawing on indigenous knowledge and contextual understanding to make public systems more responsive and inclusive.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The conference brought together academics, practitioners, and policymakers to explore how IKS can inform contemporary governance and institutional development in India.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 735, 963, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member-HR, Capacity Building Commission, participated as a panelist in the session on “IKS and Institutional Building” at the First Annual Academic Conference on Indian Knowledge Systems, held at Jawaharlal Nehru University.</p><p>The session focused on the relevance of Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS) in shaping institutional frameworks and building public leadership. Dr. Balasubramaniam spoke about how IKS and capacity building are closely linked, particularly in the context of lifelong learning as a continuous process for both individuals and institutions.</p><p>He also highlighted the need to integrate citizen-centric governance as a core outcome of capacity building efforts, drawing on indigenous knowledge and contextual understanding to make public systems more responsive and inclusive.</p><p>The conference brought together academics, practitioners, and policymakers to explore how IKS can inform contemporary governance and institutional development in India.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 736, 966, 'en', 0, '<p>On 21st April 2025, the Capacity Building Commission, in partnership with #SCOPE (Standing Conference of Public Enterprises) launched #DAKSH (Development of Aspiration, Knowledge, Succession and Harmony)-a first-of-its-kind leadership program designed exclusively for senior executives of India’s Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs). With McKinsey &amp; Company and Indian Institute of Management Ahmedabad as Knowledge Partners, DAKSH is a transformative initiative that aims to build a future-ready, value-driven leadership pipeline for the public sector.</p><p>The program was launched by Shri Arunish Chawla, Secretary, DIPAM, in the presence of Shri Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman, CBC; Smt. Soma Mondal, Member, Public Enterprises Selection Board (PESB); Shri K.P. Mahadevaswamy, Chairman, SCOPE; Shri Atul Sobti, DG, SCOPE; and Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), CBC. Their powerful insights set the tone for a future-ready, purpose-driven leadership agenda. The CMDs and Director(HR)s of #CPSEs also attended the launch program.</p><p>As CPSEs play a central role in India’s economic and social development, it is critical to develop competent, innovative and agile leaders. DAKSH is about preparing leaders to navigate complexity, scale impact, and steer India’s most strategic institutions towards inclusive, sustainable growth. It is a unique program built on world-class design principles, tailored to the Indian context.</p><p>As the DAKSH leadership journey began for the first cohort of over 70 senior officers of CPSEs, it is set to become a global benchmark in public leadership development.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 737, 967, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC) has signed a contract with the Kaivalya Education Foundation (KEF) to lead a transformative initiative focused on strengthening Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs).</p><p>As part of this partnership, 60 Gram Panchayats across Andhra Pradesh, Assam, Gujarat and Odisha will see implementation of a demonstrable, measurable, and scalable model of capacity building at the grassroots level.</p><p>Anchored in the vision of Mission Karmayogi, the initiative aims to enhance the capabilities of both elected representatives and government functionaries, fostering more effective, responsive, and citizen-centric governance.</p><p>Key Highlights:<br>🔹 Tech-enabled ecosystem for continuous capacity building<br>🔹 Custom-built e-learning platform, mobile app, and AI-powered chatbot<br>🔹 Personalized learning and on-demand support for PRI members<br>🔹 On-ground implementation anchored by KEF under the guidance of CBC</p><p>This partnership marks a major milestone as Mission Karmayogi expands to the last mile—empowering local institutions to become future-ready agents of change.</p><p>Together, we’re moving closer to a Viksit Bharat through stronger, more accountable Panchayats.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 739, 969, 'en', 0, '<p>Top leadership is in the room today because true transformation requires alignment at every level. Bottom-up change only succeeds when it is met with committed, value-driven leadership from the top. That is why Secretaries and Additional Secretaries from over 40 Ministries and Departments are undergoing an immersive orientation to lead Phase II of the Rashtriya Karmayogi – Large Scale Jan Seva Programme (RK-LSJSP)-India’s largest cognitive and behavioural transformation in governance.</p><p>This program is not about policy tweaks or procedural shifts-it’s about reimagining public service itself. Designed to reach over 7,00,000 government officials across Bharat,Rashtriya Karmayogi aims to instill hashtag#SevaBhaav, strengthen purpose, and embed citizen-first thinking across the system. As the architects of India’s governance machinery, Secretaries and Additional Secretaries are not just participants-they are the catalysts of this mission, anchoring the change within their ministries and setting the tone for cascading leadership across the country.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 739, 1308, 'en', 0, '<p>Top leadership is in the room today because true transformation requires alignment at every level. Bottom-up change only succeeds when it is met with committed, value-driven leadership from the top. That is why Secretaries and Additional Secretaries from over 40 Ministries and Departments are undergoing an immersive orientation to lead Phase II of the Rashtriya Karmyogi – Large Scale Jan Seva Programme (RK-LSJSP)-India’s largest cognitive and behavioural transformation in governance.</p><p>This program is not about policy tweaks or procedural shifts-it’s about reimagining public service itself. Designed to reach over 7,00,000 government officials across Bharat,Rashtriya Karmyogi aims to instill hashtag#SevaBhaav, strengthen purpose, and embed citizen-first thinking across the system. As the architects of India’s governance machinery, Secretaries and Additional Secretaries are not just participants-they are the catalysts of this mission, anchoring the change within their ministries and setting the tone for cascading leadership across the country.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 740, 970, 'en', 0, '<p>At the heart of today’s Learning &amp; Development Workshop at National Academy of Agricultural Sciences -NAAS India, teams stepped into innovation labs-crafting the future of grassroots governance. As part of the Capacity Building program for #ViksitPanchayat, each breakout room became a hub of collaboration where real-world challenges were met with purpose-driven design.</p><p>The modules being shaped go beyond theory. They are anchored in field realities, focused on equipping Panchayat leaders with the skills, mindsets, and tools needed to lead transformation on the ground. With citizen-centricity at their core, these learning journeys aim to make local governance the driving force behind a truly #ViksitBharat.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 741, 971, 'en', 0, '<p><span style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(33, 37, 41);display:inline !important;float:none;font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The International Day of Yoga has been celebrated across the world annually on June 21 since 2015. This year 2025, the theme for International Day of Yoga is “Yoga for One Earth, One Health.” Yoga, a transformative practice, represents the harmony of mind and body, the balance between thought and action, and the unity of restraint and fulfillment. It integrates the body, mind, spirit, and soul, offering a holistic approach to health and well-being that brings peace to our hectic lives. Its power to transform is what we celebrate on this special day.</span></p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 742, 972, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission organised a two-day consultative workshop on the \"Capacity Building Needs of Civil Services of India\" at the Lal Bahadur Shastri National Academy Of Administration from 22nd to 23rd April 2024.</p><p>The workshop included the participation of leadership and senior faculties from the 25 Central Training Institutions (CTIs), the respective Cadre Controlling Authorities, and senior leadership from LBSNAA and the Department of Personnel and Training (DoPT).</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 743, 973, 'en', 0, '<p>With 6000 officials trained across 49 MDOs so far - the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program - Phase 1 is helping government officials connect their work with service to citizens.</p><p>Today, Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievances, Government of India and Department of Pension &amp; Pensioners\' Welfare (DoPPW) hosted an event to share feedback and thank the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) for facilitating Phase 1 of the program for their departments. The training had a noticeable impact on officers-helping them reflect on their work with greater clarity, build stronger connections with citizens, and understand how their roles contribute to the broader goals of governance. Seeing this shift among their teams, the departments came together to acknowledge the value of the program and express their appreciation for the structured approach taken by #CBC.</p><p>Master Trainers and participants spoke about how the training helped them reflect on their role and connect daily tasks with a deeper purpose of public service.</p><p>Shri Srinivas Voruganti, Secretary, DARPG and DoPPW, appreciated the training effort and its relevance for improving public service delivery.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, and Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman, CBC, shared their remarks and thanked officials for their honest reflections and participation.</p><p>We now look forward to Phase 2, which will train 7,00,000 officials across Bharat, further strengthening citizen-first governance.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 743, 1309, 'en', 0, '<p>With 6000 officials trained across 49 MDOs so far - the Rashtriya Karmyogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program - Phase 1 is helping government officials connect their work with service to citizens.</p><p>Today, Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievances, Government of India and Department of Pension &amp; Pensioners\' Welfare (DoPPW) hosted an event to share feedback and thank the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) for facilitating Phase 1 of the program for their departments. The training had a noticeable impact on officers-helping them reflect on their work with greater clarity, build stronger connections with citizens, and understand how their roles contribute to the broader goals of governance. Seeing this shift among their teams, the departments came together to acknowledge the value of the program and express their appreciation for the structured approach taken by #CBC.</p><p>Master Trainers and participants spoke about how the training helped them reflect on their role and connect daily tasks with a deeper purpose of public service.</p><p>Shri Srinivas Voruganti, Secretary, DARPG and DoPPW, appreciated the training effort and its relevance for improving public service delivery.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, and Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman, CBC, shared their remarks and thanked officials for their honest reflections and participation.</p><p>We now look forward to Phase 2, which will train 7,00,000 officials across Bharat, further strengthening citizen-first governance.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 744, 974, 'en', 0, '<p>Under #MissionKarmayogi, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with the Directorate of Urban Local Bodies (DULB), Government of Haryana, organized a one-day Capacity Building Workshop for Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) of the state at the Haryana Institute of Public Administration (HIPA), Gurugram.</p><p>The workshop witnessed the participation of over 100 senior officials, including Municipal Council Presidents, Commissioners, District Municipal Commissioners, Executive Officers, and representatives from #DULB and #HIPA. Participants were introduced to the #iGOTKarmayogi platform aimed at fostering a culture of anytime, anywhere, #ContinuousLearning for government officials. Deliberations throughout the day centered on embedding the principles of citizen-centric #governance and enhancing service delivery – key principles of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>The event was graced by the presence of Smt. Rajrani Malhotra (Hon\'ble Mayor, Gurugram Municipal Corporation), Dr. Alka Mittal (Member – Administration, CBC), Shri Pankaj (Director General, DULB Haryana), Shri S P Roy (Joint Secretary, CBC), and Shri Pradeep Dahiya (Commissioner, Municipal Corporation Gurugram).</p><p>This workshop marks a pivotal step in equipping Haryana’s urban governance ecosystem with the skills and capacities needed to realize the vision of #ViksitBharat2047.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 745, 975, 'en', 0, '<p>As part of #MissionKarmayogi, Capacity Building Commission (CBC) is committed to enhancing the competencies of all civil servants, including those in Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs). In today’s dynamic and rapidly evolving landscape, CPSEs need agile and future-ready leaders capable of driving transformative growth.</p><p>To support this vision, CBC, in collaboration with the Standing Conference of Public Enterprises (#SCOPE), signed an MoU on 17th June 2025 to launch the second edition of the #DAKSH Program. This program under this initiative will be delivered with Egon Zehnder as the Knowledge Partner and the Indian Institute of Management, Indore as the Academic Partner.</p><p>Egon Zehnder and #IIM Indore will co-design and implement a cutting-edge leadership program focused on building strategic, functional and behavioral capabilities among senior #CPSE executives.</p><p>The program is tailored for high-potential leaders-GMs, CGMs, and EDs-who are poised to take on Board-level roles in the near future. Through this initiative, we aim to create a robust talent pipeline of visionary and competent public sector leaders.</p><p>We express our sincere gratitude to our esteemed committee members Mr. Ayush Gupta, Director (HR), GAIL (India) Limited, Mr. K K Singh, Director (Personnel), Steel Authority of India Limited, Dr. Vinay Ranjan, PhD, Director (HR), Coal India Limited for their continued support and guidance. Thanks to Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Admin), CBC and Mr. Atul Sobti, Director General, #SCOPE, for their drive and leadership in making this happen.</p><p>This is a step forward in shaping a new generation of visionary public sector leaders-leaders who will help deliver a capable, competent and confident #ViksitBharat.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 745, 977, 'en', 0, '<p>As part of #MissionKarmayogi, Capacity Building Commission (CBC) is committed to enhancing the competencies of all civil servants, including those in Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs). In today’s dynamic and rapidly evolving landscape, CPSEs need agile and future-ready leaders capable of driving transformative growth.</p><p>To support this vision, CBC, in collaboration with the Standing Conference of Public Enterprises (#SCOPE), signed an MoU on 17th June 2025 to launch the second edition of the #DAKSH Program. This program under this initiative will be delivered with Egon Zehnder as the Knowledge Partner and the Indian Institute of Management, Indore as the Academic Partner.</p><p>Egon Zehnder and #IIM Indore will co-design and implement a cutting-edge leadership program focused on building strategic, functional and behavioral capabilities among senior #CPSE executives.</p><p>The program is tailored for high-potential leaders-GMs, CGMs, and EDs-who are poised to take on Board-level roles in the near future. Through this initiative, we aim to create a robust talent pipeline of visionary and competent public sector leaders.</p><p>We express our sincere gratitude to our esteemed committee members Mr. Ayush Gupta, Director (HR), GAIL (India) Limited, Mr. K K Singh, Director (Personnel), Steel Authority of India Limited, Dr. Vinay Ranjan, PhD, Director (HR), Coal India Limited for their continued support and guidance. Thanks to Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Admin), CBC and Mr. Atul Sobti, Director General, #SCOPE, for their drive and leadership in making this happen.</p><p>This is a step forward in shaping a new generation of visionary public sector leaders-leaders who will help deliver a capable, competent and confident #ViksitBharat.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 746, 976, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) held a meeting with the Chandigarh Administration for implementation of #MissionKarmayogi in the Union Territory of Chandigarh.</p><p>The meeting was presided over by Shri Rajeev Verma, IAS, Chief Secretary- Union Territory of Chandigarh, and attended by all Heads of department and other senior officials of the Union Territory.</p><p>The CBC team, led by Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), and Smt. V Lalithalakshmi, Secretary, CBC and CEO, Karmayogi Bharat, provided an insightful overview of Mission Karmayogi — the National Programme for Civil Services Capacity Building. The team highlighted the importance of capacity-building through Capacity Building Plans for all UT Chandigarh departments and the transition to role-based, competency-driven learning, while also providing a walkthrough of the iGOT platform in enhancing governance capabilities.</p><p>To drive the successful implementation of Mission Karmayogi in Chandigarh, the Chief Secretary directed the immediate formation of Capacity Building Unit (CBU), ensuring 100% onboarding of officials onto the #iGOT platform and completion of at least four courses by all officials within a month. A dedicated workshop will also be conducted by the #iGOTKarmayogi Bharat team, to guide nodal officers in effectively navigating the platform.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 746, 1385, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) held a meeting with the Chandigarh Administration for implementation of #MissionKarmayogi in the Union Territory of Chandigarh.</p><p>The meeting was presided over by Shri Rajeev Verma, IAS, Chief Secretary- Union Territory of Chandigarh, and attended by all Heads of department and other senior officials of the Union Territory.</p><p>The CBC team, led by Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), and Smt. V Lalithalakshmi, Secretary, CBC and CEO, Karmayogi Bharat, provided an insightful overview of Mission Karmayogi — the National Program for Civil Services Capacity Building. The team highlighted the importance of capacity-building through Capacity Building Plans for all UT Chandigarh departments and the transition to role-based, competency-driven learning, while also providing a walkthrough of the iGOT platform in enhancing governance capabilities.</p><p>To drive the successful implementation of Mission Karmayogi in Chandigarh, the Chief Secretary directed the immediate formation of Capacity Building Unit (CBU), ensuring 100% onboarding of officials onto the #iGOT platform and completion of at least four courses by all officials within a month. A dedicated workshop will also be conducted by the #iGOTKarmayogi Bharat team, to guide nodal officers in effectively navigating the platform.</p>', '', 'basic_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_event_description` (`bundle`, `deleted`, `entity_id`, `revision_id`, `langcode`, `delta`, `field_event_description_value`, `field_event_description_summary`, `field_event_description_format`) VALUES
('event', 0, 747, 978, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, visited the Matsushita Institute of Government and Management, Japan.</p><p>During his visit, he interacted with the Institute’s senior leadership and associates currently undergoing training to serve in public life. The discussions focused on understanding how the Institute nurtures young professionals to take on leadership roles in governance and public service.</p><p>Founded in 1979 by Konosuke Matsushita, the Institute was built on the belief that solving a nation\'s problems requires nurturing ethical, visionary leaders-not just bureaucrats. Its model combines intensive field experience, long-term mentoring, and a strong moral foundation. Over 50% of its alumni have gone on to hold elected office in Japan including Prime Ministers, Ministers, and Governors - a rare, measurable example of leadership development directly shaping national governance.</p><p>This aligns closely with CBC’s commitment to transforming India’s civil services into a citizen-centric, future-ready workforce-grounded in values and driven by purpose.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 748, 979, 'en', 0, '<p>Under #MissionKarmayogi, the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), in collaboration with the Department of Municipal Administration and Urban Development (MA&amp;UD), Government of Andhra Pradesh, and with the support of the Commissioner and Director of Municipal Administration (CDMA), organized a one-day #CapacityBuilding Workshop for Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) at the School of Planning &amp; Architecture Vijayawada.</p><p>The workshop brought together 175+ officials from 123 ULBs and key urban departments—including MEPMA, Public Health, and Town Planning.</p><p>Participants were introduced to the #iGOTKarmayogi platform to foster a culture of continuous learning for citizen-centric governance, and professional development. The discussions helped identify key training needs and priority areas for skilling ULB officials to drive better outcomes on the ground.</p><p>The workshop was graced by the presence of Shri Sureshkumar S Nair, I.A.S. (Principal Secretary, MA &amp; UD, Andhra Pradesh); Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Admin), Capacity Building Commission; Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi, I.A.S. (Secretary, CBC and CEO, Karamayogi Bharat); and Dr. P. Sampath Kumar, I.A.S. (Commissioner &amp; Director of Municipal Administration).</p><p>This initiative is a step toward building a resilient, future-ready urban workforce, aligned with the vision of #SwarnaAndhra2047.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 749, 980, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission carried out an on-site assessment at the Animal Training School, Indo-Tibetan Border Police, in Lohitpur, Arunachal Pradesh on 21st and 22nd March 2025.</p><p>We are delighted to announce that the institute has successfully achieved accreditation under the NSCSTI - National Standards for Civil Service Training Institutions | Capacity Building Commission. The assessment was efficiently facilitated by col (Dr) K Jagannathan and S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission, along with Jagan Sridhar and Susan Thomas.</p><p>A heartfelt thanks to the nodal officer, Mr. Pamei and his team for his support in ensuring a smooth process.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 749, 1050, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission carried out an on-site assessment at the Animal Training School, Indo-Tibetan Border Police, in Lohitpur, Arunachal Pradesh on 21st and 22nd March 2025.</p><p>We are delighted to announce that the institute has successfully achieved accreditation under the NSCSTI - National Standards for Civil Service Training Institutions | Capacity Building Commission. The assessment was efficiently facilitated by col (Dr) K Jagannathan and S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission, along with Jagan Sridhar and Susan Thomas.</p><p>A heartfelt thanks to the nodal officer, Mr. Pamei and his team for his support in ensuring a smooth process.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 750, 981, 'en', 0, '<p>Day 1 Highlights | Rise with Pride: Lead. Evolve. Transform 🌟<br>📍 Alleppey, Kerala<br>📅 11th June 2025<br>We are proud to kick off “Rise with Pride: Lead. Evolve. Transform”, a high-impact leadership development program set against the tranquil backdrop of Kerala.<br>With 50 senior professionals from both the Public Sector and Private Sector joining us, the energy, experience, and diversity in the room set the stage for powerful exchanges and meaningful learning.<br>✨ Day 1 Key Moments:<br>🔹 Welcome Address<br>By Dr. Alka Mittal, Member – Capacity Building Commission of India, Former CMD &amp; Director (HR), ONGC, and our esteemed Program Advisor. She highlighted the critical role of leadership evolution in building future-ready organizations.<br>🔹 Keynote Address<br>By Ms. Usha Singh, Director (HR), MOIL. Her address encouraged leaders to lead with authenticity, empathy, and strength.<br>🔹 Inaugural Address<br>By Dr. Dr. Ranjit Rath, Chairman &amp; Managing Director, Oil India Limited. His words inspired participants to embrace transformation and lead with vision.<br>🪔 Ceremonial Lighting of the Lamp</p><p>Dr. Alka Mittal, Ms. Usha Singh, and Dr. Dr. Ranjit Rath Rath came together to light the ceremonial lamp—an auspicious beginning to four days of growth, dialogue, and discovery.<br>This is only the beginning of an enriching journey. Stay tuned for more updates as we continue to lead, evolve, and transform together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 750, 983, 'en', 0, '<p>Day 1 Highlights | Rise with Pride: Lead. Evolve. Transform 🌟<br>📍 Alleppey, Kerala<br>📅 11th June 2025<br>We are proud to kick off “Rise with Pride: Lead. Evolve. Transform”, a high-impact leadership development program set against the tranquil backdrop of Kerala.<br>With 50 senior professionals from both the Public Sector and Private Sector joining us, the energy, experience, and diversity in the room set the stage for powerful exchanges and meaningful learning.<br>✨ Day 1 Key Moments:<br>🔹 Welcome Address<br>By Dr. Alka Mittal, Member – Capacity Building Commission of India, Former CMD &amp; Director (HR), ONGC, and our esteemed Program Advisor. She highlighted the critical role of leadership evolution in building future-ready organizations.<br>🔹 Keynote Address<br>By Ms. Usha Singh, Director (HR), MOIL. Her address encouraged leaders to lead with authenticity, empathy, and strength.<br>🔹 Inaugural Address<br>By Dr. Dr. Ranjit Rath, Chairman &amp; Managing Director, Oil India Limited. His words inspired participants to embrace transformation and lead with vision.<br>🪔 Ceremonial Lighting of the Lamp</p><p>Dr. Alka Mittal, Ms. Usha Singh, and Dr. Dr. Ranjit Rath Rath came together to light the ceremonial lamp—an auspicious beginning to four days of growth, dialogue, and discovery.<br>This is only the beginning of an enriching journey. Stay tuned for more updates as we continue to lead, evolve, and transform together.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 752, 984, 'en', 0, '<p>Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program – From Learning to Action.</p><p>The Rashtriya Karmayogi Program has trained another additional batch of officials from multiple ministries and departments over the past 3 days, continuing its mission of embedding #SewaBhaav in governance. Officials stepped away from their desks to rethink their role-not just as administrators, but as facilitators of citizen-centric service.</p><p>Understanding how every action-big or small-impacts citizens, this program is not just training but a shift in perspective rooted in Seva Bhaav and Svadharma. From the way policies are communicated to how challenges are approached, this program has encouraged participants to see governance through the lens of impact rather than process.</p><p>Now, as certified Master Trainers, they take on the responsibility of further training officials within their respective ministries, departments, and organizations-ensuring that service-oriented governance is not just discussed in a training room, but practiced at every level.</p><p>And this is just one step in a larger journey. With the next phase set to train 700000 government officials across Bharat, the movement is not far. The shift from process-driven to purpose-driven governance is taking shape.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 752, 1311, 'en', 0, '<p>Rashtriya Karmyogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program – From Learning to Action.</p><p>The Rashtriya Karmyogi Program has trained another additional batch of officials from multiple ministries and departments over the past 3 days, continuing its mission of embedding #SewaBhaav in governance. Officials stepped away from their desks to rethink their role-not just as administrators, but as facilitators of citizen-centric service.</p><p>Understanding how every action-big or small-impacts citizens, this program is not just training but a shift in perspective rooted in Seva Bhaav and Svadharma. From the way policies are communicated to how challenges are approached, this program has encouraged participants to see governance through the lens of impact rather than process.</p><p>Now, as certified Master Trainers, they take on the responsibility of further training officials within their respective ministries, departments, and organizations-ensuring that service-oriented governance is not just discussed in a training room, but practiced at every level.</p><p>And this is just one step in a larger journey. With the next phase set to train 700000 government officials across Bharat, the movement is not far. The shift from process-driven to purpose-driven governance is taking shape.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 753, 985, 'en', 0, '<p>A landmark moment for governance in the Capital</p><p>Government of NCT of Delhi Signs MoU with Capacity Building Commission and Karmayogi Bharat for Implementation of #MissionKarmayogi</p><p>In a major step towards strengthening governance and public service delivery, the Government of the National Capital Territory (NCT) of Delhi today signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and Karmayogi Bharat for the implementation of Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>The MoU was signed in the presence of the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Delhi, Smt. Rekha Gupta; the Chief Secretary of Delhi, Shri Dharmendra; Member (Administration), Capacity Building Commission, Dr. Alka Mittal and other senior officials from #CBC, Karmayogi Bharat and Delhi Government.</p><p>Under the visionary leadership of the Hon’ble Chief Minister, #Delhi is now poised to scale this effort significantly by onboarding all officials onto the #iGOT portal, marking one of the largest state-level initiatives under Mission Karmayogi.</p><p>Capacity Building Commission and Karmayogi Bharat commended the leadership of the Delhi Government and assured full support in enabling continuous learning and strengthening capacities of all the officials. This includes assistance in formulating Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) for departments, and strengthening the capacities of urban local body (ULB) officials to deliver citizen-centric services more effectively. And Large Scale Intervention for Delhi government officials for inculcating Sewa Bhav.</p><p>With this milestone, Mission Karmayogi continues to expand its footprint across states and Union Territories, creating a uniform and progressive ecosystem for capacity building.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 753, 1312, 'en', 0, '<p>A landmark moment for governance in the Capital</p><p>Government of NCT of Delhi Signs MoU with Capacity Building Commission and Karmyogi Bharat for Implementation of #MissionKarmyogi</p><p>In a major step towards strengthening governance and public service delivery, the Government of the National Capital Territory (NCT) of Delhi today signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and Karmyogi Bharat for the implementation of Mission Karmyogi.</p><p>The MoU was signed in the presence of the Hon’ble Chief Minister of Delhi, Smt. Rekha Gupta; the Chief Secretary of Delhi, Shri Dharmendra; Member (Administration), Capacity Building Commission, Dr. Alka Mittal and other senior officials from #CBC, Karmyogi Bharat and Delhi Government.</p><p>Under the visionary leadership of the Hon’ble Chief Minister, #Delhi is now poised to scale this effort significantly by onboarding all officials onto the #iGOT portal, marking one of the largest state-level initiatives under Mission Karmyogi.</p><p>Capacity Building Commission and Karmyogi Bharat commended the leadership of the Delhi Government and assured full support in enabling continuous learning and strengthening capacities of all the officials. This includes assistance in formulating Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) for departments, and strengthening the capacities of urban local body (ULB) officials to deliver citizen-centric services more effectively. And Large Scale Intervention for Delhi government officials for inculcating Sewa Bhav.</p><p>With this milestone, Mission Karmyogi continues to expand its footprint across states and Union Territories, creating a uniform and progressive ecosystem for capacity building.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 754, 987, 'en', 0, '<p>Reimagining Civil Service Training: Decolonizing Mindsets &amp; Institutions</p><p>For decades, India\'s CSTIs have operated within frameworks inherited from colonial rule-shaping administrative structures, policy-making approaches &amp; institutional cultures that often remain disconnected from realities of Bharat’s civilizational ethos. This calls for a necessary shift.</p><p>Today @IIT Delhi, Abhijnana-Workshop on Decolonizing CSTIs brings together thought leaders, policymakers &amp; academics to initiate this transformation. Organized by Capacity Building Commission,Training Division, DoPT, IKS Programme @IIT Delhi &amp; INDICA, this workshop is designed to empower civil servants &amp; CSTIs with intellectual tools to draw from IKS-not as an abstract idea, but as a practical approach to governance &amp; administration.</p><p>Nomesh Bolia, Prof., IIT Delhi,remarked that civil services are deeply respected in India not just for their authority but for their role in nation-building,urging participants to explore how key concepts can be materialized into actionable steps for decolonization.</p><p>Prof. KE Seetha Ram,Senior Consulting Specialist, ADB Institute, highlighted that institutional transformation requires rethinking foundational frameworks &amp; that IKS offers a way to rebuild civil service training programs in alignment with India\'s unique governance needs.</p><p>S P Roy, Jt. Secretary, CBC,highlighted importance of building a mindset around Indian Knowledge System and its role in governance &amp; capacity building.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, led key discussions today. His insights on how colonial constructs continue to shape public service &amp; need to realign governance with India’s cultural &amp; knowledge traditions will be instrumental in reshaping civil service training. Drawing from Panch Pran, he emphasized the need for capturing &amp; institutionalizing success stories to ensure governance becomes a structured, repeatable process that strengthens public institutions.</p><p>Shri Amit Khare (IAS), Advisor to the Hon’ble PM, the Chief Guest, reinforced that Viksit Bharat can only emerge when every state, village &amp; citizen progresses together.He emphasized a ‘saturation approach’ where every individual contributes to the nation’s growth story.He also commended CBC’s role in bringing IKS closer to civil servants, ensuring governance remains deeply connected to India’s knowledge traditions.He also made a poignant remark emphasizing the importance of sustaining their commitment to serving the nation, just as it is when they first embark on their journey in civil service.</p><p>The workshop will explore<br>🔸 Why we must decolonize our institutions<br>🔸 What elements of governance &amp; training need transformation<br>🔸 How to embed IKS into CSTI curricula, functional practices &amp; institutional culture</p><p>The workshop progresses to work towards redefining how civil servants are trained-so that they don’t just manage a system,but actively build one that is rooted in India’s knowledge traditions.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 754, 1386, 'en', 0, '<p>Reimagining Civil Service Training: Decolonizing Mindsets &amp; Institutions</p><p>For decades, India\'s CSTIs have operated within frameworks inherited from colonial rule-shaping administrative structures, policy-making approaches &amp; institutional cultures that often remain disconnected from realities of Bharat’s civilizational ethos. This calls for a necessary shift.</p><p>Today @IIT Delhi, Abhijnana-Workshop on Decolonizing CSTIs brings together thought leaders, policymakers &amp; academics to initiate this transformation. Organized by Capacity Building Commission,Training Division, DoPT, IKS Program @IIT Delhi &amp; INDICA, this workshop is designed to empower civil servants &amp; CSTIs with intellectual tools to draw from IKS-not as an abstract idea, but as a practical approach to governance &amp; administration.</p><p>Nomesh Bolia, Prof., IIT Delhi,remarked that civil services are deeply respected in India not just for their authority but for their role in nation-building,urging participants to explore how key concepts can be materialized into actionable steps for decolonization.</p><p>Prof. KE Seetha Ram,Senior Consulting Specialist, ADB Institute, highlighted that institutional transformation requires rethinking foundational frameworks &amp; that IKS offers a way to rebuild civil service training programs in alignment with India\'s unique governance needs.</p><p>S P Roy, Jt. Secretary, CBC,highlighted importance of building a mindset around Indian Knowledge System and its role in governance &amp; capacity building.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), CBC, led key discussions today. His insights on how colonial constructs continue to shape public service &amp; need to realign governance with India’s cultural &amp; knowledge traditions will be instrumental in reshaping civil service training. Drawing from Panch Pran, he emphasized the need for capturing &amp; institutionalizing success stories to ensure governance becomes a structured, repeatable process that strengthens public institutions.</p><p>Shri Amit Khare (IAS), Advisor to the Hon’ble PM, the Chief Guest, reinforced that Viksit Bharat can only emerge when every state, village &amp; citizen progresses together.He emphasized a ‘saturation approach’ where every individual contributes to the nation’s growth story.He also commended CBC’s role in bringing IKS closer to civil servants, ensuring governance remains deeply connected to India’s knowledge traditions.He also made a poignant remark emphasizing the importance of sustaining their commitment to serving the nation, just as it is when they first embark on their journey in civil service.</p><p>The workshop will explore<br>🔸 Why we must decolonize our institutions<br>🔸 What elements of governance &amp; training need transformation<br>🔸 How to embed IKS into CSTI curricula, functional practices &amp; institutional culture</p><p>The workshop progresses to work towards redefining how civil servants are trained-so that they don’t just manage a system,but actively build one that is rooted in India’s knowledge traditions.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 755, 988, 'en', 0, '<p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The Capacity Building Commission conducted an on-site assessment of the National CPWD Academy, Ghaziabad (Delhi NCR) on 28th and 29th May 2025.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">We are pleased to share that the institute has successfully attained accreditation under the National Standards for Civil Service Training Institutes (#NSCSTI).</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">The assessment process was effectively facilitated by Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), CBC, Shri Prasanta Kumar Mahapatra, Assessor along with Ritika Aggarwal, NABET and Susan Thomas, CBC.</p><p style=\"-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(33, 37, 41);font-family:Poppins, sans-serif;font-size:17.136px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;margin:0px 0px 1rem;orphans:2;padding:0px;text-align:start;text-decoration-color:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;\">Our sincere appreciation goes to Shri Ujjwal Mitra, ADG (T&amp;R) and his dedicated team for their exemplary support in ensuring a seamless and well-coordinated assessment process.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 756, 990, 'en', 0, '<p>While iGOT has come a long way-</p><p>With 8 million users and 1,900 courses-there’s still a massive opportunity ahead. Today, learners engage for just 3 hours a year. Imagine if we could shift that to 25 hours per user today, not as an obligation, but as a habit, a mindset, a way of life, and make doing that “cool”!</p><p>That’s exactly why #CBC and #iGOT brought together some of India’s sharpest minds in marketing, branding, and digital engagement at ‘KarmaConnect: Increasing Learner Engagement’ workshop. They didn’t just discuss ideas; they challenged the way we think about #learning.</p><p>Leaders and changemakers like Suhel Seth (Founder &amp; Managing Partner, Counselage India), Ajay Gahlaut (Independent Creative &amp; Former CCO, Dentsu Creative Service), Sahibjeet Singh Sawhney (Marketing Head, Zomato), Pankaj Bansal (पंकज बंसल) (Board Member, KB, &amp; Co-founder, Peoplestrong), Gayatri Yadav (Group CMO &amp; EVP, Strategic Initiatives, Reliance Industries), Hari Krishnan (Managing Director, Publicis Content &amp; GroupéMarcomm), Biju Dominic (Chief Evangelist, Fractal Analytics), Prashasti Rastogi (Senior Director, Education and Government, Coursera), Sumit Harjani (Managing Director, India, Harvard Business Publishing), Swati Agarwal (Partner, Deloitte), Abhishek Singh (Additional Secretary, Ministry of Electronics and IT, and CEO, India AI Mission) didn’t hold back. They broke down engagement into its raw elements - behavior, motivation, habit-building.</p><p>💡 Why do people binge-watch content but struggle with courses?&nbsp;<br>💡 What makes a message stick?&nbsp;<br>💡 How do we make learning irresistible?</p><p>Discussions went beyond theory. Behavioral nudges, branding that inspires action, and celebrating learners like influencers-all of this was put on the table. 15 pages of brilliant ideas that we now have the responsibility to bring to life.</p><p>Thank you to all our participants for helping us drive #iGOT and #MissionKarmayogi to new heights!</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 757, 994, 'en', 0, '<p>Building towards a future-ready civil service, the Capacity Building Commission is cultivating deep partnerships with states, fostering skilled and responsive governance aligned with India\'s evolving needs.</p><p>Today marks a significant milestone as the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat, and the Government of Arunachal Pradesh signed a tripartite MoU. This agreement signifies a pivotal step in enhancing governance capabilities within the state.</p><p>The signing ceremony was followed by an insightful orientation session led by Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR) at CBC, focusing on #MissionKarmayogi and the Karmayogi Competency Model (#KCM). Ms. Soumi Banerjee, GM – Strategic Alliance and Partnership from Karmayogi Bharat, provided an overview of the functionalities and usage of the iGOT platform.</p><p>Shri Manish Kumar Gupta, Chief Secretary of Arunachal Pradesh, emphasized the critical importance of #CapacityBuilding for government officials and highlighted the need for a transformative mindset among civil servants. He also commended Mission Karmayogi for its structured approach to competency development.</p><p>Shri S P Roy, Joint Secretary, CBC, outlined specific areas for collaboration between the state and #CBC, while Shri Yashpal Garg, Commissioner of the Department of Personnel, underscored the necessity of tailored training programs based on identified needs.</p><p>The orientation session saw active participation from Secretaries, Special Secretaries, Commissioners, Additional Secretaries, Joint Secretaries, Directors, and Heads of departments from across the Government of Arunachal Pradesh.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 758, 997, 'en', 0, '<p>The Department of Social Justice and Empowerment (DoSJE) inaugurated the first batch of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Jan Seva Programme on 5th March 2025—a transformative training initiative launched by the Capacity Building Commission to foster Seva Bhav (spirit of service) among government officials.<br><br>Hon’ble Shri Amit Yadav, Secretary, DoSJE, in his inaugural address, reinforced the essence of public service: “Every action taken by public servants contributes to the nation’s progress. This programme serves as a reminder of why we serve—to bring meaningful change in people’s lives.”<br><br>The training is being led by Ms. Kajal Singh (Director, DoSJE), Shri Puspendra Singh (Deputy Secretary, DoSJE), and supported by Ms. Shipra Singh (Capacity Building Commission).</p><p>Held at Dr. Ambedkar International Centre, New Delhi, the ongoing training program is witnessing active participation from officials as they gain deeper insights into their roles in nation-building, policy formulation, grievance redressal, and citizen-centric governance. This initiative continues to strengthen efforts toward a more efficient, impactful, and service-driven public administration.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 758, 1394, 'en', 0, '<p>The Department of Social Justice and Empowerment (DoSJE) inaugurated the first batch of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Jan Seva Program on 5th March 2025—a transformative training initiative launched by the Capacity Building Commission to foster Seva Bhav (spirit of service) among government officials.<br><br>Hon’ble Shri Amit Yadav, Secretary, DoSJE, in his inaugural address, reinforced the essence of public service: “Every action taken by public servants contributes to the nation’s progress. This program serves as a reminder of why we serve—to bring meaningful change in people’s lives.”<br><br>The training is being led by Ms. Kajal Singh (Director, DoSJE), Shri Puspendra Singh (Deputy Secretary, DoSJE), and supported by Ms. Shipra Singh (Capacity Building Commission).</p><p>Held at Dr. Ambedkar International Centre, New Delhi, the ongoing training program is witnessing active participation from officials as they gain deeper insights into their roles in nation-building, policy formulation, grievance redressal, and citizen-centric governance. This initiative continues to strengthen efforts toward a more efficient, impactful, and service-driven public administration.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 759, 998, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission is pleased to support the dynamic efforts led by Smt. Tilotama Varma, DG, UP Police Training; to train 60,000 newly recruited #police constables in #UttarPradesh. Together with Karmayogi Bharat, CBC will enable curated learning on the #iGOTKarmayogi platform and #JanSeva training - building a new generation of police personnel committed to citizen-first governance.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 760, 999, 'en', 0, '<p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission met with the faculty of Kautilya School of Public Policy, Hyderabad, to discuss ways to enhance the effectiveness of Knowledge Partners (KPs) in civil services #CapacityBuilding.&nbsp;</p><p>The conversation focused on strengthening collaboration between CBC and academic institutions to develop high-quality, competency-based training for civil servants. Dr. Balasubramaniam emphasized the role of KPs in shaping structured learning programs, designing relevant courses on #iGOT, and contributing research-driven insights to improve governance and public service delivery. The discussion also explored opportunities for the institution to contribute to Amrit Gyaan Kosh through case writing and to engage students as interns, fostering a deeper connection between academic research and real-world policymaking.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 761, 1000, 'en', 0, '<p>Tech WARI – Maharashtra Tech Learning Week was inaugurated today at the Mantralaya, Mumbai by Hon’ble Deputy Chief Minister Shri Ajit Pawar and Hon’ble Cabinet Minister for IT &amp; Cultural Affairs (Maharashtra) Shri Ashish Shelar.</p><p>An initiative of the Government of Maharashtra, in partnership with Karmayogi Bharat and the Capacity Building Commission, #TechWARI brings together learners, leaders, and innovators to celebrate digital empowerment in governance.</p><p>As part of the in-person sessions today, Distinguished Fellow, NITI Aayog, Ms Debjani Ghosh spoke on ‘Frontier Tech for Viksit Maharashtra’, and CEO, IndiaAI Mission &amp; DG, NIC, Shri Abhishek Singh addressed the gathering on ‘Artificial Intelligence’.</p><p>Visit the iGOT Karmayogi stall over the next 4 days to explore how Maharashtra’s officials are upskilling for the future!</p><p>With nearly 5 lakh learners enrolled in over 15 lakh courses and more than 10 lakh completions on the iGOT platform, Maharashtra now ranks among the top 3 performing States in the country.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 763, 1002, 'en', 0, '<p>Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman of the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), held insightful discussions with the Secretary, Department of Commerce to explore the ways to enhance learning and development within the department.</p><p>The discussions focused on:<br>Utilizing the iGOT platform<br>Development of courses aligned with the department’s priorities<br>Conducting workshops to equip officials with cutting-edge knowledge<br>Charting a future roadmap</p><p>With a strong commitment to upskilling, these initiatives will play a crucial role in enhancing the capabilities of officials, fostering efficiency, and driving excellence in #trade and #commerce.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 764, 1003, 'en', 0, '<p>Today marks a defining moment as we launch Phase II of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Programme at Indian Institute of Corporate Affairs , IMT Manesar (Lead Trainer Training Workshop). What began by impacting over 11,000 civil servants in Phase I is now set to scale to reach 700,000 government officials across Bharat, guided by a shared purpose and strengthened by Illumine Knowledge Resources, our knowledge partner in this transformative journey.</p><p>This is not a training rollout but a national movement, led by 300 Lead Trainers and 20,000 Karmayogi Coaches, designed to spark deep shifts in mindset, motivation and method across every office, from the grassroots to the highest corridors of administration.</p><p>We are not just building skills but building a citizen-first civil service, powered by purpose and anchored in Seva Bhaav.</p><p>The scale is historic. The intent is urgent. And the outcome will shape how #Bharat is served in the years to come.</p><p>Ms. Ankita Singh, Director, Capacity Building Commission, set the tone for the workshop with her opening remarks, welcoming participants and urging them to engage wholeheartedly in this transformative national mission.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 765, 1004, 'en', 0, '<p>On Feb 10, 2025, the National Standards for Civil Service Training Institutes (NSCSTI)Workshop was conducted as part of the consultative process to update the #NSCSTI accreditation framework. The workshop aimed to gather comprehensive feedback from all stakeholders, including training institutes, onsite assessors, &amp; desktop assessors, to refine the framework’s 8 pillars. A total of 40 training institutes participated, including 6 Administrative Training Institutes(ATIs) &amp; 15 Central Civil Service Training Institutes(CTIs).</p><p>The event was chaired by Adil Zainulbhai, Chairman, CBC who emphasized importance of this reiterative process in developing a framework that is both accessible for training institutes &amp; aspirational in driving continuous improvement.</p><p>Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission, spoke to the institutes about the various initiatives under the Commission aimed @ strengthening &amp; facilitating the capacity building of civil service training institutes across the country.</p><p>To facilitate in-depth discussions, institutes were divided into 3 breakout groups, each focusing on specific pillars of framework.</p><p>Group 1 was led by Sh. Adil Zainulbhai, Group 2 by Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi (CEO, Karmayogi Bharat), &amp; Group 3 by Dr. Alka Mittal (Member Admin, CBC). Participants deliberated on which aspects of the framework should be retained &amp; proposed modifications to enhance its effectiveness.Each group then presented their insights to larger gathering, exchanging notes &amp; identifying key problem areas.</p><p>The valuable feedback gathered from workshop will be incorporated into revised framework,which is set to be rolled out in May 2025,ensuring it remains both relevant &amp; progressive for training institutes across the country.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 766, 1005, 'en', 0, '<p>On January 31 and February 1, 2025, the Office Of The Controller General Of Patents, Designs And Trade Marks (CGPDTM), organized simultaneous sessions in #Nagpur and #Hyderabad for newly appointed officials, focusing on #MissionKarmayogi. S P Roy, Joint Secretary, Capacity Building Commission, delivered an insightful lecture on the mission\'s significance and its pivotal role in transforming civil services.</p><p>Mission Karmayogi, officially known as the National Programme for Civil Services Capacity Building (NPCSCB), was approved by the Government of India on September 2, 2020. It aims to transition civil services from a \'rule-based\' to a \'role-based\' system, emphasizing competency development and fostering a culture of #ContinuousLearning among government officials.</p><p>The sessions underscored the mission\'s objective to equip civil servants with the necessary skills and knowledge to meet the evolving challenges of governance. By leveraging #digitallearning platforms and structured training modules, Mission Karmayogi aspires to create a future-ready civil service dedicated to serving the nation effectively.</p><p>The participation of the newly appointed CGPDTM officials in these sessions marks a significant step towards enhancing their capabilities and aligning them with the mission\'s vision. Such initiatives are crucial in building a proficient and responsive civil service committed to the nation\'s progress.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 767, 1008, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and Karmayogi Bharat, in collaboration with the India AI Mission organised an event on “AI for Capacity Building: Transforming Governance”, in New Delhi.</p><p>At the inaugural session, MoS Dr Jitendra Singh said that Mission Karmayogi and iGOT platform are built on Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s vision to shift governance from rule-based to role-based functioning. The Minister said that a hybrid model combining Artificial Intelligence with human intelligence will be critical to building a future-ready, responsive and effective public administration. He further mentioned that the iGOT platform has adopted AI-driven tools such as AI Saarthi, AI Tutor and AI-based Capacity Building Plans. These tools, he said, are enabling personalised learning pathways, faster planning and improved delivery across ministries and departments.</p><p>The event was attended by senior dignitaries including Smt. Rachna Shah, Secretary, Department of Personnel &amp; Training; Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission; and Shri Subramanian Ramadorai, Chairperson, Karmayogi Bharat, along with senior officers from the Centre and States, representatives from academia, industry, training institutions and capacity building units across ministries.</p><p>Smt. Rachna Shah, Secretary, DoPT, emphasised that AI can significantly strengthen transparent, responsive and citizen-centric governance by improving relevance, timeliness and personalisation in capacity building, while underscoring the importance of ethical safeguards and inclusive access.</p><p>Smt. Chhavi Bhardwaj, CEO, KB, highlighted that iGOT has emerged as the foundational digital infrastructure for public sector capacity building, with over 1.5 crore learners and more than 6.7 crore course completions.</p><p>A key highlight of the event was the launch of “Karmayogi Classroom”, a new AI-enabled feature on the iGOT Karmayogi platform designed to enhance contextual, interactive and personalised learning for civil servants.</p><p>The programme also featured live demonstrations and thought leadership sessions by leading AI ecosystem partners, showcasing AI tutors, AI-driven capacity building plans, competency mapping tools and indigenous AI solutions tailored for public administration.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2212462&amp;reg=3&amp;lang=1\" target=\"_blank\">Press Release</a></p>', '', 'full_html'),
