('event', 0, 768, 1009, 'en', 0, '<p>Honored to have Dr. Jitendra Singh, Union Minister of State for Personnel, Public Grievances, and Pensions, inaugurate the Advanced Case Writing and Teaching Workshop and officially launch the Amrit Gyaan Kosh Portal at the Sushma Swaraj Institute of Foreign Service (SSIFS), New Delhi today.</p><p>This initiative by the Capacity Building Commission in collaboration with Asian Development Bank Institute (ADBI) and the Stanford Leadership Academy for Development (LAD) marks the beginning of a transformative journey to institutionalize case-based learning in governance.&nbsp;</p><p>The Amrit Gyaan Kosh Portal is now live, offering complete access to Atmanirbhar case studies and supporting materials on iGOT. It is more than a repository-it’s a national knowledge treasure designed to:</p><p>?Empower faculty and practitioners to create contextual, impactful governance models.<br>?Facilitate experiential learning by capturing real-world challenges and solutions.<br>?Foster collaboration and innovation across academies and sectors.</p><p>This initiative is aligned with the vision of making “learning just a click away,” ensuring accessible, high-quality, indigenous resources for governance professionals and academies.</p><p>Together, let’s embark on this transformative journey to empower public service delivery and inspire future generations!</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 768, 1051, 'en', 0, '<p>Honored to have Dr. Jitendra Singh, Union Minister of State for Personnel, Public Grievances, and Pensions, inaugurate the Advanced Case Writing and Teaching Workshop and officially launch the Amrit Gyaan Kosh Portal at the Sushma Swaraj Institute of Foreign Service (SSIFS), New Delhi today.</p><p>This initiative by the Capacity Building Commission in collaboration with Asian Development Bank Institute (ADBI) and the Stanford Leadership Academy for Development (LAD) marks the beginning of a transformative journey to institutionalize case-based learning in governance.&nbsp;</p><p>The Amrit Gyaan Kosh Portal is now live, offering complete access to Atmanirbhar case studies and supporting materials on iGOT. It is more than a repository-it’s a national knowledge treasure designed to:</p><p>?Empower faculty and practitioners to create contextual, impactful governance models.<br>?Facilitate experiential learning by capturing real-world challenges and solutions.<br>?Foster collaboration and innovation across academies and sectors.</p><p>This initiative is aligned with the vision of making “learning just a click away,” ensuring accessible, high-quality, indigenous resources for governance professionals and academies.</p><p>Together, let’s embark on this transformative journey to empower public service delivery and inspire future generations!</p>', '', 'basic_html');
INSERT INTO `node_revision__field_event_description` (`bundle`, `deleted`, `entity_id`, `revision_id`, `langcode`, `delta`, `field_event_description_value`, `field_event_description_summary`, `field_event_description_format`) VALUES
('event', 0, 769, 1013, 'en', 0, '<p>Chairman (NHAI) and Member (Admin) &nbsp;Capacity Building Commission held a pivotal meeting to strengthen NHAI\'s workforce for &nbsp;dealing with the complexities of modern infrastructure development. Key note address &nbsp;was given by Member CBC) emphasizing the need for &nbsp;technical leadership, and problem-solving skills; and stressing on the importance of continuous learning and creating a culture of excellence . The Chairman stressed on the NHAI team to focus on behavioral, domain and functional competencies . S P Roy, Joint secretary (CBC) &nbsp;laid down the steps involved in the creation of the capacity building plan , and &nbsp;assured full support &nbsp;of CBC and PwC in developing the Capacity Building Program for NHAI. The Kick off meeting ended with &nbsp;Member (Admin) CBC highlighting the scope for continuous improvement, hoping that NHAI, as an apex institution, will set a benchmark for others in the infrastructure sector.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 769, 1052, 'en', 0, '<p>Chairman (NHAI) and Member (Admin) &nbsp;Capacity Building Commission held a pivotal meeting to strengthen NHAI\'s workforce for &nbsp;dealing with the complexities of modern infrastructure development. Key note address &nbsp;was given by Member CBC) emphasizing the need for &nbsp;technical leadership, and problem-solving skills; and stressing on the importance of continuous learning and creating a culture of excellence . The Chairman stressed on the NHAI team to focus on behavioral, domain and functional competencies . S P Roy, Joint secretary (CBC) &nbsp;laid down the steps involved in the creation of the capacity building plan , and &nbsp;assured full support &nbsp;of CBC and PwC in developing the Capacity Building Program for NHAI. The Kick off meeting ended with &nbsp;Member (Admin) CBC highlighting the scope for continuous improvement, hoping that NHAI, as an apex institution, will set a benchmark for others in the infrastructure sector.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 770, 1016, 'en', 0, '<p>Constitution Day is celebrated in our country on 26th November every year to commemorate the adoption of the Constitution of India. On 26th November 1949, the Constituent Assembly of India adopted the Constitution of India, which came into effect from 26th January 1950.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 770, 1053, 'en', 0, '<p>Constitution Day is celebrated in our country on 26th November every year to commemorate the adoption of the Constitution of India. On 26th November 1949, the Constituent Assembly of India adopted the Constitution of India, which came into effect from 26th January 1950.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 771, 1017, 'en', 0, '<p>Mission Karmayogi team led by Dr Alka Mittal, Member, Capacity Building Commission called on the Hon\'ble Governor of Himachal Pradesh Shri Shiv Pratap Shukla on 21st November, 2024, in Raj Bhawan, Shimla.</p><p>Team consisting of officials from CBC and Karmayogi Bharat discussed various initiatives and interventions related to capacity building of the officials of Himachal Pradesh.</p><p><br>The team had brief interaction with the Chief Secretary, Shri Prabodh Saxena and Secretary, Urban Development, Shri Devesh Kumar, to discuss the way forward for Capacity Building in the State of Himachal Pradesh.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 772, 1018, 'en', 0, '<p>A tripartite MoU was signed between the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), Karmayogi Bharat, and the Government &nbsp;Of Assam , India, marking an important step in the mission to strengthen governance capabilities. The signing ceremony was attended by the Chief Secretary of Assam, Dr. Ravi Kota, IAS ; Dr. R Balasubramaniam, Member HR, CBC; Dr. Alka Mittal, Member Admin, CBC; Smt. V. Lalithalakshmi, Secretary, CBC &amp; CEO of Karmayogi Bharat, and Shri S P Roy, Secretary, CBC.</p><p>Following the signing, a workshop outlined key achievements of #MissionKarmayogi over the past three years, including CBC and Karmayogi Bharat’s work with Central and State Governments. Discussions covered promising areas of collaboration, such as:</p><p>* CBC’s Viksit Panchayat Initiative<br>* Interventions with Urban Local Bodies<br>* Development of a Centre of Excellence for Urban Planning and Development for Assam<br>* District-Level Leadership Program</p><p>Principal Secretaries and department heads from Assam’s Secretariat participated in the workshop. Chief Secretary Dr. Ravi Kota Ji expressed the state’s commitment to effective governance through #CapacityBuilding and ongoing collaboration with #CBC and #KarmayogiBharat.</p><p>Together, CBC, Karmayogi Bharat, and the Government of Assam are excited to enhance the capacity in public administration, paving the way for a brighter and more empowered future, and contributing to #ViksitBharat.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 773, 1019, 'en', 0, '<p>We are delighted to announce the #KarmayogiSaptah - National Learning Week (#NLW) will be launched by our Hon’ble Prime Minister, Shri Narendra Modi, at 10 am.</p><p>The #NLW, from 19th-25th October, is aimed to inspire civil servants to embrace a culture of continuous learning, crucial for driving India towards #ViksitBharat.</p><p>We invite you to join us: https://lnkd.in/gzN-gf28</p><p>Also, as part of your commitment to professional excellence, we encourage all civil servants to dedicate at least 4 hours to completing iGOT courses, this week. iGOT certificates and Karma Points will be awarded to recognize your efforts.</p><p>Let’s come together to make the Karmayogi Saptah a grand success!</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 773, 1054, 'en', 0, '<p>We are delighted to announce the #KarmayogiSaptah - National Learning Week (#NLW) will be launched by our Hon’ble Prime Minister, Shri Narendra Modi, at 10 am.</p><p>The #NLW, from 19th-25th October, is aimed to inspire civil servants to embrace a culture of continuous learning, crucial for driving India towards #ViksitBharat.</p><p>We invite you to join us: https://lnkd.in/gzN-gf28</p><p>Also, as part of your commitment to professional excellence, we encourage all civil servants to dedicate at least 4 hours to completing iGOT courses, this week. iGOT certificates and Karma Points will be awarded to recognize your efforts.</p><p>Let’s come together to make the Karmayogi Saptah a grand success!</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 774, 1021, 'en', 0, '<p>The Department Of Personnel &amp; Training hosted the \"Workshop on Mission Karmayogi for Capacity Building Units of Ministries/Departments\" on October 3, 2024, in New Delhi. The workshop underscored the evolving role of Ministries and Departments in capacity building, reinforcing CBC’s efforts to equip civil servants with the competencies needed to achieve Viksit Bharat.</p><p>The Capacity Building Commission (CBC) presented key highlights of the upcoming National Learning Week, aimed at fostering SevaBhaav and aligning civil servants with the vision of ViksitBharat through continuous learning.</p><p>CBC also shared updates on the Karmayogi Seva Bhaav program, a large-scale behavioral intervention set to engage 700,000 Central Government employees. This initiative, designed to develop 20,000 Karmayogi Coaches, seeks to instill a spirit of public service, enhancing the delivery of citizen-centric governance. Mission Karmayogi is in full momentum as National Learning Week approaches.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 775, 1022, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission met Mr. Koosiram Conhye, Secretary for Public Service (Mauritius), to discuss proposed capacity-building programs by CBC and iGOT. The 3- member delegation showed keen interest in the large-scale interventions undertaken by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC), along with the iGOT online platform, which provides competency-based courses for civil servants. They were excited to try out some courses themselves. The collaboration aims to strengthen international partnerships and enhance global best practices in civil service governance.</p><p>They were very complimentary of the speed and scale of the efforts in India on capacity building.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 776, 1023, 'en', 0, '<p>Pledge taking ceremony on Swachh Bharat Campaign at CBC</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 777, 1024, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission team, led by Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), along with Ms V. Lalithalakshmi, Secretary,Ms &nbsp; Anuradha Mukharjee (Retd IRS Official and QIP Mentor) and Ms Navneet Kaur, Director, conducted onsite meetings at the Institute of Secretariat Training and Management (ISTM), Delhi, focusing on the Quality Improvement Plan (QIP) based on the NSCSTI framework.&nbsp;</p><p>This initiative is driving significant progress in enhancing training quality. The institute remains committed to contributing to the nation’s capacity-building efforts.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 777, 1241, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission team, led by Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), along with Ms V. Lalithalakshmi, Secretary,Ms &nbsp; Anuradha Mukharjee (Retd IRS Official and QIP Mentor) and Ms Navneet Kaur, Director, conducted onsite meetings at the Institute of Secretariat Training and Management (ISTM), Delhi, focusing on the Quality Improvement Plan (QIP) based on the NSCSTI framework.&nbsp;</p><p>This initiative is driving significant progress in enhancing training quality. The institute remains committed to contributing to the nation’s capacity-building efforts.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 777, 1251, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission team, led by Dr. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), along with Ms V. Lalithalakshmi, Secretary,Ms &nbsp; Anuradha Mukharjee (Retd IRS Official and QIP Mentor) and Ms Navneet Kaur, Director, conducted onsite meetings at the Institute of Secretariat Training and Management (ISTM), Delhi, focusing on the Quality Improvement Plan (QIP) based on the NSCSTI framework.&nbsp;</p><p>This initiative is driving significant progress in enhancing training quality. The institute remains committed to contributing to the nation’s capacity-building efforts.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 778, 1025, 'en', 0, '<p>Signing of MoU with Piramal Foundation for Education Leadership<br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 779, 1026, 'en', 0, '<p>CBC was delighted to welcome the team of National Informatics Centre, MeitY (NIC) lead by DG NIC &amp; CEO Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) Sh Amit Agrawal.</p><p>The brainstorming session focused around Capacity Building, HR Transformation, Knowledge Management, Change management &amp; Technology Integration. &nbsp;NIC is the key enabler of technology driven solutions for Central and State Governments. CBC is glad to support NIC in this journey.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 780, 1027, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission today launched the “National Karmayogi Seva Bhaav&nbsp;program” with participation from more than 15 Ministries/Departments of the Government of India.&nbsp;</p><p>Phase 1 of this program will build the capacity of officers of the entire Secretariat of the Government of India in the next 3 months covering all 93 Ministries and Departments.&nbsp;</p><p>The impact of governance should be felt by the citizens of the last mile. With the focus on changing mindsets, this program will ensure that all officers go through 1 day of training on building karmayogi competencies and mindsets and operating like a karmayogi.&nbsp;</p><p>Supported by the knowledge partner, the trainers will be created from the nominated DSs/Directors of the MDO who will bring the right context and experience to the training.</p><p>CBC aims to ensure that the National Karmayogi Seva Bhaav program will catalyse and rekindle the spirit of Janbhagidari to help India achieve the goal of Viksit Bharat, as envisioned by the Hon\'ble Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 781, 1028, 'en', 0, '<p>We just ended the communication workshop for CPSE finance executives which was attended by 30 executives from 15 CPSEs, 15 analysts and investors , DIPAM officers. Each executive got a chance to get one on one coaching on their analyst presentation and had to do the presentation 3 times in front of a panel of communications coaches, analysts, investors, &amp; &nbsp;dipam officers.</p><p>The 2 days were intense but the workshop went off very well. Kudos to the cbc team , E&amp;Y, Initium and DIPAM for making this happen.</p><p>Every participant thought it was &nbsp;a very good training workshop.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 782, 1030, 'en', 0, '<p>Secretary (CBC) addressed the group of civil servants from Gamibia, at National Centre for Good Governance , who are in India as part of their mid career &nbsp;training programme. The &nbsp;group was informed about the achievements under &nbsp;Mission Karmayogi focussing on building Competencies to enable the shift &nbsp;from Rule to Role based performance, citizen centric and groomed to be tech enabled and future ready.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 782, 1384, 'en', 0, '<p>Secretary (CBC) addressed the group of civil servants from Gamibia, at National Centre for Good Governance , who are in India as part of their mid career &nbsp;training program. The &nbsp;group was informed about the achievements under &nbsp;Mission Karmayogi focussing on building Competencies to enable the shift &nbsp;from Rule to Role based performance, citizen centric and groomed to be tech enabled and future ready.</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 783, 1031, 'en', 0, '<p>“गुरु ब्रह्मा गुरु विष्णु, गुरु देवो महेश्वरा, गुरु साक्षात परब्रह्म, तस्मै श्री गुरुवे नमः”</p><p>At the core of Mission Karmayogi is continuous learning and competency-driven capacity building. It envisions a future-ready civil service rooted in Indian ethos, with a global perspective. Key teachers in the civil service capacity building ecosystem in India, are our Civil Service Training Institutions (CSTIs), and the IGOT Karmayogi platform, shouldering the responsibility of teaching and training ~31 lakh Karmayogis.</p><p>On this Teachers\' Day, the Commission extends its heartfelt thanks and celebrates the dedicated faculty of all 800+ CSTIs who play a pivotal role in shaping the future of our nation\'s governance. Your commitment to excellence and passion for imparting knowledge and empowering our civil servants with the skills and insights necessary for effective public service is commendable.</p><p>As we reflect on these invaluable contributions, we also acknowledge the pivotal role of the IGOT Karmayogi platform in facilitating anytime-anywhere learning, ensuring that every civil servant has access to essential resources and guidance for their professional development. The platform boasts over 4.3 million registered civil servants, 1100+ digital courses, and 11 million courses completed. The teachings on IGOT not only impart knowledge but also instill the values that make a true public servant.</p><p>Together, these efforts cultivate a culture of lifelong learning and excellence in public administration. The contributions of CSTIs and the IGOT platform have been instrumental in advancing the competency-driven capacity-building goals of Mission Karmayogi. Taking inspiration from Dr. Radhakrishnan’s teachings , the end of all education should be the betterment of the individual and society. This spirit embodies the mission of shaping future leaders who will work towards citizen-centric, effective, and efficient public service delivery.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 784, 1032, 'en', 0, '<p>As part of working with States, the Capacity Building Commission team had discussions with officials from the State of Odisha, to spearhead Mission Karmayogi in the state and onboard officials for the Capacity Building process at the State and Local levels.&nbsp;</p><p>The meeting was attended by the Chief Secretary of Odisha, Shri Manoj Ahuja, IAS, Shri Surendra Kumar, IAS Additional Chief Secretary, Smt. Anu Garg, IAS, Development Commissioner, G Mathi Vathanan, IAS, DG Gopabandhu Academy of Administration, Shri Manish Agarwal, IAS Additional DG and other senior officials.&nbsp;</p><p>Very fruitful discussions took place leading to concrete action plans.&nbsp;</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 784, 1033, 'en', 0, '<p>As part of working with States, the Capacity Building Commission team had discussions with officials from the State of Odisha, to spearhead Mission Karmayogi in the state and onboard officials for the Capacity Building process at the State and Local levels.&nbsp;</p><p>The meeting was attended by the Chief Secretary of Odisha, Shri Manoj Ahuja, IAS, Shri Surendra Kumar, IAS Additional Chief Secretary, Smt. Anu Garg, IAS, Development Commissioner, G Mathi Vathanan, IAS, DG Gopabandhu Academy of Administration, Shri Manish Agarwal, IAS Additional DG and other senior officials.&nbsp;</p><p>Very fruitful discussions took place leading to concrete action plans.&nbsp;</p><p><br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 785, 1034, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission, along with Karmayogi Bharat, has been enhancing capacity building for central civil servants for the last two years. Recently, CBC met with Andhra Pradesh CM Nara Chandrababu Naidu and his team in Amravati to extend the benefits of capacity building to all 4.5 lakh civil servants across all levels.</p><p>The CM\'s vision for Andhra Pradesh necessitates every civil servant’s contribution to the state\'s GDP and citizens’ ease of living.&nbsp;</p><p>R Balasubramaniam, Rakesh Verma, and S P Roy led the discussions with Andhra Pradesh CM Chandrababu Naidu and his team in Amravati, aiming to establish a model for capacity building that could benefit all states. Capacity Building Commission and Karmayogi Bharat are committed to supporting Andhra in this mission and pioneering the measurement of the impact of these efforts alongside capacity building.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 786, 1035, 'en', 0, '<p>The Capacity Building Commission successfully organized the CSTI Convention 2024 at Vigyan Bhawan on 12th August 2024, bringing together all Civil Service Training Institutions (CSTIs) accredited under the National Standards for Civil Service Training Institutions (NSCSTI).</p><p>At this convention, 144 accredited CSTIs were awarded certificates in the presence of the Chief Guest, Hon’ble MoS Dr. Jitendra Singh, recognizing their collective commitment to excellence in civil service capacity building. Addressing the gathering, Hon’ble MoS remarked, “We have accredited over 140 training institutes, and each accreditation represents a step towards a more competent, efficient, and responsive civil service.” The Commission extends its heartfelt congratulations to all accredited CSTIs and our esteemed partners.</p><p>During the convention, Hon. MoS also launched three significant initiatives: the Faculty Development Program, Amrit Gyaan Kosh, and Quality Improvement Program—all dedicated to fostering continuous learning and competency-driven capacity building among CSTIs.</p><p>Digimanthan 2.0 resulted in institutions committing to digitalising 300+ courses for the IGOT Karmayogi platform.&nbsp;</p><p>The Commission expresses its deep gratitude to Hon. MoS PP Dr. Jitendra Singh, all participants, and our distinguished speakers for making this event a resounding success.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 787, 1036, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and Centre for Effective Governance of Indian States signed an MoU for collaboration on various capacity-building initiatives for the various departments of the Government of India.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 788, 1037, 'en', 0, '<p>The International Day of Yoga has been celebrated across the world annually on June 21 since 2015. This year the theme for International Day of Yoga is “Yoga for Self and Society.” Yoga, a transformative practice, represents the harmony of mind and body, the balance between thought and action, and the unity of restraint and fulfillment. It integrates the body, mind, spirit, and soul, offering a holistic approach to health and well-being that brings peace to our hectic lives. Its power to transform is what we celebrate on this special day.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 789, 1038, 'en', 0, '<p>Today, CBC leadership called on Shri Jitendra Singh, Union MoS(Ind. Charge)Science &amp; Technology; Earth Sciences; MoS PMO, PP/ DoPT, Atomic Energy, Space.&nbsp;</p><p>They also presented a draft copy of the #KarmayogiCompetencyModel (KCM), which is the first indigenous Public HR Management Model developed in the country and will be of global standards at par with other competency models across the world.&nbsp;</p><p>It\'s always a pleasure to get inspiration for #MissionKarmayogi from him.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 790, 1039, 'en', 0, '<p>In another milestone, CBC hosted the induction session for 11 Program Coordinators (Karmayogi Sarthis) in New Delhi on June 11, 2024. Piramal Foundation members, especially CEO Aditya Natraj and Director Saurabh Johri, along with representatives from various Ministries, Departments, and Organizations (MDOs), graced the occasion.</p><p>CBC leadership, including Chairman Mr. Adil Zainulbhai, members - Dr. Alka Mittal, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, and secretary Mr. S P Roy were delighted to interact with the Karmayogi Sarthis along with the MDO’s to bring them up to speed on various activities of CBC and expectation of the MDO’s.</p><p>These young, dynamic, and dedicated Program Coordinators will play a pivotal role in enhancing #capacitybuilding and fostering #collaboration within various MDOs as part of #MissionKarmayogi. They will assist the Capacity Building Unit (CBU) team in implementing the Annual Capacity Plan, enforcing Karmayogi Guidelines, and supporting the Central Civil Service Training Institutions in onboarding the Accreditation framework.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 790, 1055, 'en', 0, '<p>In another milestone, CBC hosted the induction session for 11 Program Coordinators (Karmayogi Sarthis) in New Delhi on June 11, 2024. Piramal Foundation members, especially CEO Aditya Natraj and Director Saurabh Johri, along with representatives from various Ministries, Departments, and Organizations (MDOs), graced the occasion.</p><p>CBC leadership, including Chairman Mr. Adil Zainulbhai, members - Dr. Alka Mittal, Dr. R Balasubramaniam, and secretary Mr. S P Roy were delighted to interact with the Karmayogi Sarthis along with the MDO’s to bring them up to speed on various activities of CBC and expectation of the MDO’s.</p><p>These young, dynamic, and dedicated Program Coordinators will play a pivotal role in enhancing #capacitybuilding and fostering #collaboration within various MDOs as part of #MissionKarmayogi. They will assist the Capacity Building Unit (CBU) team in implementing the Annual Capacity Plan, enforcing Karmayogi Guidelines, and supporting the Central Civil Service Training Institutions in onboarding the Accreditation framework.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 795, 1060, 'en', 0, '<p>Mr. Hemang Jani, Secretary, Capacity Building Commission (CBC), addressed the AMP Participants today at the Bella Vista Campus of Administrative Staff College of India (ASCI) and had a discussion withSri Padmanabhaiah Kantipudi, Chairman-ASCI, Dr.Nirmalya Bagchi, DG(I/c), Dr. Valli Manickam, Dean, Bose S.K &amp; Dr O P Singh, Registrar (I/c)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'full_html'),
('event', 0, 799, 1064, 'en', 0, '<p>In partnership with Korn Ferry, the SHRMExecutiveNetwork held a Knowledge and Networking Breakfast with SHRM India to welcome 13 new members as well as discuss the challenges and trends in workforce management. Sharing their insights and connecting with attendees were Secretary of Capacity Building Commission, Hemang Jani, Country Manager - India UKG, Sumeet Doshi, and Director of Tata Management Training Center (TMTC) and Senior Vice President Group HR at Tata Group, Anand Shankar</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 817, 1085, 'en', 0, '<p>Celebrating 75 Years of Independence</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 817, 1086, 'en', 0, '<p>Celebrating 75 Years of Independence</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 847, 1145, 'en', 0, '<p>Joint Secretary, Shri Jagdeep Gupta, IPoS (2004) joins Capacity Building Commission (CBC) today.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 847, 1218, 'en', 0, '<p>Joint Secretary, Shri Jagdeep Gupta, IPoS (2004) joins Capacity Building Commission (CBC) today.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 847, 1240, 'en', 0, '<p>Joint Secretary, Shri Jagdeep Gupta, IPoS (2004) joins Capacity Building Commission (CBC) today.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 855, 1153, 'en', 0, '<p>Joint Secretary, Shri Jagdeep Gupta, IPoS (2004) joins Capacity Building Commission (CBC) today.&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 855, 1222, 'en', 0, '<p>Joint Secretary, Shri Jagdeep Gupta, IPoS (2004) joins Capacity Building Commission (CBC).&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 855, 1252, 'en', 0, '<p>Joint Secretary, Shri Jagdeep Gupta, IPoS (2004) joins Capacity Building Commission (CBC).&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 895, 1477, 'en', 0, '<p>AI-Enabled Capacity Building Plans:\r\n\r\nCapacity Building Commission, in coordination with Mahatma Gandhi State Institute of Public Administration (MGSIPA), conducted the AI-enabled Capacity Building Plan (CBP) Workshop (15–16 January 2026) under Mission Karmayogi.\r\n\r\nOver two days, departments moved from planning to implementation:\r\n•	48 departments participated\r\n•	10 departments developed CBPs\r\n•	5 departments successfully made their CBPs live on the iGOT Karmayogi platform\r\n•	33 departments were oriented to complete their CBPs at the earliest \r\n\r\nThe sessions were guided by senior leadership whose insights set both direction and momentum:\r\n\r\nSmt. Chandralekha Mukherjee highlighted the transformative potential of Mission Karmayogi in shifting civil services from a rule-based to a role-based approach. She emphasized that clearly defined roles, supported by targeted competency development, would enable officials to become more effective, productive, and responsive in addressing citizens’ needs.\r\n\r\nMr. Gulshan, Executive Director, MGSIPA shared the simplicity and usability of the AI-enabled CBP tool, noting that it not only supports structured training planning but also helps departments strategically utilize their existing resources for competency development.\r\n\r\nCol. Dalbir Singh, Training Director, MGSIPA, provided sustained operational leadership, reinforcing the importance of systematic and executable training plans.\r\n\r\nThe workshop was facilitated by Ms. Zainab Naaz and Ms. Akanksha Mahapatro, Programme Coordinators, who led hands-on demonstrations and ensured seamless support for departments transitioning their CBPs to the iGOT platform.\r\n\r\nThis milestone marks a significant step in institutionalising technology-enabled, role-specific, and future-ready capacity building at the state level strengthening the foundations of Mission Karmayogi through action, ownership, and implementation.\r\n<br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 896, 1478, 'en', 0, '<p>Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, <a href=\"https://in.linkedin.com/company/capacity-building-commission?trk=public_post-text\"><strong>Capacity Building Commission</strong></a> urged graduates to align their professional efforts with the National Vision of \"Viksit Bharat\" and highlighted the disruptive yet transformative power of Artificial Intelligence. She emphasized that AI must be managed with a focus on ethics, equity, and inclusion to prevent widening the digital divide.\r\n\r\nShe was addressing the Convocation Ceremony at <a href=\"https://in.linkedin.com/company/administrative-staff-college-of-india-asci?trk=public_post-text\"><strong>Administrative Staff College of India (ASCI)</strong></a>, Hyderabad.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 897, 1479, 'en', 0, '<p>Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson - Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and Smt. Santhi Kumari, Vice Chairperson &amp; Director General - Dr. Marri Channa Reddy Human Resource Development Institute of Telangana (MCRHRDIT) held an interaction focusing on Capacity Building of State at Hyderabad today.\r\n\r\nDuring the deliberations, the ATI highlighted multiple areas reflecting innovative progress, wherein domain expertise has been identified for curating digital content and converting the same into structured digital courses.\r\n\r\nChairperson, CBC underscored the critical importance of formulation and implementation of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) by all State Departments, reiterating the emphasis laid during the meeting of Chief Secretaries that every State Department must have a CBP in place.\r\n\r\nThe Chairperson, CBC further highlighted the need for integration of training data with HRMS systems, enabling effective personalisation of learning pathways for officials. She urged the ATI to supplement the competency gaps identified through CBPs by aligning and delivering appropriate training programmes, including blended learning, thereby facilitating a transition from a supply-driven to a demand-driven training ecosystem.\r\n\r\nSmt. S Radha Chauhan also assured continued guidance and support to the ATI in strengthening its capabilities in emerging technology domains, as part of ongoing capacity-building efforts.\r\n\r\nThe interaction concluded with a campus tour, during which the Chairperson, CBC was apprised of the Institute’s infrastructure, including training halls, labs, sports facilities, and the Women SHG-run canteen operating within the campus.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 897, 1480, 'en', 0, '<p>Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson - Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and Smt. Santhi Kumari, Vice Chairperson &amp; Director General - Dr. Marri Channa Reddy Human Resource Development Institute of Telangana (MCRHRDIT) held an interaction focusing on Capacity Building of State at Hyderabad today.\r\n\r\nDuring the deliberations, the ATI highlighted multiple areas reflecting innovative progress, wherein domain expertise has been identified for curating digital content and converting the same into structured digital courses.\r\n\r\nChairperson, CBC underscored the critical importance of formulation and implementation of Capacity Building Plans (CBPs) by all State Departments, reiterating the emphasis laid during the meeting of Chief Secretaries that every State Department must have a CBP in place.\r\n\r\nThe Chairperson, CBC further highlighted the need for integration of training data with HRMS systems, enabling effective personalisation of learning pathways for officials. She urged the ATI to supplement the competency gaps identified through CBPs by aligning and delivering appropriate training programmes, including blended learning, thereby facilitating a transition from a supply-driven to a demand-driven training ecosystem.\r\n\r\nSmt. S Radha Chauhan also assured continued guidance and support to the ATI in strengthening its capabilities in emerging technology domains, as part of ongoing capacity-building efforts.\r\n\r\nThe interaction concluded with a campus tour, during which the Chairperson, CBC was apprised of the Institute’s infrastructure, including training halls, labs, sports facilities, and the Women SHG-run canteen operating within the campus.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 917, 1609, 'en', 0, '<p>The Inaugural Session of the second batch of DAKSH (Development of Aspiration, Knowledge, Succession and Harmony), a flagship leadership development programme for senior executives of Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs), was held at the SCOPE Convention Centre, New Delhi. The programme is jointly organised by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and the Standing Conference of Public Enterprises (SCOPE) under Mission Karmayogi.<br><br>The event was attended by senior leadership from the Government of India and the public sector, including Dr. P. K. Mishra, Principal Secretary to the Prime Minister; Shri K. Moses Chalai, Secretary, Department of Public Enterprises; Smt. Rachna Shah, Secretary, Department of Personnel and Training; Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission; Shri K. P. Mahadevaswamy, Chairman, SCOPE; Shri Atul Sobti, Director General, SCOPE; and Smt. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), Capacity Building Commission.<br><br>Welcoming participants, Shri Atul Sobti said DAKSH will help leaders reflect, prepare and transform themselves, while enabling leadership emergence, strategic development and international exposure.<br><br>Setting the context, Smt. Alka Mittal described DAKSH as a 12-month leadership programme integrating digital learning, classroom engagement, executive coaching, action learning and international exposure. She noted that 73 senior CPSE officials were trained in the first batch &amp; 72 participants from diverse sectors form the second. Highlighting Mission Karmayogi initiatives such as iGOT onboarding, Karmayogi Saptah, the Competency Model, accreditation of institutions and Amrit Gyaan Kosh, she emphasised leadership development, competency-based growth and technology-enabled learning for CPSE reforms.<br><br>Delivering the address, Dr. P. K. Mishra highlighted the evolving role of CPSEs and their foundational contribution to India’s industrial and infrastructure base. He said globalisation and reforms have shifted focus to competitiveness, efficiency and innovation, requiring greater agility while serving national priorities and competing globally. Referring to the Public Sector Enterprise Policy of 2021, he noted that despite an expanding role for private enterprises, CPSEs remain vital in strategic sectors such as energy, defence, infrastructure and finance, and in balancing markets involving public goods and national security. He stressed innovation, continuous learning and strategic thinking through initiatives like DAKSH.<br><br>Earlier, Shri K. Moses Chalai highlighted the economic contribution of CPSEs to GDP &amp; the Central Exchequer, stressing the need for future-ready leadership and describing DAKSH as timely.&nbsp;<br><br>Shri Jagdeep Gupta, Secretary, Capacity Building Commission gave the vote of thanks. He reiterated the commitment of the Commission to take forward the vision of Mission Karmayogi.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 917, 1610, 'en', 0, '<p>The Inaugural Session of the second batch of DAKSH (Development of Aspiration, Knowledge, Succession and Harmony), a flagship leadership development programme for senior executives of Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs), was held at the SCOPE Convention Centre, New Delhi. The programme is jointly organised by the Capacity Building Commission (CBC) and the Standing Conference of Public Enterprises (SCOPE) under Mission Karmayogi.<br><br>The event was attended by senior leadership from the Government of India and the public sector, including Dr. P. K. Mishra, Principal Secretary to the Prime Minister; Shri K. Moses Chalai, Secretary, Department of Public Enterprises; Smt. Rachna Shah, Secretary, Department of Personnel and Training; Smt. S. Radha Chauhan, Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission; Shri K. P. Mahadevaswamy, Chairman, SCOPE; Shri Atul Sobti, Director General, SCOPE; and Smt. Alka Mittal, Member (Administration), Capacity Building Commission.<br><br>Welcoming participants, Shri Atul Sobti said DAKSH will help leaders reflect, prepare and transform themselves, while enabling leadership emergence, strategic development and international exposure.<br><br>Setting the context, Smt. Alka Mittal described DAKSH as a 12-month leadership programme integrating digital learning, classroom engagement, executive coaching, action learning and international exposure. She noted that 73 senior CPSE officials were trained in the first batch &amp; 72 participants from diverse sectors form the second. Highlighting Mission Karmayogi initiatives such as iGOT onboarding, Karmayogi Saptah, the Competency Model, accreditation of institutions and Amrit Gyaan Kosh, she emphasised leadership development, competency-based growth and technology-enabled learning for CPSE reforms.<br><br>Delivering the address, Dr. P. K. Mishra highlighted the evolving role of CPSEs and their foundational contribution to India’s industrial and infrastructure base. He said globalisation and reforms have shifted focus to competitiveness, efficiency and innovation, requiring greater agility while serving national priorities and competing globally. Referring to the Public Sector Enterprise Policy of 2021, he noted that despite an expanding role for private enterprises, CPSEs remain vital in strategic sectors such as energy, defence, infrastructure and finance, and in balancing markets involving public goods and national security. He stressed innovation, continuous learning and strategic thinking through initiatives like DAKSH.<br><br>Earlier, Shri K. Moses Chalai highlighted the economic contribution of CPSEs to GDP &amp; the Central Exchequer, stressing the need for future-ready leadership and describing DAKSH as timely.&nbsp;<br><br>Shri Jagdeep Gupta, Secretary, Capacity Building Commission gave the vote of thanks. He reiterated the commitment of the Commission to take forward the vision of Mission Karmayogi.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 918, 1611, 'en', 0, '<p>Chairperson, Capacity Building Commission, Ms S. Radha Chauhan, visited Sardar Patel Institute of Public Administration (SPIPA), Ahmedabad, Gujarat today. \r\n\r\nShe chaired a meeting with the Deputy Director General, SPIPA, Shri Chandresh Kotak, Joint Secretary &amp; Knowledge Manager, Ms Ruta Bhatt and others. During the meeting, various matters related to the implementation of Mission Karmayogi in the state of Gujarat were discussed.</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 919, 1612, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission’s Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Programme (Phase-II) concludes\r\n\r\nDr. R. Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission chaired the Closing Session of Phase-II of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program today. Around 10.5 lakh government servants have been trained under this interactive behavioural training program across the country. The closing session was attended virtually by around 300 participants from various Ministries and Departments. A key outcome of the program has been the creation of a nationwide cohort of 822 Lead Trainers and over 16,500 Master Trainers, equipped with facilitation skills grounded in adult-learning principles and activity-based learning methodologies.&nbsp;\r\nDr. R. Balasubramaniam lauded all participating MDOs for their enthusiastic involvement in the entire program. He emphasized that the initiative\'s core aim was to realign inner purpose with outward service, fostering empathetic, efficient, and citizen-centric service delivery, with \"Seva Bhav\" as the driving force. Dr. Balasubramaniam stressed that this is merely the beginning of a long-term transformation, urging the institutionalization of these efforts to cultivate a responsive, resilient, and future-ready administrative culture for a \"Viksit Bharat.\" \r\n\r\nShri Jagdeep Gupta, Secretary of CBC extended gratitude to the MDOs, highlighting the unprecedented scale of over 500 organizations participating and the overwhelmingly positive feedback.\r\n<br>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 923, 1617, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission’s Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Programme (Phase-II) concludes Dr. R. Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission chaired the Closing Session of Phase-II of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program today. Around 10.5 lakh government servants have been trained under this interactive behavioural training program across the country. The closing session was attended virtually by around 300 participants from various Ministries and Departments. A key outcome of the program has been the creation of a nationwide cohort of 822 Lead Trainers and over 16,500 Master Trainers, equipped with facilitation skills grounded in adult-learning principles and activity-based learning methodologies.&nbsp; Dr. R. Balasubramaniam lauded all participating MDOs for their enthusiastic involvement in the entire program. He emphasized that the initiative\'s core aim was to realign</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
('event', 0, 923, 1618, 'en', 0, '<p>Capacity Building Commission’s Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Programme (Phase-II) concludes Dr. R. Balasubramaniam, Member (HR), Capacity Building Commission chaired the Closing Session of Phase-II of the Rashtriya Karmayogi Large Scale Jan Seva Program today. Around 10.5 lakh government servants have been trained under this interactive behavioural training program across the country. The closing session was attended virtually by around 300 participants from various Ministries and Departments. A key outcome of the program has been the creation of a nationwide cohort of 822 Lead Trainers and over 16,500 Master Trainers, equipped with facilitation skills grounded in adult-learning principles and activity-based learning methodologies.&nbsp; Dr. R. Balasubramaniam lauded all participating MDOs for their enthusiastic involvement in the entire program. He emphasized that the initiative\'s core aim was to realign</p>', '', 'basic_html'),
