(378, 'en', 'node_search', ' a preworkshop discussion was held in the presence of smt chandralekha mukherjee principal advisor capacity building commission and shri sachin sinha a preworkshop discussion was held in the presence of smt chandralekha mukherjee principal advisor capacity building commission and shri sachin sinha adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1405 a preworkshop discussion was held in the presence of smt chandralekha mukherjee principal advisor capacity building commission and shri sachin sinha dg rcvp noronha academy bhopal department hods and senior officials presented their draft capacity building plans receiving key guidance for finalisation mon 8 dec 2025 1200 workshops madhya pradesh a preworkshop discussion was held in the presence of smt chandralekha mukherjee principal advisor capacity building commission and shri sachin sinha ', 0),
(379, 'en', 'node_search', ' chairperson cbc ms s radha chauhan and chief secretary government of madhya pradesh shri anurag jain address the state level capacity building plan development workshop chairperson cbc ms s radha chauhan and chief secretary government of madhya pradesh shri anurag jain address the state level capacity building plan development workshop adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1416 chairperson cbc ms s radha chauhan and chief secretary government of madhya pradesh shri anurag jain address the state level capacity building plan development workshop conducted at rcvp noronha academy of administration and management bhopal madhya pradesh the chairperson highlighted the paradigm shift towards role and demandbased training she said that these departmental capacity building plans will facilitate the training of cadres in their respective departments and aim to enhance the capacities of officials through role based demand led training courses programmes the chief secretary advised departmental heads to make modifications as required while finalising the capacity building plans dg of ati shri sachin sinha emphasised upon continuous learning unlearning and relearning shri sanjay shukla acs general administration department was also present at the workshop in the pre workshop exercises around 29 key departments and their 60 sub departments directorates boards authorities 89 in total prepared capacity building plans covering 1089 unique designations this first of its kind workshop in the nation marks another milestone towards state level capacity building bringing madhya pradesh to the forefront of capacity building initiatives under mission karmayogi event venue rcvp noronha academy of administration and management bhopal madhya pradesh mon 8 dec 2025 1200 chairperson cbc ms s radha chauhan and chief secretary government of madhya pradesh shri anurag jain address the state level capacity building plan development workshop ', 0),
(380, 'en', 'node_search', ' the preworkshop on capacity building plan development was conducted in the presence of ms rehana batool director general the preworkshop on capacity building plan development was conducted in the presence of ms rehana batool director general adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1434 the preworkshop on capacity building plan development was conducted today in the presence of ms rehana batool director general along with her team from the jammu kashmir institute of management public administration and rural development j k impard and smt chandralekha mukherjee principal advisor and her team from the capacity building commission looking forward to the collaborative efforts ahead and to translate these discussions into impactful outcomes for the region mon 8 dec 2025 1200 jammu kashmir institute of management public administration and rural development j k impard the preworkshop on capacity building plan development was conducted in the presence of ms rehana batool director general  ', 0),
(381, 'en', 'node_search', ' rashtriya karmyogi jan seva program 800000 government officials trained rashtriya karmyogi jan seva program 800000 government officials trained adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1439 rashtriya karmyogi jan seva program 800000 government officials trained the capacity building commission cbc is proud to share that the rashtriya karmyogi jan seva program has trained over 800000 government officials across the country in oneday training along with 16000 master trainers and 822 lead trainers phase ii of the program launched in may 2025 with an aim of training about 700000 government officials has been completed which is a testament to the enthusiasm and commitment of government employees nationwide this milestone marks a significant advancement in embedding the spirit of seva bhav and the ethos of a karmyogi across india s administrative landscape by strengthening purpose intent and service orientation at scale the program continues to contribute meaningfully to the larger vision of citizencentric governance cbc acknowledges the efforts of all ministries departments organisations and every participating official for their active engagement and support your dedication has transformed this initiative into a powerful movement for behavioural transformation in government together we move closer to building a more responsive empathetic and serviceoriented governance ecosystem tue 9 dec 2025 1200 lsi rashtriya karmyogi jan seva program 800000 government officials trained ', 0),
(382, 'en', 'node_search', ' jammu kashmir oneday workshop on developing capacity building plans jammu kashmir oneday workshop on developing capacity building plans adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1441 jammu kashmir oneday workshop on developing capacity building plans in collaboration with the cbc the institute of management public administration and rural development impard jammu kashmir organised a oneday workshop on the development of cbps tue 9 dec 2025 1200 workshops jammu and kashmir institute of management public administration and rural development impard jammu kashmir jammu kashmir oneday workshop on developing capacity building plans ', 0),
(383, 'en', 'node_search', ' ms s radha chauhan chairperson capacity building commission visited delhi metro rail corporation dmrc academy ms s radha chauhan chairperson capacity building commission visited delhi metro rail corporation dmrc academy adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1446 ms s radha chauhan chairperson capacity building commission visited delhi metro rail corporation dmrc academy on 10122025 during her visit she was given a brief presentation on the academy and its facilities providing her with an overview of its training capabilities and its centres of excellence following the presentation the chairperson visited the academy s stateoftheart training infrastructure which included computer based training lab model rooms digital library driving maintenance simulators etc shri ghansham bansal director general dmrc academy was also present on the occasion wed 10 dec 2025 1200 delhi delhi metro rail corporation dmrc academy ms s radha chauhan chairperson capacity building commission visited delhi metro rail corporation dmrc academy ', 0),
(384, 'en', 'node_search', ' national conference on the role of young generation women in a strong and vibrant indian national power grid national conference on the role of young generation women in a strong and vibrant indian national power grid adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1451 dr alka mittal member capacity building commission cbc delivered the address at the national conference on the role of young generation women in a strong and vibrant indian national power grid held in new delhi today she highlighted the aspect of valuedriven leadership grounded in integrity empathy and fairness and stressed upon the need for courage in decisionmaking by taking tough calls with accountability emphasizing upon a peoplecentric approach dr mittal highlighted the importance of listening and empathy in large organizations she urged leaders to broaden their strategic outlook by moving from an operational to an organizational perspective and aligning personal vision with institutional goals for emerging leaders she advised investing in continuous learning building resilience by viewing failure as feedback communicating with authenticity and developing a personal leadership brand anchored in strong values reminding everyone that leadership is not about titles it s about influence and impact during her address she also mentioned that the capacity building commission is associating itself with the dpe scope and the pse leadership to evolve a strategic hr ecosystem for aligning it with the national development goals she concluded with a call to action lead with courage compassion and conviction always walk the talk thu 11 dec 2025 1200 capacity building initiatives delhi yashobhoomi iicc new delhi national conference on the role of young generation women in a strong and vibrant indian national power grid ', 0),
(385, 'en', 'node_search', ' capacity building commission organises national workshop on future readiness of central training institutes  capacity building commission organises national workshop on future readiness of central training institutes adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1455 capacity building commission organises national workshop on future readiness of central training institutes training institutes need to reimagine revamp and redefine their roles in ever evolving training ecosystem says ms s radha chauhan chairperson cbc at the inaugural session she added that training needs to be dynamic focussing on learning unlearning and relearning the chairperson highlighted the significance of human element that needs to play its role in meeting the aim of citizencentric governance for viksit bharat within the overall technologydriven environment ms chandralekha mukherjee principal advisor cbc made a detailed presentation on the future readiness of central training institutes she shared that now five 5 ctis are rated 5star as per the nscsti 2o framework she added that focus now moves beyond ratings towards centres of excellence competencydriven training and citizencentric outcomes former chairman cbc sh adil zainulbhai while addressing virtually said that going ahead tis need to aim for becoming fivestar rated worldclass training institutes collaborate among themselves and with educational institutes think tanks and become leaders in integrating physical digital training ecosystem mr rakesh verma coo kb introduced the aienabled cbp tool highlighting its potential to support institutes in designing competencydriven training plans aligning with the dynamic needs of training institutes mdos key feature of the workshop were three parallel breakout sessions which enabled focused deliberations on critical aspects of future readiness on the topics building excellence through roles responsibilities and technologyenabled training quality strengthening the nscsti framework enabling resource pooling and enhancing courses on igot through ai tools domain course identification the sessions were moderated by the principal advisor cbc ms chandralekha mukherjee and senior faculty from ctis including ms madhavi das dg ncaf ms shanmuga priya mishra deputy director sr lbsnaa ms archana gopinath joint director raknpa sh rakesh verma coo kb ms uma s advisor cbc other team members from cbc the findings from breakout sessions were presented before the audience leading to convergence on actionable recommendations and implementation pathways dr alka mittal member admin cbc complimented all groups for their active engagement during discussions she said that the institutes should not only sustain standards but should play the role of mentors she appealed that we should ensure that all of us come together sh s p roy secretary cbc reaffirmed cbc s commitment to supporting ctis in becoming agile techenabled futureready institutions under mk mon 15 dec 2025 1200 capacity building commission organises national workshop on future readiness of central training institutes  ', 0),
(386, 'en', 'node_search', ' cbc organises bharat cpses consultative conclave on shaping india s growth story through daksh pses 2047  cbc organises bharat cpses consultative conclave on shaping india s growth story through daksh pses 2047 adarsh thu 8 jan 2026 1500 chairperson cbc emphasizes upon desiloization of governance and democratization of learning she highlighted the importance of embedding competencybased governance leadership development and performancelinked learning within cpses as part of india s broader civil services reform agenda the ethos of karmayogi should imbibe in every delivery of public service she said dr alka mittal member cbc underscores strategic role of cpses as critical institutions for nationbuilding while setting the context of the conclave dr mittal underscored the strategic role of cpses as critical institutions for nationbuilding beyond their commercial mandate she highlighted that cpses are not only engines of economic growth but also custodians of public values governance standards and longterm institutional capability the inaugural address was delivered by shri k moses chalai secretary dpe who highlighted the fact that leadership is very important and we need visionary leaders he later added that we should be open to change and adopt good changes members of the pesb shri alkesh kumar sharma and shri roop narayan sunkar also shared their key observations a strategic keynote session was delivered by dr c jayakumar executive vice president head corporate human resources larsen toubro l t ltd on hr strategies for purposedriven leadership focusing on building resilient leadership pipelines and aligning organisational values with national priorities this was followed by a presentation on daksh by shri atul sobti dg scope outlining a structured framework for leadership development succession planning and hr reforms in cpses secretary mnre shri santosh kumar sarangi dr r balasubramaniam member hr cbc ceo karmayogi bharat kb ms chhavi bhardwaj senior officials from dpe ministries cbc were also present during the inaugural session the conclave featured focused roundtable discussions on reimagining hr systems for highimpact cpse performance and translating vision into action cpse hr strategy where participants emphasised the need for institutionalised collaboration shared knowledge platforms and integrated capacitybuilding efforts to enhance efficiency innovation and public value creation beyond financial returns the program concluded with closing reflections by shri s p roy secretary cbc who said that cbc is always committed to support capacity building initiatives of cpses the vote of thanks was delivered by ms navneet kaur director cbc the cbc will also bring the training institutes psus and states on a common platform for collaboration aligned with karmayogi capacity building efforts across governance space thu 18 dec 2025 1200 delhi cbc organises bharat cpses consultative conclave on shaping india s growth story through daksh pses 2047  ', 0),
