(682, 'en', 'node_search', ' member hr capacity building commission dr r balasubramaniam visited all india institute of speech and hearing aiish mysore member hr capacity building commission dr r balasubramaniam visited all india institute of speech and hearing aiish mysore admin tue 13 jan 2026 941 member hr capacity building commission dr r balasubramaniam visited all india institute of speech and hearing aiish mysore and address the staff there on 4th december 2025 he stressed on imbibing the spirit of continuous learning bringing about the behavioural change becoming futureready and to encourage derive benefit by crosspollination of ideas and collaboration his address also covered concepts of vikas garv kartavya and ekta principles of swadhyaya sahkaryata rajyakarma and swadharma besides adoption of indian knowledge systems and quotes from indic literature a brief presentation about the institute was made by the director aiish covering governance aspects and the institute s work across four verticalsmanpower development clinical services research and public education in the area of communication speech and hearing this was followed by visits to the departments of special education clinical services centre for public education in communication disorders cpecd and department of prevention of communication disorders the visit concluded with the member hr cbc addressing the officers of the institute followed by an interactive session during the visit the aiishians of the year 2025 were presented awards by member hr cbc aiish has achieved 984 staff coverage under the rashtriya karmayogi jan sewa rkjs program by cbc and has developed 18 domainspecific courses for the kb in the domain of health thu 4 dec 2025 1200 karnataka all india institute of speech and hearing aiish mysore member hr capacity building commission dr r balasubramaniam visited all india institute of speech and hearing aiish mysore  ', 0),
(683, 'en', 'node_search', ' signing of memorandum of understanding and orientation workshop on mission karmyogi signing of memorandum of understanding and orientation workshop on mission karmyogi admin tue 13 jan 2026 949 the capacity building commission cbc karmyogi bharat and the government of mizoram signed a memorandum of understanding in aizawl to strengthen capacity building initiatives in the state mr khilli ram meena chief secretary mizoram acknowledged the need for systematic capacity building to meet the requirements of an evolving workforce he welcomed the support of cbc and karmyogi bharat in enabling the state to ensure that officials are equipped with the right competencies and skills for effective governance he emphasised on lifelong learning of officers in mizoram dr r balasubramaniam member hr cbc emphasized the vital role of administrative training institutes in shaping a futureready civil service he highlighted the importance of competencybased capacity building integration of ehrms with the igot platform and preparing officers today to deliver on the vision of viksit bharat 2047 shri s p roy secretary cbc highlighted the role of capacity building units in enabling the capacity building in the state he explained the structural framework of overall coordination between the state and capacity building commission he also highlighted the importance of capacity building plan and the workshop to be planned for its development this partnership marks a significant step in advancing missionkarmyogi and building an agile skilled and citizencentric workforce wed 3 dec 2025 1200 mizoram signing of memorandum of understanding and orientation workshop on mission karmyogi  ', 0),
