(746, 'en', 'node_search', ' the cbc held a meeting with the chandigarh administration for implementation of missionkarmayogi in the cbc held a meeting with the chandigarh administration for implementation of missionkarmayogi in admin tue 13 jan 2026 1449 the capacity building commission cbc held a meeting with the chandigarh administration for implementation of missionkarmayogi in the union territory of chandigarh the meeting was presided over by shri rajeev verma ias chief secretary union territory of chandigarh and attended by all heads of department and other senior officials of the union territory the cbc team led by dr alka mittal member administration and smt v lalithalakshmi secretary cbc and ceo karmayogi bharat provided an insightful overview of mission karmayogi the national program for civil services capacity building the team highlighted the importance of capacitybuilding through capacity building plans for all ut chandigarh departments and the transition to rolebased competencydriven learning while also providing a walkthrough of the igot platform in enhancing governance capabilities to drive the successful implementation of mission karmayogi in chandigarh the chief secretary directed the immediate formation of capacity building unit cbu ensuring 100 onboarding of officials onto the igot platform and completion of at least four courses by all officials within a month a dedicated workshop will also be conducted by the igotkarmayogi bharat team to guide nodal officers in effectively navigating the platform tue 25 mar 2025 1200 chandigarh the cbc held a meeting with the chandigarh administration for implementation of missionkarmayogi in ', 0),
(747, 'en', 'node_search', ' dr r balasubramaniam member hr cbc visited the matsushita institute of government and management japan dr r balasubramaniam member hr cbc visited the matsushita institute of government and management japan admin tue 13 jan 2026 1452 dr r balasubramaniam member hr capacity building commission visited the matsushita institute of government and management japan during his visit he interacted with the institute s senior leadership and associates currently undergoing training to serve in public life the discussions focused on understanding how the institute nurtures young professionals to take on leadership roles in governance and public service founded in 1979 by konosuke matsushita the institute was built on the belief that solving a nation s problems requires nurturing ethical visionary leadersnot just bureaucrats its model combines intensive field experience longterm mentoring and a strong moral foundation over 50 of its alumni have gone on to hold elected office in japan including prime ministers ministers and governors a rare measurable example of leadership development directly shaping national governance this aligns closely with cbc s commitment to transforming india s civil services into a citizencentric futureready workforcegrounded in values and driven by purpose sat 22 mar 2025 1200 matsushita institute of government and management japan dr r balasubramaniam member hr cbc visited the matsushita institute of government and management japan ', 0),
(748, 'en', 'node_search', ' workshop for urban local bodies ulbs at the school of planning architecture vijayawada workshop for urban local bodies ulbs at the school of planning architecture vijayawada admin tue 13 jan 2026 1453 under missionkarmayogi the capacity building commission cbc in collaboration with the department of municipal administration and urban development ma ud government of andhra pradesh and with the support of the commissioner and director of municipal administration cdma organized a oneday capacitybuilding workshop for urban local bodies ulbs at the school of planning architecture vijayawada the workshop brought together 175 officials from 123 ulbs and key urban departments including mepma public health and town planning participants were introduced to the igotkarmayogi platform to foster a culture of continuous learning for citizencentric governance and professional development the discussions helped identify key training needs and priority areas for skilling ulb officials to drive better outcomes on the ground the workshop was graced by the presence of shri sureshkumar s nair ias principal secretary ma ud andhra pradesh dr alka mittal member admin capacity building commission smt v lalithalakshmi ias secretary cbc and ceo karamayogi bharat and dr p sampath kumar ias commissioner director of municipal administration this initiative is a step toward building a resilient futureready urban workforce aligned with the vision of swarnaandhra2047 tue 17 jun 2025 1200 andhra pradesh school of planning and architecture vijayawada andhra pradesh workshop for urban local bodies ulbs at the school of planning architecture vijayawada  ', 0),
(749, 'en', 'node_search', ' the cbc carried out an onsite assessment at the animal training school indotibetan border police the cbc carried out an onsite assessment at the animal training school indotibetan border police admin tue 13 jan 2026 1455 the capacity building commission carried out an onsite assessment at the animal training school indotibetan border police in lohitpur arunachal pradesh on 21st and 22nd march 2025 we are delighted to announce that the institute has successfully achieved accreditation under the nscsti national standards for civil service training institutions capacity building commission the assessment was efficiently facilitated by col dr k jagannathan and s p roy joint secretary capacity building commission along with jagan sridhar and susan thomas a heartfelt thanks to the nodal officer mr pamei and his team for his support in ensuring a smooth process fri 21 mar 2025 1200 animal training school lohitpur arunachal pradesh the cbc carried out an onsite assessment at the animal training school indotibetan border police ', 0),
(750, 'en', 'node_search', ' rise with pride lead evolve transform a highimpact leadership development program set against the tranquil backdrop of kerala rise with pride lead evolve transform a highimpact leadership development program set against the tranquil backdrop of kerala admin tue 13 jan 2026 1456 day 1 highlights rise with pride lead evolve transform 🌟 📍 alleppey kerala 📅 11th june 2025 we are proud to kick off rise with pride lead evolve transform a highimpact leadership development program set against the tranquil backdrop of kerala with 50 senior professionals from both the public sector and private sector joining us the energy experience and diversity in the room set the stage for powerful exchanges and meaningful learning day 1 key moments 🔹 welcome address by dr alka mittal member capacity building commission of india former cmd director hr ongc and our esteemed program advisor she highlighted the critical role of leadership evolution in building futureready organizations 🔹 keynote address by ms usha singh director hr moil her address encouraged leaders to lead with authenticity empathy and strength 🔹 inaugural address by dr dr ranjit rath chairman managing director oil india limited his words inspired participants to embrace transformation and lead with vision 🪔 ceremonial lighting of the lamp dr alka mittal ms usha singh and dr dr ranjit rath rath came together to light the ceremonial lamp an auspicious beginning to four days of growth dialogue and discovery this is only the beginning of an enriching journey stay tuned for more updates as we continue to lead evolve and transform together wed 11 jun 2025 1200 uttar pradesh jaipuria institute of management lucknow rise with pride lead evolve transform a highimpact leadership development program set against the tranquil backdrop of kerala  ', 0),
(752, 'en', 'node_search', ' rashtriya karmyogi large scale jan seva program from learning to action rashtriya karmyogi large scale jan seva program from learning to action admin tue 13 jan 2026 1458 rashtriya karmyogi large scale jan seva program from learning to action the rashtriya karmyogi program has trained another additional batch of officials from multiple ministries and departments over the past 3 days continuing its mission of embedding sewabhaav in governance officials stepped away from their desks to rethink their rolenot just as administrators but as facilitators of citizencentric service understanding how every actionbig or smallimpacts citizens this program is not just training but a shift in perspective rooted in seva bhaav and svadharma from the way policies are communicated to how challenges are approached this program has encouraged participants to see governance through the lens of impact rather than process now as certified master trainers they take on the responsibility of further training officials within their respective ministries departments and organizationsensuring that serviceoriented governance is not just discussed in a training room but practiced at every level and this is just one step in a larger journey with the next phase set to train 700000 government officials across bharat the movement is not far the shift from processdriven to purposedriven governance is taking shape thu 20 mar 2025 1200 sushma swaraj institute of foreign service new delhi rashtriya karmyogi large scale jan seva program from learning to action ', 0),
(753, 'en', 'node_search', ' government of the national capital territory nct of delhi signed a memorandum of understanding mou with the cbc and karmyogi bharat government of the national capital territory nct of delhi signed a memorandum of understanding mou with the cbc and karmyogi bharat admin tue 13 jan 2026 1459 a landmark moment for governance in the capital government of nct of delhi signs mou with capacity building commission and karmyogi bharat for implementation of missionkarmyogi in a major step towards strengthening governance and public service delivery the government of the national capital territory nct of delhi today signed a memorandum of understanding mou with the capacity building commission cbc and karmyogi bharat for the implementation of mission karmyogi the mou was signed in the presence of the hon ble chief minister of delhi smt rekha gupta the chief secretary of delhi shri dharmendra member administration capacity building commission dr alka mittal and other senior officials from cbc karmyogi bharat and delhi government under the visionary leadership of the hon ble chief minister delhi is now poised to scale this effort significantly by onboarding all officials onto the igot portal marking one of the largest statelevel initiatives under mission karmyogi capacity building commission and karmyogi bharat commended the leadership of the delhi government and assured full support in enabling continuous learning and strengthening capacities of all the officials this includes assistance in formulating capacity building plans cbps for departments and strengthening the capacities of urban local body ulb officials to deliver citizencentric services more effectively and large scale intervention for delhi government officials for inculcating sewa bhav with this milestone mission karmyogi continues to expand its footprint across states and union territories creating a uniform and progressive ecosystem for capacity building thu 29 may 2025 1200 government of the national capital territory nct delhi government of the national capital territory nct of delhi signed a memorandum of understanding mou with the cbc and karmyogi bharat  ', 0),
(754, 'en', 'node_search', ' abhijnanaworkshop on decolonizing cstis brings together thought leaders policymakers academics abhijnanaworkshop on decolonizing cstis brings together thought leaders policymakers academics admin tue 13 jan 2026 1500 reimagining civil service training decolonizing mindsets institutions for decades india s cstis have operated within frameworks inherited from colonial ruleshaping administrative structures policymaking approaches institutional cultures that often remain disconnected from realities of bharat s civilizational ethos this calls for a necessary shift today iit delhi abhijnanaworkshop on decolonizing cstis brings together thought leaders policymakers academics to initiate this transformation organized by capacity building commission training division dopt iks program iit delhi indica this workshop is designed to empower civil servants cstis with intellectual tools to draw from iksnot as an abstract idea but as a practical approach to governance administration nomesh bolia prof iit delhi remarked that civil services are deeply respected in india not just for their authority but for their role in nationbuilding urging participants to explore how key concepts can be materialized into actionable steps for decolonization prof ke seetha ram senior consulting specialist adb institute highlighted that institutional transformation requires rethinking foundational frameworks that iks offers a way to rebuild civil service training programs in alignment with india s unique governance needs s p roy jt secretary cbc highlighted importance of building a mindset around indian knowledge system and its role in governance capacity building dr r balasubramaniam member hr cbc led key discussions today his insights on how colonial constructs continue to shape public service need to realign governance with india s cultural knowledge traditions will be instrumental in reshaping civil service training drawing from panch pran he emphasized the need for capturing institutionalizing success stories to ensure governance becomes a structured repeatable process that strengthens public institutions shri amit khare ias advisor to the hon ble pm the chief guest reinforced that viksit bharat can only emerge when every state village citizen progresses togetherhe emphasized a saturation approach where every individual contributes to the nation s growth storyhe also commended cbc s role in bringing iks closer to civil servants ensuring governance remains deeply connected to india s knowledge traditionshe also made a poignant remark emphasizing the importance of sustaining their commitment to serving the nation just as it is when they first embark on their journey in civil service the workshop will explore 🔸 why we must decolonize our institutions 🔸 what elements of governance training need transformation 🔸 how to embed iks into csti curricula functional practices institutional culture the workshop progresses to work towards redefining how civil servants are trainedso that they don t just manage a system but actively build one that is rooted in india s knowledge traditions thu 6 mar 2025 1200 iit delhi abhijnanaworkshop on decolonizing cstis brings together thought leaders policymakers academics ', 0),
(755, 'en', 'node_search', ' capacity building commission conducted an onsite assessment of the national cpwd academy ghaziabad delhi ncr  capacity building commission conducted an onsite assessment of the national cpwd academy ghaziabad delhi ncr admin tue 13 jan 2026 1500 the capacity building commission conducted an onsite assessment of the national cpwd academy ghaziabad delhi ncr on 28th and 29th may 2025 we are pleased to share that the institute has successfully attained accreditation under the national standards for civil service training institutes nscsti the assessment process was effectively facilitated by dr alka mittal member administration cbc shri prasanta kumar mahapatra assessor along with ritika aggarwal nabet and susan thomas cbc our sincere appreciation goes to shri ujjwal mitra adg t r and his dedicated team for their exemplary support in ensuring a seamless and wellcoordinated assessment process wed 28 may 2025 1200 national cpwd academy ghaziabad capacity building commission conducted an onsite assessment of the national cpwd academy ghaziabad delhi ncr  ', 0),
(756, 'en', 'node_search', ' workshop on karmaconnect increasing learner engagement under mission karmayogi workshop on karmaconnect increasing learner engagement under mission karmayogi admin tue 13 jan 2026 1502 while igot has come a long way with 8 million users and 1900 coursesthere s still a massive opportunity ahead today learners engage for just 3 hours a year imagine if we could shift that to 25 hours per user today not as an obligation but as a habit a mindset a way of life and make doing that cool that s exactly why cbc and igot brought together some of india s sharpest minds in marketing branding and digital engagement at karmaconnect increasing learner engagement workshop they didn t just discuss ideas they challenged the way we think about learning leaders and changemakers like suhel seth founder managing partner counselage india ajay gahlaut independent creative former cco dentsu creative service sahibjeet singh sawhney marketing head zomato pankaj bansal पंकज बंसल board member kb cofounder peoplestrong gayatri yadav group cmo evp strategic initiatives reliance industries hari krishnan managing director publicis content groupemarcomm biju dominic chief evangelist fractal analytics prashasti rastogi senior director education and government coursera sumit harjani managing director india harvard business publishing swati agarwal partner deloitte abhishek singh additional secretary ministry of electronics and it and ceo india ai mission didn t hold back they broke down engagement into its raw elements behavior motivation habitbuilding 💡 why do people bingewatch content but struggle with courses 💡 what makes a message stick 💡 how do we make learning irresistible discussions went beyond theory behavioral nudges branding that inspires action and celebrating learners like influencersall of this was put on the table 15 pages of brilliant ideas that we now have the responsibility to bring to life thank you to all our participants for helping us drive igot and missionkarmayogi to new heights thu 6 mar 2025 1200 vigyan bhawan new delhi workshop on karmaconnect increasing learner engagement under mission karmayogi ', 0),
(757, 'en', 'node_search', ' capacity building commission cbc karmayogi bharat and the government of arunachal pradesh signed a tripartite mou capacity building commission cbc karmayogi bharat and the government of arunachal pradesh signed a tripartite mou admin tue 13 jan 2026 1503 building towards a futureready civil service the capacity building commission is cultivating deep partnerships with states fostering skilled and responsive governance aligned with india s evolving needs today marks a significant milestone as the capacity building commission cbc karmayogi bharat and the government of arunachal pradesh signed a tripartite mou this agreement signifies a pivotal step in enhancing governance capabilities within the state the signing ceremony was followed by an insightful orientation session led by dr r balasubramaniam member hr at cbc focusing on missionkarmayogi and the karmayogi competency model kcm ms soumi banerjee gm strategic alliance and partnership from karmayogi bharat provided an overview of the functionalities and usage of the igot platform shri manish kumar gupta chief secretary of arunachal pradesh emphasized the critical importance of capacitybuilding for government officials and highlighted the need for a transformative mindset among civil servants he also commended mission karmayogi for its structured approach to competency development shri s p roy joint secretary cbc outlined specific areas for collaboration between the state and cbc while shri yashpal garg commissioner of the department of personnel underscored the necessity of tailored training programs based on identified needs the orientation session saw active participation from secretaries special secretaries commissioners additional secretaries joint secretaries directors and heads of departments from across the government of arunachal pradesh tue 27 may 2025 1200 itanagar arunachal pradesh capacity building commission cbc karmayogi bharat and the government of arunachal pradesh signed